{"_id":"04Z1e9RUVWNPaXof","name":"High Goblin Maiden","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:high-goblin-maiden","level":13,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Drakish","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"12/-","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"18 (25)","source":"BM","description":"Created as the leader of High Goblins , she is almost always followed by another species of High Goblin, especially High Goblin Fanatics .\n\nAlthough she is stunningly beautiful, she is otherwise no different from other High Goblins with her pale skin, huge red eyes, and the Anti- Magic Enchantment that covers her entire body. Although she is not a powerful fighter, she can make High Goblins go crazy with her body and can emit an aroma that heals wounds. This strengthens the High Goblins around her and protects her, thus ensuring her own safety. They also have the ability to regenerate her own strength by being bathed in the blood of those who have been offered to her.\n\nThey are arrogant, selfish, brutal, and cunning. However, it is said that she instinctively feels strong affection for the stronger Drakes and is willing to obey their commands. For this purpose, she will expend the lives of any number of High Goblins under her command.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Frenzy Aroma","description":"It releases a frenzied scent from its entire body that disperses over a wide area, making High Goblins go into a frenzy. This ability costs 5 HP for this monster.\nFor 10 seconds (1 round), within \"Range: Caster\" \"Target: All Areas (20m Radius)/All\" all High Goblins (of any type) receive a +1 bonus on Accuracy checks and +4 to damage. At the same time, it gives a -4 penalty to Evasion checks.\nThis effect is of the psychic type and is not cumulative."},{"title":"► Healing Aroma","description":"The entire body releases a scent that activates High Goblin's resilience and disperses it over a wide area. When using this ability, the High Goblin Maiden consumes its own HP in any range from 1 to 25 points (chosen by this monster). At the same time, all High Goblins (all species except High Goblin Maiden) within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (20m Radius) / All\" will regain the same number of points of HP."},{"title":"⏩ Blood Offering/Can't","description":"High Goblin Maiden instantly kills within \"Range: Touch\" one High Goblin (except another High Goblin Maiden). At the same time, it's own HP is restored to the same number of points as the High Goblin's HP had immediately before dying from this effect.\nThis effect can only be used once per round and before the Maiden takes a Major Action."},{"title":"◯ Advanced Anti-Magic Enchantment","description":"When this monster performs a Willpower check against magic, if Willpower succeeds, the result is treated as Negated regardless of the type of magic. Furthermore, even if the Willpower check fails, the effect of the magic is still Negated and costs 10 MP to the High Goblin. This effect does not occur if no MP is consumed.\nThis ability does apply to effects other than spells, even if they require a Resistance Check."},{"title":"◯ Psychic Resistance","description":"High Goblin Maidens are immune to Psychic (Weak) effects.\nThey also gains a +4 bonus when they makes a Willpower roll against any Psychic-type spell or unique skill.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nBeautiful Necklace (300G/Gold White A) |\n5 - 7 |\nLuxury Ornaments (500G/Gold White A) x 1d |\n8 - 11 |\nGlittering Necklace (2,000G/Gold White S) |\n12+ |\nHeraldic Ring (3,000G/Gold White S) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"High Goblin Maiden","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"0917NCeHXe3XNozR","name":"Merman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:merman","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":2,"languages":"Merman, Elven","habitat":"Ocean","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"5 (Leap)/20(Swimming)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 336","description":"Also called mermaids, these Barbarous have the lower half of a fish. Since they live in the sea, they have had little contact with other Barbarous and Humanoids, so they have remained neutral and were not eradicated in the Magitech Civilization era.\n\nAs a race, Mermen tend to avoid fighting except in self-defense and are often neutral towards most other races. However, they have a hostile relationship with some marine Barbarous, which could theoretically be leveraged into an alliance with Elves against the other aquatic races.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Underwater Specialization","description":"Can move in water without penalties and restrictions. Conversely, all action checks are subject to a -2 penalty on the ground."},{"title":"🗨 △ Cover I","description":"Can use the [ Cover I ] Combat Feat.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nRusty Spear (50G/Black White B) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7+ |\nBeautiful Shell (180G/Gold White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Merman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"0IrGiqsC0Yh31Bfv","name":"Merient Medusa","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:merient-medusa","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla , p. 123","description":"This is a Medusa whose snake-like head appears like tree branches and leaves. While its name comes from having plant-like structures on its head, it has no racial connection to Meria whatsoever. Rather, it is believed to be the result of the Medusa developing forest mimicry over hundreds of years. It makes its atelier in quiet forest locations, where it enjoys decorating trees with beautiful art pieces resembling Humanoids, Barbarous, and Daemons. The multiple humanoid-shaped trees also serve to conceal the Merient Medusa's location.\n\nHowever, they hold a particular aversion to the Meria, perhaps because they are natural enemies, even in terms of aesthetic sensibilities. Similarly, most Meria regards the Merient Medusa as a malevolent race.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"►Simultaneous Attack","description":"Attacks all enemies within their skirmish area using branch-snake hair."},{"title":"◯Severed Branches","description":"If they receive 6 or more points of damage at once from an edged weapon or slashing-type attack, they lose the [►Simultaneous Attack] ability for the next 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"◯Arboreal Branch-Hair / 6 (13) / Willpower / Negates","description":"When the branch-snake hair attack hits, it inflicts an arboreal curse on the target. This effect is treated as Petrifaction (Dexterity or Agility /-6), but instead of turning to stone, the target transforms into a tree that closely resembles its original form.\nImmediately after transformation, the tree is vibrant with fresh, green leaves, but it gradually withers, becoming completely dead wood after 2 days.\nThis effect is Curse-type, and curse-removal effects are effective both during the transformation process and after it is complete. However, effects that remove petrification, such as [ Cure Stone ] magic, are ineffective.\nIf the curse is removed within 2 days of the transformation, the character survives intact. However, if 2 days pass and the tree withers, the target is considered dead even after curse removal, requiring [ Resurrection ] or similar magic. For calculating time since death, the time of complete withering is considered the time of death."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"2 - 4","loot":"|"},{"roll":"5 - 6","loot":"|"},{"roll":"7+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Merient Medusa","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"0kvmrWj9jJLqYRz3","name":"Areigo Daved","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:areigo-daved","level":12,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Drakish","habitat":"Plains, Ruins","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"20/-","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"BM","description":"An Areigo Tactician . Areigo rarely command from the vanguard of the army, so it is considered to be the de facto highest rank amongst them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ Stratagem &amp; Maneuvers / All Areas (50m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Surging Offense IV: Blaze ] (+3 Physical Damage).\nEvery third turn uses [ Maneuver: Unexpected Blow II ] (Accuracy +4, Damage +4). If there are no characters eligible to be effected by a Stratagem, these abilities will not be used."},{"title":"► Life in Death / 15 (22) / Fortitude / Half","description":"At \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / 20, deals 2d+12 Bludgeoning magic damage. This ability can be used only once, and Areigo Daved HP is reduced to 1 HP after it is used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nNoble Barbarous' Banner (5500G Red Green S) |\n2 - 6 |\nNone |\n7 - 10 |\nExplosive Reactant Crystal Debris (600G / Red Black A) |\n11+ |\nFragment of Explosive Reactant Crystal (1600G / Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Areigo Daved","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"2trOZNeij15YYr6k","name":"Bolg","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bolg","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":7,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 401","description":"Bolgs are Barbarous Youma which are larger, stronger, and hairier than Humans.\n\nThey have bluish skin, and most of their body hair is white. They are characterized by their large fangs and ferocious nature.\n\nThey prefer swords, spears, long-handled weapons, etc. Their intellect is low, they love a fight, and they will fight to the death because they believe they can turn the tables no matter how unfavorable the odds are.\n\nThey are also good at training animals and mounts and can force a mount or other inferior Barbarous to serve them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +4 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nWeapon (30G/Black White B) |\n7+ |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bolg","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3ASuDUap4GSs3BF5","name":"Drake Count (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:drake-count-human-form","level":17,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":18,"weakness":25,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":23,"movementSpeed":"30/60(Flying)","fortitude":"23 (30)","willpower":"23 (30)","source":"CR III p. 341","description":"One of the highest-ranking Barbarous, Drake Counts have a regal air about themselves that lesser Drakes do not. While they may be the same as other Drakes physically, a Drake Count's appearance and mannerisms have that noble look about them, unconsciously showing off their status to other Barbarous. At the same time, Drake Counts are masterful combatants and tacticians, able to easily control thousands of Barbarous beneath them.\n\nA massive beast, the dragon form of a Drake Count, is much larger than those of the Drake Barons underneath them. With glistening translucent green scales, its glory is only surpassed by its frightening combat unique skill.\n\nFor the Dragon form of this monster, see Drake Count (Dragon Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 15 Level/Magic Power 21 (28)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"A Drake Count (Human Form) can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Multi-Action ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"A Drake Count (Human Form) can use the [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Recovery (9 pts.) ], [ Giant Arms ], and [ Sphinx Knowledge ] Techniques."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Drake Count receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +21 damage","description":"A Drake Count may deal an additional +21 damage to their next melee attack. If they do, at risk, they receive a -2 penalty to Fortitude and Willpower checks until their next turn."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Dragonification","description":"The Drake Count transforms into a dragon form, healing all HP and MP. Any lingering magical effects are removed as well. For more information, see the Drake Count (Dragon Form) stats. In the turn in which [ ⏩ △ Instant Dragonification] is performed, only the Body section of Dragon Form is treated as having completed the Major Action, and Wing sections can make them on this turn.\n[ ⏩ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ⏩ △ Instant Dragonification]\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHeraldic Ring (3,000G/Gold White S) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nMajestic Draconian Horn (4,200G/Red S) |\n13+ |\nNoble Draconian Horn (12,600G/Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Drake Count (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3N9uQTOjzEuvJULX","name":"Succubus Knight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:succubus-knight","level":16,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Various","reputation":22,"weakness":26,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic damage","initiative":23,"movementSpeed":"23/46 (Flying)","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"20 (27)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 103","description":"Among Succubi , Succubus Knights are especially good at fighting.\n\nThey have the ability to refine weapons, use scythes and swords, and wear tight silhouette armor. Their beautiful appearance mesmerizes and awe- inspires the viewer at the same time.\n\nThey love to attract the strong heroes and take particular pleasure in seducing them with their bewitching beauty, as well as in overpowering them with their fighting prowess, bringing them to their knees, and then sucking their energy out of them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Succubus receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Magic (2 systems) 15 Level/Magic Power 20 (27)","description":"Succubus has mastered any two of Spiritualism Magic , Divine Magic , and Summoning Arts at the 15th level."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +20 damage","description":"May deal an additional +20 damage to their next melee attack. At risk, they take a -2 penalty to their Fortitude and Willpower checks."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +12 points."},{"title":"► Indecent Dreams/20 (27)/Willpower/Neg","description":"Within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (20m radius)/All\" are put to sleep, and show a lewd dream and put to sleep. The Succubus must choose whether to target HP or MP for each use of [ ► Indecent Dreams] and will regain HP or MP equal to the damage dealt.\nThis effect is both Psychic + Curse type. However, sleep brought by this effect is treated as Psychic (Weak) type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSuccubus Lipstick (6,700G/Red S) |\n2 - 8 |\nBeautiful Tail (3,000G/Red S) |\n9 - 12 |\nCaptivating Tail (7,000G/Red S) |\n13+ |\nBewitching Tail (19,000G/Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Succubus Knight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"3OdkxY83pcN0N4ff","name":"Cryodicobraz","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cryodicobraz","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Cold Regions","reputation":13,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 119","description":"This is a leader of the Cryoblaz , appearing in large raids. They are not the type to lead from the rear but prefer to take the lead in destroying the enemy.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"It can make two Weapon attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"⏩Freezing Stance II","description":"This effect lasts for 10 seconds (1 round), does not accumulate, and consumes 5 MP when used.\nDamage caused by weapon attack becomes Water/Ice type and increases by +2. If a Cryodicobraz is hit by a melee attack, the attacker will be dealt an additional 2 Water/Ice fixed damage regardless of the success or failure of the melee attack.\nThis effect ends immediately after the Cryodicobraz receives 1 or more points of Fire-type applied damage without waiting 10 seconds (1 round). If it is caused by a melee attack, the effect disappears first, and the attacker will not be dealt fixed damage."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"5 - 9","loot":"|"},{"roll":"10+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cryodicobraz","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"4ViLoQrI5BO8v8Ec","name":"Immature Vampire","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:immature-vampire","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Nosferatu, Regional Dialect, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Silver Weapon Damage +3","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"16/32 (Flight)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"GR, Battle Mastery p. 111","description":"A Nosferatu vampire who has received the 'Blood Kiss' but is not yet at full strength (see CR II, p. 353, or ML, p. 97).\n\nThey are unable to use the gaze power that is so synonymous with vampires, and the spawns they produce are weak. Even so, they are more powerful than the average Barbarous commander and are an object of fear and awe.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 5 points","description":"At the end of each round, an Immature Vampire recovers 5 HP. This does not affect the Immature Vampire at 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Vampire Body","description":"As long as an Immature Vampire is under sunlight, it takes 5 magic damage at the end of its turn and receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks. This damage cannot be reduced in any way. Additionally, the Immature Vampire cannot use their [ ◯ Regeneration] or [ ◯ Normal Weapon Immunity] abilities."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"An Immature Vampire receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Divine Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 5 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Magical Aptitude","description":"The Immature Vampire has mastered the combat feats [ Metamagic/Targets ] and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"► Vampire Bite / 10 (17) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The Immature Vampire bites the target, dealing 2d+7 physical damage. The Immature Vampire heals HP equal to the applied damage dealt.\nIf the target is reduced to 0 HP or lower from this attack, they receive a -10 penalty to their next Death Check. If the character fails this Death Check, they receive an extra 5 soulscars and rise as a Blood Sucker.\nImmature Vampires lose 4 HP and MP per day (cumulative) that they do not drain blood via [ ► Vampire Bite] and also cannot use their [ ◯ Regeneration] unique skill. These penalties immediately disappear once the Immature Vampire successfully drains blood via [ ► Vampire Bite].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCorrupted Ash (300G/Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 11 |\nGray Cloak (300G / White A) |\n12+ |\nVampire Cloak (1,000G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Immature Vampire","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"4gB20QkmVz1tKiRu","name":"Areigo Akid","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:areigo-akid","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Drakish","habitat":"Plains, Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"BM","description":"An Areigo who holds the rank of leader. They are sometimes charged with giving orders and maintaining discipline with Barbarous legions, but it is rare that they are able to fully fulfill this role.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ Stratagem &amp; Maneuvers/All Areas (30m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Surging Offense II: Whirlwind ] (Accuracy +1).\nEvery third turn uses [ Maneuver: Unexpected Blow I ] (Accuracy +2, Damage +2). If there are no characters eligible to be effected by a Stratagem, these abilities will not be used."},{"title":"► Self-Destruction/10 (17)/Fortitude/Half","description":"\"Range: Caster\", \"Target: 1 area (6m Radius)/20\" deals 2d+8 Bludgeoning magic damage, and then the Areigo's HP becomes 0 and it dies.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBarbarous Flag (2000G / Red Green S) |\n2 - 9 |\nExplosive Reactant Crystal Debris (600G / Red Black A) |\n10+ |\nFragment of Explosive Reactant Crystal (1600G / Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Areigo Akid","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"540ZpoFlrc3vkE6g","name":"Arakcruder Hunter","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:arakcruder-hunter","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Avian, Barbaric","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":14,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"10/35(Flying)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR III p. 330","description":"Among the Arakcruder (see p. 77), these are the ones most skilled with spears, who lead their tribes in hunting and eliminating foreign enemies.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"This monster receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Spear Pursuit","description":"This monster's spear can be used as a melee attack against an opponent who has been attacked with a beak.\nAccuracy check and damage are the same as those of the beak. This effect is effective only when the monster is Flying."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"This ability can only be used with [ ◯ Spear Pursuit]. It can attack up to 3 characters within reach with melee attacks, but the damage will be reduced by -3. If more than one is hit, the damage is determined individually."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Bear Muscle ], [ Gazelle Feet ], and [ Beetleskin ] Techniques.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGems (150G/Gold A) |\n2 - 7 |\nBeautiful Feathers (30G/Gold Red B) |\n8+ |\nSeven-colored Feather (200G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Arakcruder Hunter","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5MNTImqPl73wfOyw","name":"Saber Hoodling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:saber-hoodling","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":1,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Various","reputation":7,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"11","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR I p. 398","description":"A Saber-equipped Hoodling excels at hunting in groups, using intimidation to drive the enemy toward its companions. When they appear with higher-level Youma such as Bolgs and Hugls , their attacks become even more threatening.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨 Decoy Attack I","description":"The Saber Hoodling gains -2 to Accuracy checks, but the damage is increased by +2 on hit.\nIf the declared attack is evaded, the enemy receives a -1 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative up to -4 but is lost if the target fails an Evasion check even once.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCrude Weapon (10G/Black White B) |\n2 - 6 |\nNone |\n7 - 11 |\nDirty Hood (20G/White B) |\n12+ |\nWorn Hood (80G/White B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Saber Hoodling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5npb5rr1R7YFIlw9","name":"Tusk Hammer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tusk-hammer","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Mountains, Caves","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Slashing damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Dorden , p. 119","description":"This is a small Barbarous about 1 meter tall. It has the appearance of a boar with many tusks from the neck up, and its upper body resembles a muscular Humanoid, while its lower body is hairy with hooves for feet.\n\nThey have a strong sense of kinship, and claim the Underfang Tunnel in the Dorden Region and the surrounding mountainous areas as their territory.\n\nThey prefer to use blunt weapons like maces and clubs and are adept at combining these with attacks using its enlarged bite. They are skilled at hunting animals, and their bases and settlements often gather a lot of animal meat. To preserve and process this meat, Kobold chefs often accompany them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩Fang Thrust / 5 (12) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Between attacks, a Tusk Hammer can also attack with their facial fangs, dealing 1d-1 (minimum of 0) points of fixed damage.\nIf it uses this ability on a target that has been hit with a Melee Attack during this turn, it gains a +1 bonus to the success value of this ability.\nIf it deals 1 or more points of fixed damage with this ability, the Tusk Hammer also receives 1 point of fixed damage."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If HP falls to 0 or less due to magic damage, the \"Splendid Fang\" loot will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSplendid Fang (400G/Red A) |\n2 - 10 |\nWeapon (30G/Black White B) |\n11+ |\nKeen Weapon (150G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tusk Hammer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"5pCTQ9pIXcl7N0pO","name":"Manogaryu","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:manogaryu","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Grasslands","reputation":8,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"14/-","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"BM","description":"A small but strong Barbarous, it has light green skin and stands about 1m 50cm tall as an adult.\n\nThey wield a whip in each hand and are often tasked with commanding and herding lesser beasts, livestock, and war animals. The sight of their dance-like motions in a fight is impressive and sometimes even fascinates their opponents.\n\nThey take pleasure in subjugating Humanoids, especially Lykants , and sometimes go out of their way to target them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Double Attack","description":"A Manogaryu can make two Whip attacks against the same target."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"◯ Subjugation","description":"Adds +1 bonus to Accuracy/Evasion versus Animals and Mythical Beasts."},{"title":"🗨 Whip Feint","description":"Deliberately leaves an opening in its attack to bait the opponent into evading. This has the same effect as [ Decoy Attack I ].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nDance Costume (100G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nLong, Flexible Whip (140G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Manogaryu","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"64BkzaqDwXP5N2np","name":"Alkaloid Arrow","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:alkaloid-arrow","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Youma, Drakish","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Wilderness","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"12/-","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"DA","description":"This archer handles arrows coated with a special narcotic poison. They are characterized by their burnished faces, sharp horns and fangs, and reddish body hair.\n\nIt has been hypothesized that a mixture of Bolg and Ogre would result in this appearance.\n\nSome researchers have corroborated this, but it's far from conclusive, and it is not fully accepted.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Bow","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot ,\" makes a ranged attack with a bow. Accuracy and Damage are the same as normal attacks."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur with [ ► Bow]."},{"title":"◯ Phytotoxin/6 (13)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If a [ ► Bow] attack hits, the target suffers -2 Evasion for 3 minutes (18 rounds). This effect does not stack with itself. This is a Poison-type effect.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G / Black-White A) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nVial of Phytotoxin (150G / Green-White A) |\n11+ |\nBottle of Phytotoxin (300G / Green-White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Alkaloid Arrow","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"65jEAPSbc0CrurCj","name":"Talos Warrior","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:talos-warrior","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Vulcan","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice Damage +3","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"BM","description":"Heavily armed and armored even for a Talos , it bears a sword and large shield and stands slightly taller than a Talos Soldier. Endowed with great combat ability and judgment, it stands as an impregnable line of defense against those who would harm its master.\n\nIt is unable to sustain its existence if it does not consume a Humanoid heart once every 10 months.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Anti-Magic Shell","description":"Gains a +4 bonus to resistance checks against magic. However, this does not apply to resistance to Fairy Magic and Nature Magic."},{"title":"◯ Fairy/Spirit Blindness","description":"Cannot sense or hear the voices of fairies and spirits. When damaged by Fairy Magic, Fairies, or Nature Magic, it suffers 3 additional points of damage."},{"title":"⏩ △ Defense of Ignis","description":"The Talos Warrior becomes covered in fire and gains +3 Defense for 10 Seconds (1 Round). Anyone who makes a melee attack versus the Talos during this period, regardless of success or failure, must suffer 2d of Fire magic. This causes the Talos to receive 5 points of fixed damage on its next turn."},{"title":"🗨 Power Attack I","description":"They can deal an additional +4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"🗨 △ Cover II","description":"This is identical to the combat feat [ Cover II ].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 8 |\nShattered Ignis Ore Core (300G/Gold Black A) |\n9+ |\nCracked Ignis Ore Core (1,000G/Gold Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Talos Warrior","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"6UntSzwUlnWgkkOv","name":"Baba Yaga Witch","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:baba-yaga-witch","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Varies","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"14/-","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Savage Song of Misfits p. 204","description":"These are magic-proficient Baba Yagas . Though few in number, most of them have mastered magic, and when they transform into the appearance of old women to cast their spells, they demonstrate terrifying power.\n\nThey often transform into the appearance of old women during emergencies or combat, and there have been cases where individuals have blended into Humanoid society with their true identity remaining concealed for long periods.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Baba Yaga Witch","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"75XJ5y0VWMc2yeHk","name":"Tusk Crazy","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tusk-crazy","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Mountains, Caves","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Slashing damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Dorden , p. 121","description":"These are central figures in many Tusk Hammer and Tusk Force settlements. Individuals who maintain actual power while possessing magical knowledge attain this position. They have mastered Divine Magic , and many Tusk Crazies worship Dalkhrem.\n\nRather than directly leading the herd, they prefer a method where they give advice and instructions to a few of their close aides, while keeping themselves out of the spotlight.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 9 (16)","description":""},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"🗨Mana Strike = +9 damage","description":"A Tusk Crazy may deal an additional +9 damage to their next melee attack. If they do, they receive a -2 penalty to Fortitude, and Willpower checks until their next turn."},{"title":"⏩Fang Thrust / 10 (17) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Between attacks, a Tusk Crazy can also attack with their facial fangs, dealing 1d+1 (minimum of 0) points of fixed damage.\nIf it uses this ability on a target that has been hit with a Melee Attack during this turn, it gains a +1 bonus to the success value of this ability.\nIf it deals 1 or more points of fixed damage with this ability, the Tusk Crazy also receives 2 points of fixed damage."},{"title":"⏩Boar's Roar / Can't","description":"The Tusk Crazy lets out a war cry, inspiring its allies. With \"Range: Caster\" and within \"Radius: 6m (1 area) / All,\" all Tusk Hammers , Tusk Forces , and Tusk Crazies, excluding themselves, gain a +1 bonus to their Accuracy check.\nThis effect is Psychic type."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If HP falls to 0 or less due to magic damage, the \"Decorated Fang\" loot will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nDecorated Fang (1,000G/Red A) x 2 |\n2 - 10 |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |\n8+ |\nWell-Kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tusk Crazy","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7HPp3tcjRFczQTkU","name":"Diablo Captain (Daemon Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:diablo-captain-daemon-form","level":16,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Daemonic","habitat":"Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":24,"weakness":27,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3 points","initiative":24,"movementSpeed":"25/25(Flying)","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"20 (27)","source":"CR III p. 340","description":"This is the Daemon form of the Diablo Captain (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Tough Skin","description":"Whenever it receives physical or magical damage of the bludgeoning type, it is reduced by -3 points.\nHead"},{"title":"◯ Limited 2 Actions","description":"The monster can perform two Major Actions in one round. However, the monster must choose two different actions from the melee attack, [ ► Daemonic Eyes III] or [ ► Daemonic Cursed Rain]."},{"title":"► Daemonic Eyes III/Can't","description":"Same as for Diablo Captain (Human Form)."},{"title":"► Daemonic Cursed Rain/20 (27)/Willpower/Half","description":"First, the Head must spend 10 points of MP to use this ability. Then, roll 2d, and calculate the Intensity of the effect as \"roll + 5\".\nThe Diablo Captain receives fixed damage of Intensity points, and at the same time, at \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius)/All\" receive \"Intensity x 3\" curse magical damage. Any character within this range can be excluded from the target."},{"title":"► Humanification","description":"It changes to the Human form. For data on the Human form, refer to Diablo Captain (Human Form) . If the Head section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it immediately falls unconscious.\n[ ► Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after [ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] was used. Also, [ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] cannot be used for 3 hours immediately after the [ ► Humanification] was used.\nRight Side/Left Side"},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"All sections receive a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf either the Right Side or Left Side section falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides.\nRight Side"},{"title":"◯ Daemons Strengthening","description":"All Daemon monsters within \"Range: Self\" and \"Target: All Areas(30m Radius)/All\" receive a +2 bonus on all action checks except Evasion checks, and the physical and magic damage they cause is increased by +2 points.\nLeft Side"},{"title":"◯ Barbarous Strengthening","description":"All Barbarous monsters (except this monster) within \"Range: Self\" and \"Target: All Areas(30m Radius)/All\" receive a +2 bonus on all action checks except Evasion checks, and the physical and magic damage they cause is increased by +2 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G) x 2d |\n2 - 4 |\nJet-Black Gem (2,200G/Gold S) |\n5 - 11 |\nTrue Dark Gem (4,900G/Gold S) |\n12+ |\nAbyssal Treasure (15,500G/Gold SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Diablo Captain (Daemon Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"7cuv1CqnbHqaUFHl","name":"Hook Hoodling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hook-hoodling","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Various","reputation":8,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"KF","description":"They are Hoodling Youma who quickly appear on the outer edges of towns inhabited by Humanoids and carry out destruction and looting. They carry 10-meter-long hooked ropes in their hands, which they use to hook ceilings and other objects, and move about by swinging down like a pendulum.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Hook Rope","description":"Attacks with Grappling Hook are treated as melee attacks that reach up to Range: 1 (10m)."},{"title":"⏩ △ Hanging by a Rope","description":"The piece of rope is used to hang from an overhead structure or other object. The Hook Hoodling does not receive the usual poor-footing penalty until the beginning of their next round. Additionally, they receive a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks, and damage is reduced by -2.\nNote that this ability can only be used in environments with ceilings or tall structures overhead, such as in a city.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHook Rope (50G/Black White B) x 2 |\n2 - 5 |\nNothing |\n6 - 10 |\nDirty Hood (20G/White B) |\n11+ |\nWorn Hood (80G/White B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hook Hoodling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"8i5QmgiQoZ5QhUK2","name":"Cryoblaz","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cryoblaz","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Cold Regions","reputation":9,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"2 (9)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 117","description":"This Barbarous, commonly found in the Diggad Mountains, is approximately the size of a Human and has transparent ice needles covering its body surface, similar to porcupines. As their appearance suggests, these Barbarous are well-suited to cold environments and have established their strongholds in frozen barren lands. They intermittently attack Humanoid settlements.\n\nThe \"Ice Needles\" that adorn their bodies serve as the material for Head Cooling Needles.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"⏩Freezing Stance","description":"This effect lasts for 10 seconds (1 round), does not accumulate, and consumes 3 MP when used.\nDamage caused by a Weapon attack becomes Water/Ice type and increases by +2. If the Cryoblaz is hit by a melee attack, the attacker will be dealt an additional 1 point of Water/Ice fixed damage for the duration, regardless of the success or failure of the melee attack.\nThis effect ends immediately after the Cryoblaz receives 1 or more points of Fire-type applied damage without waiting 10 seconds (1 round). If it is caused by a melee attack, the effect disappears first, and the attacker will not be dealt fixed damage."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"9+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cryoblaz","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"94UwP5ZVIMp3JJsC","name":"Zeanemo Shaman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zeanemo-shaman","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Elven, Sylvan","habitat":"Seas","reputation":13,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12/18 (swimming)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 118","description":"Among the Zeanemo , there are some who deal with Fairy Magic, perhaps as a remnant from the time when they were Elves. However, because of their aggressive and coarse treatment of magic, they are hated by the fairies.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 4 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Light, or Dark types.\nIt does not change even if the contract pattern (see MA, p. 136) is used."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles / 7 (14) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This ability may only be used once per turn, just before a Major Action. Within \"Range: Touch\" it is used to entangle \"Target: 1 Character\" with the tentacles within their right eye. If the target fails the Evasion check, the following two effects occur:\n- If the monster makes a melee attack against its target immediately afterward, the target's Evasion check is decreased by -2. This effect only applies to that single Evasion check (the tentacles automatically release after the melee attack).\n- The target must perform a Fortitude Check with Target Number 12. If the target fails, it is paralyzed for the next 1 minute (6 rounds) and suffers a -1 penalty on Accuracy checks. This effect is Poison type and does not accumulate."},{"title":"◯Behind the Right Eye","description":"The character who became the target of the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles] can declare that they will \"aim at the right eye\" when making a weapon attack against this monster on their turn (regardless of whether the Evasion check was successful or not against the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles]). If the declared attack hits, its physical and/or magic damage is increased by 4 points.\nIf this action is taken and the increase in damage actually occurs, PCs will no longer receive the loot \"Blue Strange Eye\" from the targeted monster.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBlue Strange Eye (160G/Red B) |\n2 - 7 |\nPearl Fragments (50G/Gold Red B) |\n8+ |\nOcean Pearl (200G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zeanemo Shaman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"9PVffIm6Q0S6BAMm","name":"Lesser Ogre","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lesser-ogre","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Ogre, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":9,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR I p. 402","description":"Standing about 2 meters tall, a Lesser Ogre is a fearsome flesh-eating behemoth of pure muscle. Lesser Ogres are still small among Ogres (see ML p. 58). A Lesser Ogre's most distinctive feature is its ability to take on Human form.\n\nThose who actively take on Human form often have a deep knowledge of Human culture, which may be why some have a Human-like personality and mindset. A Lesser Ogre can automatically take one unique Humanoid form which is considered \"theirs,\" but if it eats the heart of a Humanoid, it can also take that individual's form. The more hearts they eat, the more forms they can take.\n\nIt is difficult to detect a Lesser Ogre disguised as a Humanoid. The PCs must have sufficient reason to be suspicious (as judged by the GM) to perform a Detect check (see CR I, p. 111).","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 3 Level / Magic Power 5 (12)","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Personification","description":"A Lesser Ogre may take on the appearance and mannerisms of a character they have eaten or can change back. It can be either innate or something that once had its heart eaten out of it.\nWhen transformed, the Lesser Ogre's maximum HP and MP are decreased by 5. Accuracy, Evasion, Fortitude, and Willpower are also reduced by 1 point each. This form can be held up to 18 hours per day.\nThe [ ⏩ △ Personification] can also be canceled by Minor Action and Combat Preparation.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 3 |\nNothing |\n4 - 8 |\nBag of Silver (30G) x 1d |\n9 - 10 |\nBag of Silver (100) x 1d |\n11+ |\nGem (150G/Gold A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lesser Ogre","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"A26IR6jYrkaxJETh","name":"Merman Bishop","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:merman-bishop","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":2,"languages":"Merman, Elven","habitat":"Ocean","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"5 (Leap) / 20 (Swimming)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR II p. 337","description":"Bishops are one of the strongest Mermen . They follow the gods and lead their tribes as prescribed by their words. Bishops even have the ear of Merman chiefs, giving them considerable political power.\n\nWhile Merman Bishops tend to follow the Ancient Gods, regardless of whether they're gods of the First Sword, Lumiere, or the Second Sword, Ignis, some will follow gods that have recently found apotheosis and are thus unknown among the land-dwelling races.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Divine Magic 6 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"◯ Underwater Specialization","description":"Can move in water without penalties and restrictions. Conversely, all action checks are subject to a -2 penalty on the ground.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nRusty Spear (50G/Black White B) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 12 |\nBeautiful Shell (180/Gold Red A) |\n13+ |\nSilver Pearl (3,000G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Merman Bishop","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"A2GVHnStTSBkwLlS","name":"Diablo Cadet (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:diablo-cadet-human-form","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Daemonic","habitat":"Wasteland, Shallow","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Energy type damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"20/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR I p. 404","description":"It is said that this race was created at the end of the Magic Civilization Period as a result of a fusion experiment between Barbarous and Daemons. Known on the Alframe continent as the upper Barbarous along with Drakes, Cadets are young candidates for leadership.\n\nThey have blue-colored skin, large and prominent horns, and black jewels in which the mana is condensed in various body parts. Although they do not have wings, they are able to float with the power of their jewels. Their facial features resemble those of Humans and Elves, and they are intimidating and highly charismatic at the same time.\n\nWhile flexible, their skin instantly hardens to protect the body against strong attacks, and sharp prongs extend from the shoulders, elbows, knuckles, and fingertips (the presence varies from individual to individual). These protrusions can be pulled out to create their own weapons (mainly swords and spears).\n\nDiablos have the ability to transform into a form similar to that of a daemon. This transformation makes them twice their size and gives them incredible power.\n\nWith numerous Bolgs (see ML p. 75) and Goblins (see ML p. 73) in their ranks, they attack the Humanoid realm with their prowess and guile.\n\nFor the Daemon form of this monster, see Diablo Cadet (Daemon Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Tough Skin","description":"Whenever it receives physical or magical damage of the Bludgeoning type, it is reduced by -3 points."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters within its reach with melee attacks, but the damage will be reduced by -3. If more than one is hit, the damage is determined individually."},{"title":"► Daemonic Eyes/Can't","description":"With a sharp look in its eyes, it can make enemies shrivel.\nWith \"Range/Area: 1 (10m)/ Target ,\" select any number of targets and deal each of them 2 Curse magic damage. Afterward, Diablo's HP is restored by the sum of all applied damage dealt to the targets.\nUsing this ability consumes 2 points of MP per character targeted."},{"title":"► Daemonshift","description":"The character changes into a daemon form. For data, see Diablo Cadet (Daemon Form) . HP and MP are restored to their maximum values, and all effects of magic, etc., are negated. In the turn in which [ ► Daemonshift] is performed, only the Body section of the Daemon Form is treated as having completed a Major Action, and the Head section can make its own Major Action this turn.\n[ ► Daemonshift] cannot be used for 3 hours immediately after the [ ► Humanification] was used. Also, [ ► Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after [ ► Daemonshift] was used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G) |\n2 - 6 |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) |\n7 - 10 |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) x 2 |\n11+ |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Diablo Cadet (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"B92CQLdzjTtNtNao","name":"Bolg Assassinator","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bolg-assassinator","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"21","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 349","description":"This is a Bolg Youma assassin who specializes in fast attacks. Their role is to target and strike the key commanders of the enemy army.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fast Action","description":"During the first round of combat, if the monster wins initiative, it may take two Major Actions that round."},{"title":"◯ Shadow Sneak","description":"Can leave and pass through skirmishes without movement blocking or the Prepare to Withdraw action."},{"title":"► Double Attack","description":"It can attack the same target twice in one action with its Weapon."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBarbarous Decree (500G/White A) |\n2 - 7 |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) x 2 |\n8 - 12 |\nWell-Kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S) x 2 |\n13+ |\nRare Weapon (4,000G/Black White S) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bolg Assassinator","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"BbKhpArFTPWiXqkf","name":"Tannoz","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tannoz","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Sylvan","habitat":"Coast, Riverside","reputation":12,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"13/13 (Swimming)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 339","description":"Tannoz are ugly Barbarous that live mainly by the seashore and riverside. They are short and have wrinkled faces. Their right hand is a pair of crab-like pincers, and they carry a lantern in their left hand. These lanterns are used for hunting prey, confusing and stranding boats at night, and luring Humanoids into swamps and rivers. Sometimes they can also be seen inland serving other Barbarous.\n\nTannoz are hated by Humanoid fairy tamers because they do not make contracts with their fairies, but force them to work.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 6 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"It can use Earth, Water/Ice, Wind, and Dark magic types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nSharp Pincers (50G/Red B) |\n5 - 9 |\nDangerous Pincers (570G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nDeadly Pincers (1,660G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tannoz","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"BcskVtinY3FjrSsj","name":"Macabrefist","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:macabrefist","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Barrens, Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Slashing-type Damage +3","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla , p. 124","description":"This is a Rumblefist who, due to their sturdy physique, was subjected to humiliating experiments by magicians and ultimately enhanced themselves by embedding an Abyss Shard into their body out of revenge. Frequently spotted near the Haroon Magical Research Kingdom during the Magic Civilization Period, and due to this survival strategy being passed down within the race, they still occasionally appear in the Ursyla region today.\n\nDue to the power of the Abyss, they can transform mental pollution into their own strength and spread their race's inherited emotion of grudge as waves of terror.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Lightning Immunity, ◯Bludgeoning Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Elastic Skin","description":"Treated as having +3 Defense against blunt weapons."},{"title":"⏩Fist of Terror","description":"This effect can only be used when this monster is under some Psychic-type effect. Consume 1d HP to automatically remove one Psychic-type effect of your choice that is affecting you. No Success Value comparison is performed.\nFor 3 minutes (18 rounds) afterward, a face of the dead appears on their fist, granting +1 Accuracy and +2 damage to fist attacks. Additionally, when a fist attack hits, it deals 2 points of Psychic-type fixed damage to the target's MP. This effect stacks up to 3 times per psychic effect removed (maximum of +3 Accuracy, +6 damage, 6 points of fixed damage to MP). The Psychic-type removal itself can be performed any number of times.\nWhile this effect is active, Macabrefist gains \"Resistance: Optional\" against all Psychic-type effects they receive."},{"title":"►Field of Terror / 10 (17) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Using this effect consumes 7 MP points. Fills \"Range: Touch\" with \"Target: 1 area (3m radius) / 5\" with an aura of terror. Those who fail their Willpower check receive a -2 penalty modifier to Accuracy checks. This is a psychic-type effect that lasts for 3 minutes (18 rounds) and does not stack."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"Each time this monster uses [⏩Fist of Terror], add +2 to the Loot Determination roll.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G) |\n2 - 12 |\nNothing |\n13+ |\nDeceased's Facial Skin (450G/Red White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Macabrefist","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CSM0ina5WnyEgZep","name":"Arbor Elder","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:arbor-elder","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Sylvan","habitat":"Forests","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.92","description":"This is the chief of the village of Arbors . At first glance, there is no difference from the young Arbor. However, their eye-like patterns have increased, and their skin shows bark-like cracks.\n\nThey are even more adept at magic, and their ability to control fire is also formidable.\n\nIn large Arbor villages, several elders may rule in the council. These settlements are very powerful and dangerous. The elders may serve as counselors to Drakes and other Upper Barbarous and are skilled at intelligence work.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Magic (1 system) 10 Level /Magic Power 13 (20)","description":"Arbor Senior can cast either Fairy Magic or Nature Magic at the 10th level. In the case of Fairy Magic, the types used are \"Earth\" and \"Fire\"."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Metamagic/Targets ],[ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"► Roaring Fire Armor","description":"Arbor cloaks in its rage themself and its surroundings in a suit of flaming armor. Up to 10 targets in 1 area (3m radius) around the Arbor Elder treat their weapons as fire-type magic weapons (that still deal physical damage) and gain +2 points of damage for 10 seconds (1 round). At the same time, the target's Defense is reduced by 12 points.\nThis effect can be used only once per round, and it costs 10 MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nOminous Branches (130G/Red Green A) x 1d |\n2 - 8 |\nFiery Residue (900G/Gold A) |\n9+ |\nVindictive Residue (2,400G/Gold S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Arbor Elder","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CUdiyMsW0BX8VMgo","name":"Areigo","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:areigo","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Drakish","habitat":"Plains, Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"20/-","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"BM","description":"A Barbarous with a frail body but a plump abdomen. By pounding its belly like a gong, it boosts the morale of its surrounding comrades.\n\nIts stomach contains a high density of crystallized mana, which it can explode at will.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ Stratagem &amp; Maneuvers/1 Area (5m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Surging Offense I ] (Physical Damage +1).\nEvery third turn, uses [ Maneuver: Unexpected Blow I ] (Accuracy +2, Damage +2). If there are no characters eligible to be affected by a Stratagem, these abilities will not be used."},{"title":"► Self-Destruction/7 (14)/Fortitude/Half","description":"\"Range: Caster\", \"Target: 1 area (3m Radius)/5\" deals 2d+5 Bludgeoning magic damage, and then the Areigo's HP becomes 0 and it dies.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBarbarous Flag (2000G/Red Green S) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nExplosive Reactant Crystal Debris (600G/Red Black A) |\n13+ |\nFragment of Explosive Reactant Crystal (1600G/Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Areigo","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Cb2pecjUz8LLcYze","name":"Troll","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:troll","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Giantish","habitat":"Caves","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CR I p. 407","description":"A Troll's stature is like that of a boulder; standing taller than 3m, its skin is tougher than a rock. For Barbarous, Trolls have incredible discipline and take great pride in maintaining their physique. They are also devout followers of the gods.\n\nTroll blood is said to symbolize power as well, and it is often used as a sort of paint. When applied by a Troll, it will strengthen weapons and armor. Even a Troll's skin can be toughened by its own blood.\n\nTrolls are often nocturnal creatures as well and dislike bright lights. Sunlight, in particular, will significantly weaken a Troll, and they abhor going out during the daytime.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 5 Level/Magic Power 7 (14)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Weakening","description":"As long as a Troll is under sunlight, it receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nTroll Blood (100G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nLarge Weapon (300G/Black White A) |\n9+ |\nGems (150G/Gold A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Troll","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"CyCZggqWzO6zgJdm","name":"Bolg Highlander","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bolg-highlander","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":9,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 401","description":"These are the leaders of a small group of Bolg Youma tribesmen.\n\nArmed with a two-handed greatsword, they exhibit overwhelming combat prowess.\n\nThey make their home in underground labyrinths and ruins and repeatedly attack Human settlements. Bolgs believe that the bigger the weapon, the stronger they are, and they are more daring and bold in their fighting style.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨 Repeated Strike I","description":"Can make two Accuracy checks; if one hits, the damage is dealt once."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nKeen Weapon (100G/Black White A) |\n6 - 9 |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |\n10+ |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bolg Highlander","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"D0XXBGDAL4NYW8Dh","name":"Centaur","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:centaur","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Centaur, Sylvan","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"22 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CR II p. 333","description":"These are Barbarous, with a Human's upper body connected to a horse's body. They are proud to be Barbarous, fight nobly, and prefer to make a name for themself fairly and squarely.\n\nCentaurs also tend to be excellent soldiers, with a reputation for faithfully following orders.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 2 Level/Magic Power 4 (11)","description":"It can use Earth, Fire, Wind, and Light magic types."},{"title":"► Charge/5 (12)/Evasion/Negates","description":"This ability can only be used in a round in which a Normal Move is made.\nCharges and spears 1 enemy character as with melee attack, dealing 2d+7 physical damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nBattle Gear (30G/White B) |\n11+ |\nFine Outfit (120G/White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Centaur","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"D1MywFyg0CF5JF9l","name":"Cold Medusa","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cold-medusa","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Cold climates","reputation":14,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"14/-","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"CO","description":"This is a subspecies of Medusa that appears to have a body made entirely of translucent ice. Its snake hair has white scales, and it prefers to wear white garments. These creatures inhabit cold regions, such as snowfields and ice-covered caves, and are known as \"Evil Spirits of the Snow\" in some areas.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Fire Vulnerability","description":"When the Cold Medusa is hit by Fire-type damage, it takes an extra 3 damage."},{"title":"◯ Melting Fangs","description":"If the target receives 1 or more points of applied damage of Fire type, it loses the ability of [ ◯ Freezing Fang] for the following 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"► Simultaneous Attack","description":"A Cold Medusa's Snake Hair attacks all enemy characters in the same position."},{"title":"◯ Freezing Fang/7 (14)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"If a Snake Hair attack hits, the victim is petrified (Dexterity/Agility – 12).\nCharacters whose stats are reduced by 0 due to this effect (or, if the character has monster data, receives this effect 3 times), become ice statues. The ice sculpture will melt in 48 hours at room temperature, in 12 hours in heat equivalent to a bonfire, or 24 hours in heat equivalent to a torch. If the character melts, they will die and their corpse will be permanently destroyed.\nThe effect is Curse + Water/Ice type. Even after becoming an ice statue, a character can survive as long as the curse is removed. However, normal methods of removing petrification are ineffective."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If the Cold Medusa is slain while [ ◯ Melting Fangs] is active, the Loot \"Frozen Fang\" cannot be gained.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nFrozen Fang (330G/Gold Red A) |\n6 - 9 |\nFrozen Fang (330G/Gold Red A) x 2 |\n10+ |\nFrozen Fang (330G/Gold Red A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cold Medusa","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"E8V8enBbQEREBhSR","name":"Arbor","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:arbor","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Sylvan","habitat":"Forests","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 81","description":"Arbors are Barbarous that live deep within the forest. They resemble Humans but have white skin like snow and white or light green hair. They have large eye-like patterns on their forehead and all over their body.\n\nArbors are considered close relatives of Meria . Although they do not have flowers, their ecology and body structure are similar to those of the long-lived Meria. According to legend, during the War of the Gods, the trees in the forests that Dwarves burned to make large quantities of armor took human form with the hatred fueled by Ignis. Arbors especially hate Dwarves and are also enemies of Artificers , since their forests were massively cut down during the Magitech Civilization Period.\n\nArbors are skilled at spy missions and may engage in intelligence, reconnaissance, and sabotage in cooperation with Drakes and other Upper Barbarous (see ML p. 60).\n\nThey have a small number of soulscars and are not affected by Swords of Protection, so they may lead Ogres (see p. 83) to infiltrate the city. However, since Arbors themselves do not have the shapeshifting ability, it is relatively easy to detect their disguise. Even if they are discovered, Arbors are not only excellent sword-wielders, but also fearsome Fairy and Nature magic- users with the ability to make people feel the fire of rage.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Magic (1 system) 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"An Arbor can cast either Fairy Magic or Nature Magic at the 5th level.\nIn the case of Fairy Magic, the types used are \"Earth\" and \"Fire\"."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"► Weapons of Raging Fire","description":"Sows weapons with its own angry fire. The Arbor empowers up to 5 targets within an area (3m radius) centered on itself with fire. Empowered targets now deal Fire-type damage, and their melee and ranged weapons are treated as magical weapons for 3 minutes (18 rounds), granting +2 points to physical damage (not magic damage).\nUsing this effect consumes 8 points of MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nOminous Branches (130G/Red Green A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nFiery Residue (900G/Gold A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Arbor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"F7W2ktMsCRCKtnTC","name":"Ogre Wizard","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ogre-wizard","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Ogre, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.89","description":"This is a high-ranking Ogre with excellent magical abilities. They are capable of casting Truespeech Magic and Spiritualism Magic and often blend in with humanoids to carry out their evil deeds.\n\nOgre Wizards are considered elite among Ogres and sometimes command infiltration teams of Lesser Ogres . They use Lesser Ogres to secretly neutralize the Swords of Protection and enter Humanoid cities. Ogre Wizards are known to gradually replace the inhabitants of a city with Ogres under their control and then one day reveal their true nature and ravage the city. When an Ogre Wizard is discovered in a town, it is often too late to stop them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 8 Level/Magic Power 11 (18)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩ △ Personification","description":"An Ogre Wizard may take on the appearance and mannerisms of a character they have eaten or change back.\nWhen transformed, the Ogre Wizard's maximum HP and MP are decreased by 5. Accuracy, Evasion, Fortitude, and Willpower are also reduced by 1 point each. This form can be held up to 18 hours per day.\nThe [ ⏩ △ Personification] can also be ended with Minor Action or during Combat Preparation.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nBag of Silver (100G) x 1d |\n7 - 11 |\nGem (150G/Gold A) x 1d |\n12+ |\nGold Bracelet (2,500G/Gold White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ogre Wizard","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FG5TFzbB60gwGYWt","name":"Dawn Walker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dawn-walker","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"KF","description":"Dawn Walkers are Barbarous creatures that wear black cloaks and infiltrate humanoid habitats. They are about 1.8 meters tall, with stout, rounded backs. Their bodies are entirely covered in dark-colored body hair, and they have long, sharp claws on both hands.\n\nThey possess knowledge of stealth and carry out their duties unnoticed at the request of the Upper Barbarous. Loyal and modest, they prioritize the accomplishment of their mission above all else.\n\nThey follow Dalkhrem, Zeides, and Eiryak, and sometimes act as liaisons between their Barbarous followers and their pagan cults of Humanoids.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 4 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBarbarous' Orders (500G/White A) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8+ |\nNight Robe (280G/White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dawn Walker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"FLmj4I0SJaJcJ7bb","name":"Sabinga","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sabinga","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Mountains, Floating Rocks","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Wind-type Damage +3","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"10/10 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"CO","description":"The Sabinga are flying Youma , whose existence is confirmed in Genguntekul, \"The Rock of the Feather Prince,\" in the Constellation of Colonies Cyrecode. Similar to Goblins in appearance, they possess large, fin-like wings on their lower limbs, which they spread wide to fly. They move slowly while in flight, but by rapidly opening and closing their wings, they can maneuver in a somersault-like motion.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨 Somersault Attack","description":"Flips and flutters back and forth in front of the target, attacking at an irregular trajectory.\nDeclaring this before a melee attack grants the Sabinga a +1 bonus to its Accuracy Check, but incurs a -1 penalty to its Evasion Check.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 9 |\nWeapon (30G/Black White B) |\n10+ |\nKeen Weapon (100G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sabinga","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"GMsReq1eZwEn2xBT","name":"Tusk Force","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tusk-force","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Mountains, Caves","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Slashing damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Natural History of Dorden , p. 120","description":"This is a Tusk Hammer who leads the herd. Their body length is slightly larger, reaching about 1.5 meters, and they stand out from others with accessories and higher quality weapons.\n\nAfter hunting animals for meat, Tusk Forces have a custom of collecting and storing the drained animal blood somewhere. The purpose of this practice has not been revealed to this day, and among various theories, none are considered particularly convincing.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩Fang Thrust / 5 (12) / Evasion / Negates","description":"Between attacks, a Tusk Force can also attack with their facial fangs, dealing 1d-1 (minimum of 0) points of fixed damage.\nIf it uses this ability on a target that has been hit with a Melee Attack during this turn, it gains a +1 bonus to the success value of this ability.\nIf it deals 1 or more points of fixed damage with this ability, the Tusk Force also receives 1 point of fixed damage."},{"title":"⏩Boar's Roar / Can't","description":"The Tusk Force lets out a war cry, inspiring its allies. With \"Range: Caster\" and within \"Radius: 6m (1 area) / All,\" all Tusk Hammers , Tusk Forces, and Tusk Crazies , excluding themselves, gain a +1 bonus to their Accuracy check.\nThis effect is Psychic type."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If HP falls to 0 or less due to magic damage, the \"Splendid Fang\" loot will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSplendid Fang (400G/Red A) x 2 |\n2 - 7 |\nKeen Weapon (100G/Black White A) |\n8+ |\nHigh-Quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tusk Force","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"GVSHyXrQfumATdF0","name":"Drake Baron (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:drake-baron-human-form","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"20/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 346","description":"Similar in appearance to the Drakes , yet with a much more regal presence, Drake Barons are imposing leaders of the Barbarous. The only difference is that they are more beautiful and more refined and are dressed in luxurious costumes. The dragon form is one size larger than the normal Drake, and its crest is shining in copper color.\n\nWhile it's rumored there are little more than 100 of these Drake Barons throughout the entirety of Raxia, even those few are enough to bring much of humanity to its knees.\n\nFor the Dragon form of this monster, see Drake Baron (Dragon Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 7 Level /Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats[ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], and [ Recovery (5 pts.) ] Techniques."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +10 damage","description":"May deal an additional +10 damage to their next melee attack. At risk, they take a -2 penalty to their Fortitude and Willpower checks."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Dragonification","description":"The Drake transforms into a draconic form, healing all HP and MP. Any lingering magical effects are removed as well. For more information, see the Drake Baron (Dragon Form) stats. In the turn in which [ ► Dragonification] is performed, only the Body section of Dragon Form is treated as having completed the Major Action, and Wings sections can make them on this turn.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Dragonification].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSword Shard (200G) x 5 |\n2 - 9 |\nDraconian Horn (500G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nMajestic Draconian Horn (4,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Drake Baron (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"GmAPFM1aETtm6B35","name":"Kobold","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kobold","level":1,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":1,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":6,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 395","description":"Kobolds are the weakest Youma among the Barbarous. They are about 1.2m tall and resemble upright dogs. Other Barbarous treat them like slaves or emergency rations, and some of them flee to the Humanoid cities to escape persecution.\n\nThey are obedient to everyone and loyal to those who feed them. Because of their dexterity and culinary skills, they can often be seen working in the dining hall attached to the Adventurers' Guild.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kobold","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HBvxoOaaK59ZcXut","name":"Medusa","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:medusa","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Labyrinths","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR II p. 333","description":"Often mistaken for a human female, Medusae are Barbarous with multiple thin snakes for hair. Not only can a Medusa slowly petrify unlucky adventurers, but the hair snakes are also poisonous. Rarely, a Medusa's eyes may retain their fearsome gaze after death. These magical eyes can be used to make magical armor and command a high price in the markets.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Simultaneous Attack","description":"A Medusa's Snake Hair attacks all enemy characters in the skirmish, but a separate Accuracy Check is needed for each character."},{"title":"◯ Snake Venom/5 (12)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"If the Snake Hair attack hits, it inflicts 3 Poison magic damage to the target."},{"title":"◯ Eyes of Stone/4 (11)/Willpower/Negates","description":"At the end of each round, if a character faces a Medusa, they need to roll a Willpower Check or receive effects of Petrification (Dexterity, Agility/-6).\nThis effect is treated as Curse type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nViper of Medusa (50G/Red B) |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10 - 12 |\nGem (150G/Red A) x 1d |\n13+ |\nEyes of Stone (1,200G/Gold, Red, Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Medusa","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"HnxCCCrezKysNj99","name":"Goblin Lord","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:goblin-lord","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":9,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14/-","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"BM","description":"Dressed in flashy costumes, Goblin Lords represent the royals who lead Goblins from amongst the ranks of Goblin Shamans . They prefer to live under the protection of many other goblins, and thus rarely appear in the Humanoid realm.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨 Power Attack I","description":"They can deal an additional +4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"⏩ Aspect/All Areas (20m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Heavenly Domain: Invisible Pavilion ], [ Earthly Domain: Healing Earth ], and [ Spirit Domain: Determination ] with 2 Qi points."},{"title":"◯ King's Pride","description":"Gains +1 to Skill Checks it performs as long as there is a goblin other than the Goblin Lord in the same battlefield (defined as any creature with \"Goblin\" in its name [except for High Goblins] that is also Barbarous).\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nBag of Silver (50G/-) x 1d |\n8 - 12 |\nGem (150G/Gold A) x 1d |\n13+ |\nGoblin Crown (700G/Gold White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Goblin Lord","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"I4jBSI1ukUpRThW3","name":"Minotaur Caster","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:minotaur-caster","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Minotaur, languages by magic system","habitat":"Various","reputation":11,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 345","description":"A much smarter variety of Minotaur , these masters of magic are ferociously cunning. Willing to lie in wait in their labyrinth, a Minotaur Caster will use a variety of traps, spells, and other monsters to wear down any intruders before joining the fray themselves.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Magic (2 Systems) 8 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"Can use any two of Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic , Divine Magic , and Fairy Magic at 8 levels. Fairy Magic has Earth, Water/Ice, Fire, and Dark types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"A Minotaur Caster can use the Combat Feats [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Targeting ]."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters with melee attacks that can be reached, but the damage will be reduced by -3. If more than one is hit, the damage is determined individually.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMinotaur's Axe (475G/Black White A) |\n2 - 6 |\nBig Horn (150G/Red A) |\n7 - 9 |\nBeautiful Horn (600G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nMajestic Horn (3,500G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Minotaur Caster","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"IKO3hxwds0clpFUo","name":"Rumblefist","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:rumblefist","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Wastelands, Mountains","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 82","description":"These Barbarous are towering beasts cloaked in black hide, standing at an imposing 2.5 meters tall. Their fists are rock-hard, mutated into weapons of deadly force. Every inch of their bodies is encased in black, resilient skin, impervious to most impacts.\n\nThese creatures are uncivilized and meritocratic, preferring to settle disputes through duels.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Lightning Immunity, Bludgeoning Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Elastic Skin","description":"Against blunt weapons, its Defense is treated as 3 points higher."},{"title":"► Quick Spinning Fist/9 (16)/Evasion/Neg","description":"It attacks by spinning both arms and swinging them widely. Up to 5 targets of Rumblefist choice will be hit with a melee attack that deals 2d+8 points of physical damage and causes them to fall prone.\nA character whose Evasion check for this ability is only 1 or 2 short of this ability's Success Value does not take any damage but only falls prone.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nWater-repellent Skin (330G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rumblefist","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Iu8kxOZxPaNVmA82","name":"Hugl Caster","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hugl-caster","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Lizardman, Barbaric, Youma, Arcana","habitat":"Desert, Mountain","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10/15 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 400","description":"Perhaps once a servant of an evil magician, some Hugls can use magic. Such individuals become leaders of small groups of Youma or preside over evil rituals.\n\nSometimes they collaborate with Bolgs and others to plan evil acts, such as an attack on a Humanoid settlement.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 3 Level/Magic Power 4 (11)","description":""},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Spells with \"Area: Shot \" fired into a skirmish will not cause stray shots."},{"title":"⏩ △ Mobile Flying","description":"It gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns. When used in Combat Preparation, it cannot be used in the first round, regardless of the result of the Initiative check.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nEarth-toned Scales (30G/Red B) |\n8+ |\nAmber Scales (90G/Red B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hugl Caster","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"IwCwCsLdOmEwzI3c","name":"Centaur Impaler","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:centaur-impaler","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Centaur, Sylvan","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":11,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"30 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 336","description":"Spear cavalry of Centaurs (see p. 74), Impalers are often young and anxious to show off their military training. Despite their youth, Centaur Impalers are the equivalent of knights in their hierarchy and will often have subordinates following their commands. In combat, a Centaur Impaler will often seek out and fight the most potent enemy in the skirmish, looking to prove themselves in battle.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 4 Level/Magic Power 6 (13)","description":"It can use Earth, Fire, Wind, and Light types."},{"title":"► Charge/7 (14)/Evasion/Neg","description":"This ability can only be used in the round in which the Normal Move is made.\nCharges and spears 1 enemy character as with melee attack, dealing 2d+14 physical damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nSpear (50G/Black White B) |\n7 - 9 |\nHeraldic Spear (150G/Black White) |\n10+ |\nWell-Balanced Spear (600G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Centaur Impaler","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"JX8gsCCxduchYm0o","name":"Werewolf","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:werewolf","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Lycanthrope","habitat":"Various","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Silver weapon damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"21","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 341","description":"One of many different shapeshifters that fall under the classification \" Lycanthrope ,\" a Werewolf is the most common of the beastmen.\n\nWhen in their Humanoid form, they would easily pass among civilized folk without issue. However, they can turn into a bestial form, growing fur over their body, their face turning to that of a wolf, and sharp claws growing from both hands. They form their own clans, with strict hierarchies based on age, so young Werewolves are beholden to help the elders when necessary.\n\nThey cannot reproduce independently, but must kidnap Humans to join them through a special ritual. Therefore, their soulscar is relatively small, and they sometimes blend in with Human society, taking advantage of their Beastification ability. In addition to wolves, there are many other species of Lycanthrope, such as tigers and bears.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Beast Power","description":"The Werewolf receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion on the night of a full moon.\nConversely, they receive a -1 penalty for Accuracy and Evasion while under sunlight."},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Werewolf can make two Claw attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Beetleskin ] and [ Strong Blood ] Techniques."},{"title":"⏩ △ Beastification","description":"A Werewolf can turn from a humanoid to a bestial form and back again. The Werewolf can only make Claw attacks while in beast form.\nThe [ ⏩ △ Beastification] can be released with Minor Action or during Combat Preparation.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 10 |\nBeastman Fur (200G/Red A) |\n11+ |\nShining Fur (1,200G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Werewolf","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KEgfESJRTXBHV1ZV","name":"Diablo Lieutenant (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:diablo-lieutenant-human-form","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Daemonic","habitat":"Wilderness, Shallow","reputation":18,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR II p. 350","description":"This is a more experienced and mighty Diablo . While Diablos are elite Barbarous who are expected to lead the Barbarous, these lieutenants are often assistants or rangers rather than corps commanders.\n\nThey will appear as servants of the more powerful Diablos if the former. If the latter, they will often lead a small number of powerful Barbarous to raid Humanoid settlements.\n\nTheir human and Daemon forms are not comparable to that of Cadets. In particular, the Daemon form is covered with poisonous gas so foul that it can even hurt the lieutenant themself.\n\nFor the Daemon form of this monster, see Diablo Lieutenant (Daemon Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Tough Skin","description":"Whenever it receives physical or magical damage of the Bludgeoning type, the damage is reduced by 3 points."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Limited 2 Actions","description":"The monster can perform two Major Actions in one round. However, this is limited to one weapon melee attack and one [ ► Daemonic Eyes II] once each.\nIt cannot use [ 🗨 Cleave II] for that melee attack."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides."},{"title":"► Daemonic Eyes II/Can't","description":"With a sharp look in its eyes, it makes enemies shrivel.\nWith \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target \", select any number of targets and deal each of them 3 curse fixed damage.\nAfterward, Diablo's HP is restored by the sum of all applied damage dealt to the targets.\nUsing this ability consumes 3 points of MP per character targeted."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift","description":"The character changes into the daemon form with Minor Actions or during Combat Preparation. For the data, see Diablo Lieutenant (Daemon Form) . HP and MP are restored to their maximum values, and all effects of magic, etc., are negated. In the turn in which this unique skill is performed, only the Body section of the Daemon Form is treated as having completed the Major Action, and the Head section can make it this turn.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] cannot be used for 3 hours immediately after the [ ► Humanification] was used. Also, [ ► Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after [ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] was used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G) x 2 |\n2 - 8 |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) x 1d |\n9+ |\nJet-Black Gem (2,200G/Gold S) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Diablo Lieutenant (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KGU5quDXKMQTHSkv","name":"Drake (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:drake-human-form","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":10,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"20/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR I p. 408","description":"Drakes are similar in appearance to beautiful young men and women, though horns gracefully sweep from their heads and membranous wings sprout from their backs. Drakes can transform into huge dragons that wield massive swords infused with magic.\n\nOther Barbarous look to Drakes as natural leaders, and huge forces have been known to gather at Drake's disposal.\n\nWhile there is often little cooperation between Drakes, a powerful \"king\" Drake appears in rare cases, followed by many other Drakes.\n\nFor the Dragon form of this monster, see Drake (Dragon Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +8 damage","description":"A Drake can deal an additional 8 damage on their next attack. However, any Fortitude or Willpower Check made by the Drake this turn receives a -1 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Dragonification","description":"The Drake transforms into a draconic form, healing all HP and MP. Any lingering magical effects are removed as well. For more information, see the Drake (Dragon Form) stats. In the turn in which [ ► Dragonification] is performed, only the Body section of Dragon Form is treated as having completed the Major Action, and Wings sections can make them on this turn.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Dragonification].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSword Shard (200G) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Drake (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KqeDmzESbRJoN1rC","name":"Succubus","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:succubus","level":12,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"19/38(Flying)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.98","description":"This Barbarous, with its beautiful female form and bat-like wings, is commonly known as a \"monster appearing in dreams.\" She appears at night to the sleeping opposite sex and sucks their life force by giving them lewd dreams. The victim eventually weakens and dies. Females are called Succubus, and males are called Incubus.\n\nThey are often seen in the service of the Immortal Queen Zeides or the Mad God Laris.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Succubus receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"► Magic (2 systems) 12 Level/Magic Power 16 (23)","description":"Succubus has mastered any two of Spiritualism Magic , Divine Magic , and Summoning Arts at the 12th level."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► Indecent Dreams / 16 (23) / Willpower / Negates","description":"Within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (20m radius)/All\" are put to sleep and shown a lewd dream. This ability deals 2d Curse damage to the target's HP or MP, immediately followed by the sleep effect. The Succubus must choose whether to target HP or MP for each use of [ ► Indecent Dreams] and will regain HP or MP equal to the damage dealt.\nThis effect is both Psychic + Curse type. However, sleep brought by this effect is treated as Psychic (Weak) type.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSuccubus Perfume (400G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nBeautiful Tail (3,000G/Red S) |\n13+ |\nCaptivating Tail (7,000G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Succubus","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"KuhZesnGcGcEynKQ","name":"Formica Chief","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:formica-chief","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Formica","habitat":"Deserts, Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Barbarous Tales (2.0 sourcebook), p. 40","description":"These are the leaders who unite the Formica tribes. Many of them are believers of Dalkhrem, the God of War. They usually stay in the nest, often guarding the nurseries, and if an enemy appears that they lead soldiers to defeat them. They may also help their tribe coexist with nearby Androscorpions .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 7 (14)","description":""},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Formica Chief can make two Weapon attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"►Formic Acid / 9 (16) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"A Formica Chief can spit acid at an enemy character in the same skirmish, dealing 2d+8 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"◯Shared Senses","description":"If there is another Formica (of any type) in the skirmish this monster is in, it gains a +1 bonus to all of its Accuracy checks. This effect is not cumulative.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGood Quality Shell (150G/Red A) |\n2 - 4 |\nSharp Weapon (100G/Black White A) x 2 |\n5 - 8 |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) x 2 |\n9+ |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Formica Chief","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Ld5Vj8QTI1Hw1aRr","name":"Formica Queen","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:formica-queen","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Formica","habitat":"Deserts, Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"5","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Barbarous Tales (2.0 sourcebook), p. 49","description":"She (Queens are always female) is the mother of an entire Formica tribe. She has a huge abdomen and lays two to three eggs per month. She can hardly move and remains quietly at the back of the nest to lay her eggs. In the absence of Formica Lords, a Queen can become the chief of the tribe.\n\nFormica juveniles spend about five years in the egg, most of which are born as Formica Soldiers. Formica live around 30 years; when the Queen feels that her death is near, she lays a special egg to produce the next Formica Queen.\n\nThey have low intelligence, and they have no interest in anything other than gathering food and producing more offspring. However, they are blessed by Dalkhrem, the God of War, and use powerful magic to heal their allies or rebuke their enemies.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 8 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Metamagic/Power Assurance ], [ Targeting ], and [ Metamagic/Distance ]."},{"title":"►Formic Acid / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"A Formica can spit acid at an enemy character in the same skirmish, dealing 2d+9 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"◯Shared Senses","description":"If there is another Formica (of any type) in the skirmish this monster is in, it gains a +2 bonus to all of its Accuracy checks. This effect is not cumulative."},{"title":"◯Distress Call","description":"If this character suffers even a single point of damage, all Formica within a 500m radius will sense it, along with the exact location of this character.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSuperior Shell (750G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nGlittering Feathers (340G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Formica Queen","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Lfe6HDvKNmlMq2gM","name":"Blood Troll","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:blood-troll","level":13,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Giantish","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"21","fortitude":"18 (25)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 334","description":"They are upper-level Dark Trolls and are in charge of leading the Trolls . They are always ready to fight without compromise to not disappoint their enemies.\n\nFighting is the highest priority in their life, and they teach other Trolls how to fight and defeat any opponent.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 13 Level / Magic Power 17 (24)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"A Blood Troll can use the Combat Feats [ Metamagic/Targets ], Multi-Action , and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +17 damage","description":"A Blood Troll may deal an additional +17 damage to their next melee attack. If they do, at risk, they receive a -2 penalty to Fortitude and Willpower checks until their next turn."},{"title":"◯ Dark Regeneration = 10 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Blood Troll recovers 10 HP. This has no effect if the Blood Troll is at 0 HP or lower or is under sunlight."},{"title":"◯ Weakened","description":"As long as a Blood Troll is under sunlight, it receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nTroll's Black Blood (500G/Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nGems (300G/Gold A) x 1d |\n7 - 11 |\nStrange Holy Symbol (3,300G/White S) |\n12+ |\nStrange God Statue (6,200G/Gold White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Blood Troll","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"MnONkbstCs4X6H0J","name":"Basilisk (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:basilisk-human-form","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Basilisk, Drakish, Youma, Arcana","habitat":"Desert, Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 342","description":"Indistinguishable from Humans at first glance, a Basilisk is a Barbarous with the power of petrification . Basilisks often wear blindfolds to suppress their petrifying gaze until they find the right target.\n\nEven then, the petrifying gaze can be used through the blindfold.\n\nOften found in deserts, they collect various lesser Barbarous as followers and enslaved people, though they have a rivalry with Drakes regarding who is stronger.\n\nPetrified animal fragments and other debris are often found near the Basilisk's birthplace.\n\nFor the Monstrous form of this monster, see Basilisk (Monstrous Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 7 Level/Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩ Petrifying Gaze/9 (16)/Willpower/Negates","description":"With \"Range/Area: 50m / Target \", it stares at the enemy and gives the effect of Petrifaction (Dexterity or Agility/-6).\nIf the target of this unique skill is holding a mirror, and if their Willpower's success value is 4 or more points higher than the Target Number, the gaze can bounce off them back to the Basilisk, always affecting them without a check even if the Basilisk is blindfolded.\nThis unique skill is Curse type, and can be used only once per round."},{"title":"◯ Poison Blood/11 (18)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"Anyone who deals damage to this monster in the same skirmish will receive 2d Poison magic damage at the end of their turn."},{"title":"► Monstrous Form","description":"The monster transforms into its monstrous form. For data on the monstrous form, see Basilisk (Monstrous Form) . HP and MP are restored to their maximum values, and all effects of spells and the like are removed. When [ ► Monstrous Form] is activated, only the Body section is treated as if it made a Major Action. The Head section may still take a Major Action on this turn. Also, the Evil Eye can use [ ⏩ Petrifying Gaze] if it has not already used it for its turn.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Monstrous Form].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBasilisk Blood (200G/Red A) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nPetrifying Eyes (1,200G/Gold Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Basilisk (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"NOZvWSd7udObWZbP","name":"Grendel","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:grendel","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Giantish, Barbaric, Sea Animal","habitat":"Sea, Coast, Lake, Shore","reputation":16,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"16/16 (Swimming)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 344","description":"These are Giants of about 4 meters in length that inhabit seashores, reefs, lakes, etc. They are sometimes found together with Tannoz .\n\nThey are especially dangerous underwater.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":"Upper Body"},{"title":"► Water Blast/12 (19)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"It slams the water's surface as hard as possible, generating waves.\nWithin \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: 1 area (4m radius) / 10,\" the target falls prone . This effect does not apply to characters not restricted while in the water by abilities such as [ ◯ Underwater Aptitude], [ ◯ Underwater Specialization], [ ◯ Underwater], or [ Sword's Grace/Gentle Water ].\nThis unique skill can only be used on or underwater.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Grendel's height prevents enemies from attacking them. The Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect disappears when the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nGold Bracelet (2,500G/Gold White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Grendel","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"O9ZIArJQ7EU9MqOP","name":"Bolg Thrower","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bolg-thrower","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Daemonic","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves, Shallows","reputation":9,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"AB, p. 89","description":"This is Bolg who uses Dark Hunter techniques. They sometimes serve as a guide for other Barbarous within the Shallows.\n\nWhile they can use their weapons directly for thrown attacks and retrieve them for reuse, this consumes HP, making their frontline durability somewhat lacking.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Thrown Attack","description":"Weapon attacks can also be treated as thrown attacks with \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot .\""},{"title":"⏩Silver Thread","description":"Retrieves the weapon used for the thrown attack back to their hand. Consumes 2 HP points before making the throwing attack.\nIf this action is not performed, this monster loses the weapon and all subsequent damage is reduced by 5 points (minimum 0)."},{"title":"⏩Aim","description":"For 30 seconds (3 rounds), gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks made during thrown attacks. Using this effect costs 1d HP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nWeapon (30G/Black White B) |\n6+ |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bolg Thrower","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"OgxiTTf3YlCfrKBa","name":"Tyrant Warrior","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tyrant-warrior","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Magitech","habitat":"Grasslands, Mountains","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"24 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Dorden , p. 119","description":"This Barbarous resides in the grasslands of the Dorden Region, with an upper body that is Humanoid and a lower body resembling a faceless black tiger. It is similar to a Centaur , but larger when fully grown.\n\nThey sometimes join other Barbarous in attacking magic trains ridden by Humanoids, but they rarely form groups within their own species, leading to frequent misidentification as large Centaur variants until recent years.\n\nTyrant Warriors are not adept at long-distance travel and usually remain near sources of water within their territory. When hunting, they utilize their impressive leg strength and attack with weapons held by their upper body. Their weapons are comparable in quality to those used by Humanoids, mainly spears and long polearms, although there are individuals known to use bows and large thrown weapons.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the HP of Lower Body section is 1 or higher and the HP of Upper Body section falls to 0 or below, the loot \"Glossy Fur\" will be lost.\nUpper Body"},{"title":"🗨Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters with melee attacks that can be reached, but the damage will be reduced by -3. If more than one is hit, the damage is determined individually."},{"title":"🗨Repeated Strike I","description":"Can make two Accuracy checks; if one hits, the damage is dealt once.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯Stable Posture","description":"If it makes a Full Move during its turn, only the Upper Body section can perform a Major Action. However, in addition to the -4 penalty on Evasion checks for Full Moves, it also receives a -2 penalty on action checks for Major Actions."},{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGlossy Fur (400G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 11 |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |\n12+ |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tyrant Warrior","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"P555hZKaN0G49p8V","name":"Tannoz Veteran","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tannoz-veteran","level":11,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Sylvan","habitat":"Coast, Riverside","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"16/16 (Swimming)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR II p. 352","description":"This is a mature and experienced Tannoz fighter. They are skilled at fighting in the water, and their sharp pincers are sharp enough to easily pierce even the hardest armor.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯ Fairy Magic 10 Level/Magic Power 12 (19)","description":"It can use Earth, Water/Ice, Wind, and Dark types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats[ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], and [ Metamagic/Targets ].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nDangerous Pincers (570G/Red A) |\n7 - 9 |\nDeadly Pincers (1,660G/Red S) |\n10+ |\nVeteran Pincers (4,400G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tannoz Veteran","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Pns0OCSR3NWM140O","name":"Centaur Penetrator","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:centaur-penetrator","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Centaurian","habitat":"Grasslands","reputation":12,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Earth damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"30 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"AB, p. 90","description":"This is a Centaur agile warrior who excels at quick movements in light armor. Despite their large build, they possess high evasion and durability, skillfully wielding a somewhat smaller spear as both a melee and thrown weapon.\n\nThey can also tactically choose between a powerful charge or thrown attacks that affects multiple targets depending on the situation. HP consumption and durability are supplemented through Techniques.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Thrown Attack","description":"Weapon attacks can also be treated as thrown attacks with \"Range/Area: 2 (20m) / Shot .\""},{"title":"⏩Silver Thread","description":"Retrieves the weapon used for the thrown attack back to their hand. Consumes 2 HP points before making the throwing attack.\nIf this action is not performed, this monster loses the weapon and all subsequent damage is reduced by 5 points (minimum 0)."},{"title":"►Charge / 8 (15) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This ability can only be used in the round in which a Normal Move is made.\nCharges and spears 1 enemy character as with melee attack, dealing 2d+16 physical damage."},{"title":"►Piercing Throw / 8(15) / Evasion / Negates","description":"When performing a [〇Thrown Attack], they can execute it as \"Range/Area: 2(20m) / Line.\" Before performing the thrown attack, consume 1d points of HP."},{"title":"⏩△Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Bear Muscle ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Gazelle Feet ], and [ Recovery (5 pts) ] Techniques.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nHeraldic Spear (150G/Black White A) |\n10 - 12 |\nWell-Balanced Spear (600G/Black White A) |\n13+ |\nWell-Kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Centaur Penetrator","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Q3x4j25dz8p5zQF2","name":"Basilisk (Monstrous Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:basilisk-monstrous-form","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Basilisk, Drakish, Youma, Arcana","habitat":"Desert, Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage + 3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"12 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 343","description":"The true identity of a Basilisk, this eight-legged beast looks like a lizard 5m long. While the Basilisk's intelligence and speed are a little lower in this form, the ability to petrify foes has increased, making the Basilisk even more dangerous.\n\nMost Basilisks feel that this form is quite ugly and hate being seen by others in this form. As such, they will almost certainly try to kill or petrify those who see this hideous form.\n\nFor the Human form of this monster, see Basilisk (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Blood/12 (19)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"It is the same as the unique skill of Basilisk (Human Form) , except for a different target number.\nEvil Eye"},{"title":"⏩ Petrifying Gaze/10 (17)/Willpower/Neg","description":"It is the same as the unique petrifaction skill of Basilisk (Human Form) , except for a different target number.\nHead"},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 7 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ].\nBody"},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Humanification","description":"It instantly transforms into Human form. Refer to Basilisk (Human Form) for data on the Human form. If the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it immediately falls unconscious.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Monstrous Form]."},{"title":"◯ Weakening","description":"When the Body section is reduced to 0 HP or fewer, the Evil Eye and Head sections of the Basilisk (Monstrous Form) receive a -2 penalty for Evasion.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBasilisk Blood (200G/Red A) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11 - 12 |\nPetrifying Eyes (1,200G/Gold Red Black S) |\n13+ |\nPetrifying Fangs (3,200G/Gold Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Basilisk (Monstrous Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"QRrZZBNDs6m7sd2A","name":"Goblin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:goblin","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":5,"weakness":10,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"11","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 397","description":"Shorter and more hunched than Humans, Goblins have green skin, short limbs, large eyes, and a large mouth.\n\nThey are small Youma that abuse anyone weaker than them, yet immediately beg for their lives when they are overmatched. They do not reflect or learn from their actions, and are quick to commit treason.\n\nThey are highly fertile and mainly work in groups. Generally goblins are not very smart, but they are resourceful. They often steal and rob to survive. They also completely lack the reflex to flee from danger.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Goblin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"QplvR1r0xQU19LDJ","name":"Glass Basilisk (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:glass-basilisk-human-form","level":12,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Basilisk, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Cold Region, Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"BM","description":"Glass Basilisks are a higher species of Basilisk possessed of glass evil eye. Their petrification gaze turns the victim into a translucent glass statue. This variant of Basilisk prefers cold climates, and bears a weakness to fire and high heat.\n\nIts second evil eye possesses the power of paralyzation, which, once seen, is difficult to escape from.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison, Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 10 Level / Magic Power 13 (20)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"Can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩Glass Gaze / 13 (20) / Willpower / Negates","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Target ,\" the Glass Basilisk gazes at a \"Target: 1 Character\", afflicting them with petrification (Dexterity / Agility -6). This effect eventually turns the target into a clear glass statue instead of a stone statue, but can be countered with [ Cure Stone ].\nIf the victim is holding a mirror is targeted with this ability, and if the Success Value of the Willpower check is 4 or more points greater than the target value, the gaze can be reflected and its effect applied to the Glass Basilisk, which does not get its own Willpower check.\nThis effect occurs even if the Glass Basilisk is blindfolded, etc. and is treated as a curse effect.\nThis ability can only be used once a round."},{"title":"⏩Paralyzing Gaze / 12 (19) / Willpower / Negates","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (50m)/Target,\" the Glass Basilisk gazes at the target, restricting its movement. If affected, the target cannot make a Full Move for 10 seconds (1 round). This also prevents special movement due to the effects of magic or items. The victim can only walk and fly using its own innate physical abilities. The ability to use the Combat Feat [ Shadow Sneak ] is also lost, along with other movement-assisting effects.\nThis ability can only be used once a round."},{"title":"◯Poisonous Blood / 13 (20) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"Anyone within the same Skirmish area who deals damage to this monster receives 2d+4 Poison magic damage at the end of their turn."},{"title":"►Monstrous Form","description":"The monster transforms into its monstrous form. For data on this form, see Glass Basilisk (Monstrous Form) . Its HP and MP are restored to their maximum values, and all effects of spells and the like are removed. When [►Monstrous Form] is activated, the new Body section is treated as if it took a Major Action. The Head section may take Major Action on this turn. Also, [Evil Left Eye] and [Evil Right Eye] sections can use their gaze abilities on their turn if the Basilisk has not already used it for its turn.\nThe ability [⏩△Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [►Monstrous Form].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBasilisk Pureblood (1000G / Red S) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nGlass Eye (2,400G / Gold Red S) |\n13+ |\nGlazed Eye (6,000G / Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Glass Basilisk (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"R9brzwU6VsZqasYK","name":"Baba Yaga","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:baba-yaga","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Varies","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"13/-","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Savage Song of Misfits p. 203","description":"Baba Yaga is a Barbarous who resembles a long-haired, humanoid female. This rare race's existence remains largely unknown to both Humanoids and other Barbarous alike.\n\nAs an all-female race, Baba Yagas must preserve their lineage by occasionally kidnapping human boys or seducing men.\n\nThrough transformation, they can temporarily increase their soulscars. During this change, their faces and skin wrinkle while their long hair whitens, giving them an elderly appearance.\n\nIn their transformed state, they reveal their true magical prowess, becoming formidable sorcerers that few dare to face.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Baba Yaga","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"RFHdtj0Yeo0rgKmj","name":"Arakcruder","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:arakcruder","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Aviary, Barbaric","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":12,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"10/30(Flying)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 13)","source":"CR III p. 330","description":"Arakcruders are a type of Barbarous with their entire body is covered with feathers, and heads resembles a bird of prey. It has a pair of large wings growing from their arms. It is about 2 meters tall, but its wing span is twice that when flying. Although their ability to manipulate objects with their hands has degenerated significantly, they can use their legs like hands while flying, and they mainly live in this way. When they have no choice but to walk, they walk upright.\n\nThey are territorial and live in groups, building primitive dwellings in caves, cliffs, or on the tops of large trees, often using floating rocks (see CR I, p. 341) as their strongholds. Although belligerent and ferocious, they revere Garuda (see p. 97) as the King of the Flying Barbarous, and many serve them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"This monster receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Spear Pursuit","description":"A monster's spear can be used as a melee attack against an opponent who has been attacked with a beak.\nAccuracy check and damage are the same as those of the beak. This effect is effective only when the monster is Flying.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 9 |\nBeautiful Feathers (30G/Gold Red B) |\n10+ |\nSeven-colored Feather (200G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Arakcruder","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"RynIbIyUE5hwleML","name":"Highland Hugl","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:highland-hugl","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Lizardman","habitat":"Mountains, Cold Climates","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Wind-type +3 damage","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15/20(Flight)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"GR, Battle Mastery p. 109","description":"A subspecies of Hugl that dwells in tall, snow-capped mountains and colder regions. Perhaps as part of adapting to the environment, it has grown larger than other Hugls, and its scales have become as white as powdered snow.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Wintry Adaptation","description":"Receives no penalties for poor footing due to snow, ice, etc."},{"title":"⏩ △ Mobile Flying","description":"It gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns. When used in Combat Preparation, it cannot be used in the first round, regardless of the result of the Initiative check."},{"title":"◯ Winged Pursuit","description":"If it hits with a Claw attack, it can make an additional melee attack with wings. Accuracy bonus, damage, and other values are the same as for the claw attack.\nThis ability cannot be used on the same turn in which [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying]\nis used. Also, once an additional attack is made with this ability, [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying] cannot be used on that turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nSnow-hued Scales (30G / Red B) |\n5 - 8 |\nWhite Scales (90G / Red B) x 1d |\n9+ |\nRainbow Hued Scales (220G / Gold Red A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Highland Hugl","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SPVBo7WpS4ytehWl","name":"Shield Hoodling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shield-hoodling","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Various","reputation":8,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 400","description":"This Hoodling Youma holds a shield large enough to conceal itself. Although they can attack by slamming with their large shield, their main role is to cover their Barbarous superiors when they are exposed to attack.\n\nThis shield is a sign of strength and self-discipline, but often makes them overconfident.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨 △ Cover I","description":"This effect is the same as the combat feat [ Cover I ] (see CR I, p. 255).\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCrude Shield (50G/Green White B) |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 10 |\nDirty Hood (20G/White B) |\n11+ |\nWorn Hood (80G/White B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shield Hoodling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SQXMIjNsZfmFYK00","name":"Diablo Cadet (Daemon Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:diablo-cadet-daemon-form","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Daemonic","habitat":"Wasteland, Shallow","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Energy type damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"20/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR I p. 405","description":"This is a giant Diablo Cadet . Its form is reminiscent of a Daemon, and it is more powerful for it. It symbolizes awe for both the Humanoid and the Barbarous and is the cause of why Diablos are feared. The fear is also heightened by the giant Diablo becoming more aggressive and brutal.\n\nHowever, after taking this form and releasing it, they cannot Daemonshift again for some time.\n\nFor the Human form of this monster, see Diablo Cadet (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Tough Skin","description":"Whenever it receives physical or magical damage of the bludgeoning type, it is reduced by -3 points.\nHead"},{"title":"► Daemonic Eyes/Can't","description":"With a sharp look in its eyes, it shrivels enemies.\nWith \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Target \", select any number of targets and deal each of them 2 curse magic damage. Afterward, Diablo's HP is restored by the sum of all applied damage dealt to the targets.\nUsing this ability consumes 2 points of MP per character targeted."},{"title":"► Chain of Curses/8 (15)/Willpower/Half","description":"Diablo injures themselves to curse an enemy.\nThey can select an arbitrary number of targets with \"Range: 1 (10m)\" and \"Area: Target \" and deal each of them 2d+6 curse magic damage.\nTo use this ability, 8 points of HP and 4 points of MP per number of targets must be consumed (HP consumption is always 8 points, regardless of the number of targets).\nBody\nAll sections receive a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf the Body section falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters within reach with melee attacks, but the damage will be reduced by -3. If more than one is hit, the damage is determined individually."},{"title":"► Humanification","description":"It changes into its Human form. For data on the Human form, refer to Diablo Cadet (Human Form) . If the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0 after this transfer, it immediately falls unconscious.\n[ ► Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after [ ► Daemonshift] was used. Also, [ ► Daemonshift] cannot be used for 3 hours immediately after the [ ► Humanification] was used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G) x 1d |\n2 - 5 |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) |\n6 - 9 |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) x 2 |\n10+ |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Diablo Cadet (Daemon Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"SyBFBunIX5NH65ia","name":"Dowi Fomor","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dowi-fomor","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Giant","habitat":"Various","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"21/-","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"BM","description":"This is a more experienced Fomor Giant .\n\nNormally, they lead Goblins or Bolg under a higher-ranking Drake or Troll . However, most of the assignments they are given are highly dangerous, such as spearheading a siege or leading a retreat.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Chain Attack","description":"After an attack, Dowi Fomor can attack the same target again, regardless of its success or failure. This ability can add only one additional attack per round."},{"title":"◯ Counter","description":"Identical to the Combat Feat [ Counter ].\nUpper Body"},{"title":"⏩ △ Technique &amp; ◯ Muscle Mystery","description":"Can use [ Cat's Eye ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Bear Muscle ], [ Giant Arms ], and [ Recovery (7 points) ]. These Techniques have twice the normal duration."},{"title":"⏩ Stratagem and Maneuver/All Areas (30m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Surging Offense III: True Aim ] (Accuracy +1, Physical Damage +1).\nEvery third turn, they can use [ Maneuver: Unexpected Blow I ] (+2 Accuracy, +2 Damage). Cannot use Stratagems if no other allies will be affected it.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Fomor's height prevents enemies from attacking it.\nThe Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nBag of Silver (50G) x 1d |\n7 - 10 |\nBag of Silver (100G) x 2d |\n11+ |\nBag of Silver (300G) x 2d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dowi Fomor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"U91XmRqzxgZrz03D","name":"Lizardman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lizardman","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Lizardman, Dragonic","habitat":"Swamps","reputation":11,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"13/13 (Swimming)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR II p. 334","description":"Lizardmen are one of the more aquatically inclined Barbarous, preferring to spend time in swamps and other wetlands worshiping their dragon gods. Standing just shy of 2 meters tall, they look like upright lizards, though they take offense if mistaken for Lildraken .\n\nWhile they cannot breathe underwater, like Elves , Lizardmen can hold their breath for up to an hour and similarly have houses with dry and wet sections.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Tail Sweep","description":"The monster can use its tail to attack up to 5 targets in the same skirmish. An Accuracy check is made on all characters at once, and damage is determined individually.\nThis attack cannot be used in consecutive rounds.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nSeven-color Scales (220G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lizardman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"UERBqLM32tinCw9O","name":"Onyx Basilisk (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:onyx-basilisk-human-form","level":13,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric,","habitat":"Desert, Ruins","reputation":11,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 335","description":"The Onyx Basilisk is a higher-level of Basilisk with an evil onyx eye. The petrification curse this Basilisk gives turns the victim into a black agate (onyx).\n\nThis monster also has an evil eye of stagnation as its second evil eye.\n\nThe transformed Onyx Basilisk is a large lizard over 5 meters in length, and its right and left evil eyes to shine in milky white and black. Unlike the rational Human form, Onyx Basilisk in this form moves with its emotions and lays waste to the beings in front of it.\n\nFor the Monstrous form of this monster, see Onyx Basilisk (Monstrous Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 12 Level/Magic Power 16 (23)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩ Onyx Gaze/15 (22)/Willpower/Neg","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Target \", it stares at \"Target: 1 Character\" and petrifies the target (Dexterity, Agility-6) (see CR II, p. 329). Under this effect, the target eventually turns into an onyx statue instead of a stone statue. It is possible to cancel the effect with [ Cure Stone ].\nIf the target of this unique skill is the one who holds the mirror, and if Willpower's success value is 4 or more points higher than the Target Number, gaze can bounce off the, giving this effect to Onyx Basilisk always affecting them without a check even if Onyx Basilisk is blindfolded. This unique skill is of curse type.\nThis unique skill can be used only once per round."},{"title":"► Stagnation Gaze/14 (21)/Willpower/Neg","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Target \", the monster stares at \"Target: 1 Character\" and prevents its movement. Target cannot take any Major Action and any Minor Action for 10 seconds (1 round). However, if the target can take multiple Major Actions, the number of Major Actions is reduced by only one (still no Minor Action can be taken)."},{"title":"◯ Poison Blood/16 (23)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"Anyone who deals damage to this monster in the same skirmish will receive 2d+6 poison magic damage at the end of their turn."},{"title":"► Monstrous Form","description":"The monster transforms into its monstrous form. For data on the monstrous form, see Onyx Basilisk (Monstrous Form) . HP and MP are restored to their maximum values, and all effects of spells and the like are removed. When [ ► Monstrous Form] is activated, only the Body section is treated as if it made a Major Action; the Head and Evil Eyes sections may still take a Major Action on this turn.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Monstrous Form].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBasilisk Pureblood (1,000G/Red S) |\n2 - 5 |\nNothing |\n6 - 11 |\nOnyx Eye (4,000G/Gold Red S) |\n12+ |\nEye of Stagnation (10,000G/Gold Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Onyx Basilisk (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"UZ91hpHda5IiQN0n","name":"Formica Lord","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:formica-lord","level":11,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Formica","habitat":"Deserts, Ruins","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Barbarous Tales (2.0 sourcebook), p. 52","description":"This is the king of the Formica tribe. He is the largest of the Formica, has better intellect than the others, and can even negotiate for the tribe. However, he is still emotionless and thinks rationally. They are also strong believers of Dalkhrem, the God of War, and are powerful priests. They are the leaders of the entire tribe, and their subordinates absolutely obey the orders of the Formica Lord, even if they are suicidal.\n\nThe Formica Lord's greatest love is the Formica Queen , and the highest priority for them is to increase the number of the entire tribe. If the Queen is harmed or killed, he will likely fly into a rage and attack everyone. If the Queen is taken hostage, he may be willing to negotiate if it is the last Queen in the tribe.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 8 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"A Formica Lord can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"►Formic Acid / 13 (20) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"A Formica can spit acid at an enemy character in the same skirmish, dealing 2d+12 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"◯Shared Senses","description":"If there is another Formica (of any type) in the skirmish this monster is in, it gains a +2 bonus to all of its Accuracy checks. This effect is not cumulative.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSuperior Shell (750G/Red A) |\nAlways |\nGlittering Feathers (340G/Gold Red A) x 2 |\n2 - 8 |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) x 2 |\n9+ |\nWell-kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Formica Lord","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"UaBxM6HLvGgMcK2s","name":"Tannoz Cleric","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tannoz-cleric","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Sylvan","habitat":"Coast, Riverside","reputation":14,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15/15 (Swimming)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 344","description":"They are the leader of the Tannoz , who use Divine Magic in addition to Fairy Magic. Tannoz generally follow Sea Snatcher Eiryak , whose teachings Tannoz Clerics preach to their companions. Clerics prefer to summon fairies and support allies with Divine Magic.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Divine Magic 9 Level &amp; Fairy Magic 9 Level/Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"It can use Earth, Water/Ice, Wind, and Dark Fairy Magic types."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], and [ Metamagic/Targets ].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nDangerous Pincers (570G/Red A) |\n9 - 11 |\nDeadly Pincers (1,660G/Red S) |\n12+ |\nVeteran Pincers (4,400G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tannoz Cleric","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"UkpNmcJjhSj3t5ms","name":"Scissorscorpion","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:scissorscorpion","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Androscorpion, Magitech","habitat":"Desert, Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"17 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 338","description":"A warrior branch of the Androscorpions , Scissorscorpions have often seen leading groups in sorties or at the head of a squadron of Androscorpions in emergencies. As the name suggests, Scissorscorpions have a pair of large pincers that can cut through enemies like scissors through paper.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Magitech 5 Level/Magic Power 7 (14)","description":""},{"title":"► Gunfire/7 (14)/Evasion/Neg","description":"A Scissorscorpion can attack with a readied gun, whose Max. Magazine is 4, the range is 2 (30m), and the Critical Threshold is 10."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Poison/8 (15)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"If the Scissorscorpion's Lower Body hits with their Tail attack, the target will receive an extra 8 poison-type damage."},{"title":"◯ Weakening","description":"When the Lower Body section is reduced to 0 HP or fewer, the Upper Body and Pincers sections of the Scissorscorpion receive a -2 penalty for Evasion.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nScorpion Shell (50G/Red B) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 10 |\nPoison Stinger with Intact Poison Sac (800G/Red A) |\n11+ |\nPoison Stinger with Deadly Poison Sac (1,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Scissorscorpion","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VL03vSv7r6Rv4752","name":"Deep Gremlin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:deep-gremlin","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":1,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Plateaus, Mountains","reputation":8,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Wind-type damage +3","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10/18 (Flying)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"BM","description":"A variant of Gremlin , these Barbarous Youma have strikingly purple skin. They are also a bit larger than their kin, ending up roughly the size of a human child.\n\nDeep Gremlins are also much more brutally cunning, going above and beyond what would normally be considered harmless pranks. For example, a Deep Gremlin \"prank\" will see them kill some livestock, [ Disguise ] itself as one of the dying animals, and call out to human children in order to scare and terrify them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 4 Level/Magic Power 6 (13)","description":""},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Deep Gremlin receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 10 |\nStrange Necklace (160G/White A) |\n11+ |\nBeautiful Necklace (300G/Gold White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Deep Gremlin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VkwwWgqfJcPPlIK9","name":"Murcielago Latigo","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:murcielago-latigo","level":15,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Nosferatu, Arcana","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":23,"weakness":26,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":22,"movementSpeed":"25/25(Flying)","fortitude":"19 (26)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 102","description":"Among the Murcielago , Latigo vampires are especially favored by Nosferatu . While Murcielagos excel at seducing and cajoling Humanoids, Latigo vampires are known to be equally skilled and even better fighters.\n\nThey educate and direct the regular Murcielagos, serving as a Nosferatu's close associates and personal guards, protecting them with their lives. They also boast of their overwhelming good looks and sometimes use them to discredit superior heroes in humanoid society or even to seduce and take them as their own servants.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Murcielago receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Swords of Protection Resistance","description":"If the Murcielago is within the influence of Swords of Protection, the Murcielago's soulscars are treated as 2 points lower than it originally was."},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 15 Level/Magic Power 19 (26)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +19 damage","description":"May deal an additional +19 damage to their next melee attack. At risk, they take a -2 penalty to their Fortitude and Willpower checks."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides."},{"title":"► Bonds of Love and Blood/18 (25)/Willpower/Neg","description":"The same ability as of a Murcielago ."},{"title":"⏩ △ Bat Shapeshifting","description":"Murcielago changes its own appearance into a bat about 20 cm in length. Or, it returns to its original form from the state of being a bat.\nWhen in the form of a bat, the physical abilities of the bat will be equivalent to its appearance (enough to fly as a bat), and all unique skills will be ineffective. Also, the bat form is not treated as a character and is not a target of any effect. If the character is changed during a battle, it can leave the battlefield.\nThis ability can be used only once per hour, and unless this ability is used, the shape never changes.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nThe Lustrous Blood of Murcielago (2,000G/Red S) x 1d |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7+ |\nBlood Family Directives (5,000G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Murcielago Latigo","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VqCiMQYCVeU2dVDv","name":"Lesser Vampire","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lesser-vampire","level":11,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Nosferatu, Regional Dialect, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Silver weapon damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"18/36 (Flying)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR II p. 353","description":"Immortalized by a Blood Kiss from an older Nosferatu , Lesser Vampires are incredibly powerful, even among the Barbarous. Often, they are followers of Zeides who were once Humans that have fallen into the good graces of other vampires and left their humanity behind. Despite this, they are often stunning, and even their gaze can paralyze and fascinate lesser creatures.\n\nLesser Vampires must still drink blood daily to keep themselves at peak performance. The actual source of the blood can be any living being, but often, they will prey upon beautiful members of the opposite gender. Occasionally, they will even starve themselves to fit into society and get closer to their desired target, making the drinking all sweeter. Care has to be taken, however, as it is effortless to drain a target entirely and raise them as a subordinate Blood Sucker , and often a Lesser Vampire has a small retinue of followers.\n\nDespite their powers, sunlight is the bane of the Lesser Vampire, reducing them to ash in a small amount of time. After only a few minutes outside during the day, all that will be left of the Lesser Vampire is a pile of ashes and possibly some clothing. Because of this, Lesser Vampires will be reluctant to move out of their roost during daylight hours.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 10 Level / Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 8 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":""},{"title":"⏩ Gaze/13 (20)/Willpower/Negates","description":"A Lesser Vampire may attempt to paralyze with \"Range/Area: 50m/Target\". If the target fails to resist the Gaze, they are paralyzed for 10 seconds (1 round), cannot take any Minor Actions, and may not use active combat feats. If the target's resistance roll is 16 or less, the target is instead charmed by the Lesser Vampire and will move to aid and defend it for the next minute (6 rounds). This effect is treated as a Psychic type.\nThis ability can be used only once per round."},{"title":"► Vampire Bite/13 (20)/Evasion/Neg","description":"The Lesser Vampire bites the target, dealing 2d+10 physical damage. The Lesser Vampire heals HP equal to the applied dealt.\nIf the target is reduced to 0 HP or lower from this attack, they receive a -10 penalty to their next Death Check. If the character fails this Death Check, they receive an extra 5 soulscars and rise as a Blood Sucker .\nLesser Vampires lose 6 HP and MP per day (cumulative) that they do not drain blood via [ ► Vampire Bite] and also cannot use their [ ◯ Regeneration] unique skill. These penalties immediately disappear once the Lesser Vampire successfully drains blood via [ ► Vampire Bite]."},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 7 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Lesser Vampire recovers 7 HP. This does not affect the Lesser Vampire at 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Vampire Body","description":"As long as a Lesser Vampire is under sunlight, it takes 7 magic damage at the end of its turn and receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks. This damage cannot be reduced in any way. Additionally, the Lesser Vampire cannot use their [ ◯ Regeneration] or [ ◯ Normal Weapon Immunity] abilities."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Lesser Vampire receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCorrupted Ash (300G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nVampire Cloak (1,000G/White S) |\n13+ |\nJet-Black Cloak (5,000G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lesser Vampire","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VuQGqhbwsLkGQPhf","name":"Garuda","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:garuda","level":12,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Aviary","habitat":"Mountain","reputation":14,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning damage +3","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"25/50 (Flying)","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"CR II p. 354","description":"A 3m tall Barbarous with a bird-like head and large wings on their back, Garudas are masters of the winds.\n\nThey are known as \"Sky Kings\" among the lower ranks of the Barbarous, and with good reason. They despise any others flying in what they consider their airspace and will often go out alone to drive out or kill the interlopers.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack II","description":"If a Garuda successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack. They can make a third attack against the same target if a second attack hits."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"A Garuda can use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Bear Muscle ], and [ Beetleskin ] Techniques.\nBody"},{"title":"⏩ Turbulent Winds/15 (22)/Fortitude/Half","description":"It creates turbulence in a 6m/20 radius around itself, dealing 2d+12 Wind magic damage to the targets and causing them to fall prone .\nThis unique skill can be used only once per turn, at the end of each turn."},{"title":"► Wind-Edge Blade/15 (22)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (30m)/ Target \", the Garuda uses a blade made of feathers to deal 2d+15 Slashing magic damage."},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"All sections receive a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks. This unique skill is lost if the Body section is reduced to 0 or less HP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nNothing |\n6 - 11 |\nLarge Feathers (200G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nWind-Edge Feathers (3,500G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Garuda","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"VwIEYyKgnT4EpCLW","name":"Hugl","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hugl","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":1,"languages":"Lizardman, Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Desert, Mountain","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"10/15 (Flying)","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 399","description":"This Youma has a lizard-like face, brown scales, and a long tail. It has large, strong, leathery wings on its back and can fly.\n\nAlthough smaller in stature than Humans, they are strong enough to grab a Human child or goat and fly away.\n\nThe Hugl can attack simultaneously with sharp claws on both arms and wings on their back. However, it is not good at flying and fighting simultaneously.\n\nHugls live in family units on rocky mountains, but are often seen accompanying other Barbarous as bouncers.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ △ Mobile Flying","description":"The Hugl gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns. When used in Combat Preparation, it cannot be used in the first round, regardless of the result of the Initiative check."},{"title":"◯ Winged Pursuit","description":"If it hits with a Claw attack, it can make an additional melee attack with wings. Accuracy bonus, damage, and other values are the same as for the claw attack.\nThis ability cannot be used on the same turn in which [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying] is used. Also, once an additional attack is made with this ability, [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying] cannot be used on that turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nEarth-toned Scales (30G/Red B) |\n10+ |\nAmber Scales (90G/Red B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hugl","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WH20ivRNEmV4OfeK","name":"Kobold Marksman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kobold-marksman","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":1,"languages":"Trade common, Barbaric, Youma, Magitech","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":7,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12/-","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"BM","description":"This is a Kobold Youma who has the Artificer class and can attack at long range with their dexterity.\n\nOn the other hand, they are extremely bad at hand-to-hand combat, so once they get caught up in a melee, they can be easily defeated by even a newbie adventurer. As a Barbarous gunslinger, they are often slaves of Androscorpions .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Magitech 1 Level/Magic Power 2 (9)","description":""},{"title":"► Gunfire / 3 (10) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The max magazine is 2 with Range: 2 (20m)."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCrude Weapon (10G/Black White B) |\n2 - 7 |\nNone |\n8+ |\nBag of Silver (30G/-) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kobold Marksman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WTtJDXfgq7hj9MBQ","name":"Lizardman Mariner","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lizardman-mariner","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Barbaric, Lizardman, Dragonic","habitat":"Swamps, Wetlands","reputation":12,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"14/14 (Swimming)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 85","description":"These are members of an elite group of Lizardmen trained to rush into enemy territory and create openings for other Barbarous from within. In the past, there was concern that these elite Lizardmen could take down cities under united leadership. Today, they are rarely seen.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯ Coordination","description":"A Lizardman Mariner gains a bonus to their Accuracy equal to the number of other Lizardman Mariners in the same skirmish, up to a maximum of +4."},{"title":"◯ Rage","description":"When another Lizardman (regardless of type) in the same skirmish is defeated, the Lizardman Mariner gains a cumulative +2 bonus to damage for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThe GM decides when a Lizardman is defeated (so it cannot recover).\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nNothing |\n10+ |\nSilver Medal (700G/Gold A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lizardman Mariner","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"WgmgLAzNzwvuYeTi","name":"Glasell","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:glasell","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Daemonic","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":13,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"AB, p. 89","description":"These are Barbarous with a stocky build, carrying a large shell on their backs. Their body type resembles that of a stout Human, with a reptilian face like a scaled frog, and they can freely extend a flexible tongue from their mouth which they use as a weapon. While they sometimes carry weapons in their short arms, they don't seem particularly skilled in handling them compared to other Barbarous.\n\nThey inhabit mines and mineral deposits where rare ores can be found, and have a habit of coating these with oil secreted from their shell, then licking and polishing them. There are rumors that this process can cause the ores to mutate into rarer varieties, but this hasn't been confirmed.\n\nThey have been spotted living around the Abyss Core within Shallow Abysses, where they've been observed licking and polishing it.\n\nWhen fighting alongside Daemons who guard the Abyss Core, they sometimes lick their wounds to heal them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Shell Deflection / 7 (14) / Adventurer Level+Dexterity Modifier / Negates","description":"Using the shell on its back for defense, this ability deflects enemy weapons.\nWhen this monster receives a melee attack and successfully evades by having the attacker's Accuracy check result equal to the Evasion check result, the attacker must make a check against this ability. On a failure, they drop the weapon used for the attack.\nThis effect does not apply to ranged attacks, innate weapons, or melee attacks made with weapons that enhance Punches or Kicks."},{"title":"►Oil Application","description":"Using its long tongue at \"Range: Touch,\" it applies healing oil from its shell to 1 target character other than itself. The target recovers 2d HP points. Using this ability consumes 5 points of both HP and MP."},{"title":"◯Magical Attunement","description":"When this monster receives physical damage or magical damage of \"Fire\", \"Water/Ice\", \"Wind\", \"Earth\", or \"Lightning\" type, for the next 10 seconds (1 round), this monster's tongue attacks become imbued with magic power and change to that type, increasing damage by +2 points.\nThe type granted by this effect is updated each time the monster receives physical damage or magical damage of the corresponding type (the values do not stack).\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 11 |\nShell Oil (250G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nHigh Viscosity Oil (720G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Glasell","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YPziyzb0tkZeZXRP","name":"Zeanemo Rider","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zeanemo-rider","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Elven","habitat":"Seas","reputation":16,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"16 (4 legs) / 20 (swimming)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 119","description":"These Zeanemo have tamed the Coast Lizards and are now running wild on their back.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯ Dismounting","description":"This monster's Rider section is mounted on the Lizard section. If the Rider is dismounted, all sections suffer a -2 penalty on all Skill Checks and have their damage reduced by -2 points.\nSee the Rider class and the Riding Rules (see CR III, p. 87) for rules for this monster on how to dismount and mount back at the mount.\nThe movement speed of the Rider section does not change even when it is unmounted."},{"title":"►Trample","description":"Makes a melee attack against a target within Range/Area: 1 (20m) / Breakthrough . This melee attack can be done by any section of this monster.\nAfter using this ability, all sections have completed their Major Action. This ability cannot be used when the HP of the Lizard section is 0 or less or [◯Dismounting] occurs.\nRider"},{"title":"🗨Cleave I","description":"It makes a Weapon attack against up to 3 characters within the skirmish in which it resides, dealing -3 less damage to each."},{"title":"⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles / 11 (18) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This ability may only be used once per turn, just before a Major Action. Within \"Range: Touch\" it is used to entangle \"Target: 1 Character\" with the tentacles within their right eye. If the target fails the Evasion check, the following two effects occur:\n- If the monster makes a melee attack against its target immediately afterward, the target's Evasion check is decreased by -2. This effect only applies to that single Evasion check (the tentacles automatically release after the melee attack).\n- The target must perform a Fortitude Check with Target Number 16. If the target fails, it is paralyzed for the next 1 minute (6 rounds) and suffers a -1 penalty on Accuracy checks. This effect is Poison type and does not accumulate."},{"title":"◯Behind the Right Eye","description":"The character who became the target of the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles] can declare that they will \"aim at the right eye\" when making a weapon attack against this monster on their turn (regardless of whether the Evasion check was successful or not against the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles]). If the declared attack hits, its physical and/or magic damage is increased by 4 points.\nIf this action is taken and the increase in damage actually occurs, PCs will no longer receive the loot \"Strange Red Eye\" from the targeted monster.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nStrange Red Eye (800G/Red A) |\n2 - 8 |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |\n9+ |\nWell-Kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zeanemo Rider","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YdvX59TF9G2GWmri","name":"Volticfist","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:volticfist","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Barren lands, Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Slashing type damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 87","description":"Among the Rumblefists , there are individuals who have undergone a special ritual that allows them to control lightning. These individuals have a black horn on the top of their heads, which they can use to summon lightning. This ability is only demonstrated in the heat of battle. By channeling the lightning through their bodies, they are able to attack with lightning-charged fists.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Lightning Immunity, Bludgeoning Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Elastic Skin","description":"Against bludgeoning weapons, its Defense is treated as 3 points higher."},{"title":"◯ Charged Fist","description":"Fists fill lightning, increasing its striking power.\nIf the Volticfist is the target of a lightning-type effect, their fists become hard and treated as magic weapons (though still dealing physical damage), increasing physical damage by +2 points over 3 minutes (18 rounds). This effect is cumulative up to 3 times (+6 total)."},{"title":"► Thunder Scream/10 (17)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"The Volticfist shouts to the heavens and drop bolts of lightning around themselves.\nUp to 2 random creatures (including itself) in the melee area where it is located are hit by this effect and are dealt 2d+8 lightning magic damage.\nThis effect can be used while in melee, and it costs 6 MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nThunder Horn (2,100G/Red Black S) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 11 |\nWater-repellent Skin (330G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nGlossy Skin (1,720G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Volticfist","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"YwSKKG5vl6P74jxo","name":"Daemonic Barbaroi: Minotaur Grunel","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:daemonic-barbaroi","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Minotaur, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Wilderness, Labyrinths, Shallow Abysses","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla , p. 124","description":"Daemonic Barbaroi are threats that primarily appear in the border regions of Zamsaska territory, possessing forms and abilities that can be described as a fusion of Barbarous and Daemon. It is said that they are either Barbarous who became tainted by the Abyss in their pursuit of power or those whose souls were taken over through Daemon manipulation.\n\nHere, we introduce a combination of Minotaur and Grunel , but GMs can create their own \"Daemonic Barbaroi\" by combining other creatures.\n\nHere are the guidelines:\n\nChoose Barbarous and Daemon with similar monster levels (too large of a level difference diminishes the purpose of fusion).\n\nThe monster level should be higher than the two +1.\n\nWeak point can be chosen from either creature.\n\nFor various stats, choose the higher value from each (\"cherry-pick\"). Reputation gets an additional +1 (weaknesses remain unchanged). This applies to Intellect and Perception as well.\n\nRetain all unique skills from both creatures, including languages. Add \"Dual Classification\" to their unique skills.\n\nAdjust movement and loot while maintaining elements from both creatures.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Divine Magic 7 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"⏩△Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Bear Muscle ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Gazelle Feet ], and [ Recovery (5 pts.) ] Techniques."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ]."},{"title":"🗨Sweeping Strike I","description":"Choose up to 3 characters capable of melee attacks and perform melee attacks against them. Damage is reduced by -3 points."},{"title":"🗨Power Strike I","description":"Increases damage by +4 points. As a risk, apply a -2 penalty to its own Evasion check."},{"title":"🗨Mana Strike = +10 damage","description":"Deals +10 points of damage. As a risk, apply a -2 penalty modifier to its own Fortitude and Willpower checks.\nTail"},{"title":"◯Entangling Tentacles","description":"When a Tail attack hits, it entangles the target with entangling tentacles. The target becomes immobilized and receives a -2 penalty to Accuracy and Evasion checks. From the next turn, attacks from that Tail section automatically hit the target. Even if affected by multiple entangling tentacles simultaneously, the penalty modifiers do not stack.\nWhen the target tries to escape, use de-bonding rules.\nWhile entangling a target with this ability, the Tail section cannot attack other characters. If this monster wishes to release the target, it can do so automatically as a Minor Action.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nDaemon's Blood (100G/Red A) |\nAlways |\nMinotaur's Axe (475G/Black White A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 9 |\nLarge Decorated Horn (410G/Gold Red White A) |\n10+ |\nBeautiful Decorated Horn (1,800G/Gold Red White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Daemonic Barbaroi: Minotaur Grunel","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"Z12h50IvsZHPnhaI","name":"Cryodilcobraz","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cryodilcobraz","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Cold Regions","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 120","description":"With a large body that stands out from the rest of the Cryoblaz , these are the ultimate guardians, protecting their allies with their huge bodies.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"🗨△Cover II &amp; Guardian I","description":"This is the same effect as the Combat Feat [ Cover II ]. Multiple targets can be selected at the time of declaration, and [Cover] can be executed up to 3 times per declaration."},{"title":"🗨Decoy Attack I","description":"It gains -2 to Accuracy checks, but the damage is increased by +2 on hit.\nIf the declared attack is evaded, the enemy receives a -1 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative up to -4 but is lost if the target fails an Evasion check even once."},{"title":"⏩Freezing Stance II","description":"This effect lasts for 10 seconds (1 round), does not accumulate, and consumes 5 MP when used.\nDamage caused by weapon attack becomes Water/Ice type and increases by +2. If a Cryodilcobraz is hit by a melee attack, the attacker will be dealt an additional 2 Water/Ice fixed damage regardless of the success or failure of the melee attack.\nThis effect ends immediately after the Cryodilcobraz receives 1 or more points of Fire-type applied damage without waiting 10 seconds (1 round). If it is caused by a melee attack, the effect disappears first, and the attacker will not be dealt fixed damage."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"6 - 10","loot":"|"},{"roll":"11+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cryodilcobraz","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"aCapgH72xcDCFHb8","name":"Fomor","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:fomor","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Giantish","habitat":"Various","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"18/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"BM","description":"A green-skinned race of Giants that stand approximately 5 meters tall, the Fomor are said to be a noble race of Barbarous who once led Goblins , Bolgs and Ogres in battle. However, they were deprived of their positions by the plotting of Drakes and now possess low status.\n\nFomors are said to be the bravest of the Barbarous, always taking the lead in battles. In this sense, they get along with Trolls . However, where a Troll tends to be guided only by its own strength as a warrior, Fomors excel at commanding troops. It has even been said that \"a Goblin army led by a Fomor will defeat a Troll army led by a Goblin.\"\n\nThe Drakes, who now occupy the upper echelons of Barbarous society, highly value the abilities of the Fomors but are wary of conspiracy of rebellion amongst them. For this reason, Fomors are not allowed to assemble in groups larger than a family unit, and their children are forced into independence at an early age to be incorporated into Barbarous armies.\n\nIn such armies, they are often given command and staff positions in small units composed of Goblins, Bolgs, and other Barbarous. Several Fomors do not usually appear together in these units.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Chain Attack","description":"After an attack, Fomor can attack the same target again, regardless of its success or failure. This ability can add only one additional attack per round."},{"title":"◯ Counter","description":"Identical effect as the Combat Feat [ Counter ].\nUpper Body"},{"title":"⏩ △ Technique &amp; ◯ Muscle Mystery","description":"Can use [ Cat's Eye ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Bear Muscle ], and [ Recovery (7 points) ]. These Techniques have twice the normal duration."},{"title":"⏩ Stratagem and Maneuver/All Areas (20m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Surging Offense II: Whirlwind ] (Accuracy +1). Every third turn, they can use [ Maneuver: Unexpected Blow I ] (+2 Accuracy, +2 Damage). This monster cannot use Stratagems if no other allies will be affected.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Fomor height prevents enemies from attacking it.\nThe Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nBag of Silver (50G / -) x 1d |\n7 - 10 |\nBag of Silver (100G / -) x 1d |\n11+ |\nRare Gems (1500G / Gold S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Fomor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"aIDgRvqHHl0HbLiI","name":"Manozalyu","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:manozalyu","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forest, Meadow","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14/-","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"BM","description":"A superior species of Manogaryu known for subjugating numerous beasts and presenting them to high ranking Barbarous. Identical to Manogaryu in size, their skin is instead a dark green.\n\nThey possess greater skill at handling whips, but their intelligence is still low, and thus their status in Barbarous society is not much improved.\n\nThere is no skill or technique to their beast taming, as it seems to stem from intuition. As such, it is unique to each individual and cannot be taught to others.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Double Attack","description":"A Manozalyu can make two Whip attacks against the same target."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"◯ Subjugation","description":"Adds +1 bonus to Accuracy/Evasion versus Animals and Mythical Beasts."},{"title":"🗨 Whip Feint","description":"Deliberately leaves an opening in its attack to bait the opponent into evading. This has the same effect as [ Decoy Attack I ]."},{"title":"🗨 Vital Aim","description":"Aims the whip for a weak point and attacks. If the Accuracy Check roll result is 9 or greater, +5 damage is added to the attack. As a risk, the Manozalyu receives a -2 penalty to its attack.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nDance Costume (100G / Red A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 11 |\nFlexible Whip (140G / Red A) |\n12+ |\nBeast Tamer's Whip (660G / Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Manozalyu","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"aMB5rL9GDjrYK9Ag","name":"Glasell Violet","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:glasell-violet","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Daemonic","habitat":"Ruins, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Bludgeoning type damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"AB, p. 90","description":"These are Glasells whose entire bodies and shells have turned purple. It is said that those who have dwelled in the Shallows for long periods undergo this discoloration.\n\nThe discolored ones are said to have adapted to the Shallow environment, increasing their threat. They are also known to have a symbiotic relationship with the Daemons that protect the Shallow, sometimes working together to achieve common goals.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Purple Shell Deflection / 9 (16) / Adventurer Level+Dexterity Modifier / Negates","description":"Using the shell on its back for defense, this ability deflects enemy weapons.\nWhen this monster receives a melee attack and successfully evades by having the attacker's Accuracy check result equal to the Evasion check result, the attacker must make a check against this ability. On a failure, they drop the weapon used for the attack.\nThis effect does not apply to ranged attacks, innate weapons, or melee attacks made with weapons that enhance Punches or Kicks.\nIn Shallows or similar environments, when this ability activates, it first deals 1d points of fixed damage to the attacker before attempting the weapon drop check."},{"title":"►Oil Application","description":"Using its long tongue at \"Range: Touch,\" it applies healing oil from its shell to 1 target character other than itself. The target recovers 2d+4 HP points. Using this ability consumes 7 points of both HP and MP."},{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Glasell Violet can make two Tongue attacks each round, though each attack requires its Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯Magical Attunement","description":"When this monster receives physical damage or magical damage of \"Fire\", \"Water/Ice\", \"Wind\", \"Earth\", or \"Lightning\" type, for the next 10 seconds (1 round), this monster's tongue attacks become imbued with magic power and change to that type, gaining a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks and increasing damage by +4 points.\nThe type granted by this effect is updated each time the monster receives physical damage or magical damage of the corresponding type (the values do not stack).\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nShell Oil (250G/Red A) |\n8 - 10 |\nHigh Viscosity Oil (720G/Red A) |\n11+ |\nGlittering Oil (2,400G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Glasell Violet","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"aQgPQ5cbdTyvirup","name":"Androscorpion","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:androscorpion","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Androscorpion, Magitech","habitat":"Desert, Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15 (Many Legs)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 335","description":"These odd Barbarous have a humanoid upper body growing out of the lower body of a giant scorpion.\n\nLiving in deserts and around ruins, Androscorpions are reasonably capable Artificers in their own right. They will often be seen carrying and wearing the various spoils of their expeditions, whether armor, weapons, or strong magical artifacts.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Magitech 4 Level / Magic Power 6 (13)","description":""},{"title":"► Gunfire/6 (13)/Evasion/Neg","description":"An Androscorpion can attack with a readied gun, whose Max. Magazine is 4, range is 2 (20m), and Critical Threshold is 10."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Poison/5 (12)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"If the Androscorpion's Lower Body hits with their Tail attack, the target will receive an extra 6 poison-type damage."},{"title":"◯ Weakening","description":"When the Lower Body section is reduced to 0 HP or fewer, the Androscorpion receives a -2 penalty for Evasion.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nScorpion Shell (50G/Red B) |\n2 -6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 11 |\nPoison Stinger (100G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nPoison Stinger with Intact Poison Sac (800G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Androscorpion","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"abr1F7FWKsudTjkE","name":"Shard Medusa","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:shard-medusa","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Daemonic","habitat":"Labyrinths, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"16","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"AB, p. 91","description":"This is a Medusa variant adapted to the Shallow environment. Compared to previously known Medusae, it is notably larger, and those caught in the magic power of its snake hair transform into mineral-like entities equivalent to Abyss Shards. Furthermore, they have mastered Abyssal Magic, and their high magic power is recognized as a threat.\n\nWhile their intelligence is thought to be on par with an average Human, they harbor an intense hatred for Humanoids, and there are no reported instances of it engaging in conversation.\n\nWhile there are many differences compared to the original Medusa, and similarities have been noted between its mineralizing magic power and that of the Basilisk , this monster is believed to never reveal these secrets to Humanoids.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Eyes of Stone / 10 (17) / Willpower / Negates","description":"At the end of each round, if a character faces a Medusa, they need to roll a Willpower Check or receive effects of Petrification (Dexterity, Agility / -6) (see ML, p. 71).\nIf an ability score drops to 0 or below due to this ability, the target turns into a mineral formation similar to giant Abyss Shard.\nThis effect is treated as Curse type.\nHair"},{"title":"◯Attack Obstacle = +2 • +2","description":"Countless moving serpentine strands of hair conceal the body. Section Body gains a +2 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks and ranged attacks.\nThis effect is lost when the Hair section's HP falls to 0 or below."},{"title":"►Simultaneous Attack","description":"A Medusa's Snake Hair attacks all enemy characters in the skirmish area, but a separate Accuracy Check is needed for each character."},{"title":"◯Snake Venom / 11 (18) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Snake Hair attack hits, it inflicts 6 Poison magic damage to the target.\nBody"},{"title":"► Abyssal Magic 9 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":"The enhancement effect can be used up to 2 rounds."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], [ Magic Convergence ], and [ Magic Control ].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMedusa's Curse (400G/Red A) |\n2 - 10 |\nGem (150G/Red A) x 1d |\n11+ |\nShard Petrifying Eyes (4,100G/Gold Red Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Shard Medusa","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"aqNMNxKMJzOFnuPR","name":"Hill Giant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hill-giant","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Giantish","habitat":"Hills","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 349","description":"Standing around 5m tall, the Hill Giant is the smallest of the Giants . Not too bright either, a Hill Giant will chase down prey and attempt to eat just about anything once. While other barbarous do use the services of Hill Giants because of their immense power and strength, it's also fairly easy to exploit the poor giants, and more than a few end up as butts of jokes.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► War Cry/12 (19)/Willpower/Negates","description":"The Hill Giant unleashes a mighty yell, causing fear in those who fail to resist within a 10-meter radius around Hill Giant. This fear, treated as a psychic effect, gives a -2 penalty to all Skill Checks for the next 30 seconds (3 rounds).\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Hill Giant's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect disappears when the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nGold Bracelet (2,500G/Gold White S) |\n13+ |\nGiant Helmet (9,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hill Giant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"b1aY0rdDIVcRXIRy","name":"Murcielago","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:murcielago","level":11,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric,","habitat":"Unknown","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20/20(Flying)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.96","description":"Murcielago serve the high Nosferatu Barbarous, and look no different from a Humanoid.\n\nIn addition to their high fighting prowess, they have the ability to shapeshift into bats. They are also resistant to Swords of Protection, and their abilities and appearance allow them to carry out important missions such as infiltrating Humanoid cities.\n\nThey are considered dangerous because they often treat those they have bonded with as \"lovers\" and use them as stepping stones to infiltrate or plot against them by forcing them to do as they wish.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Murcielago receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Swords of Protection Resistance","description":"If the Murcielago is within the influence of Swords of Protection, the Murcielago's Soulscars are treated as 2 points lower."},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 11 Level/Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ],[ Multi-Action ], and [ Rune Master ]."},{"title":"► Bonds of Love and Blood/14 (21)/Willpower/Neg","description":"Murcielago extract the blood of the character they have chosen to fight for life, and offer their own bodily fluids to strengthen the bond between them.\nThis ability can be used once a week during combat, and each time it is used, Bonds of Love and Blood points will accumulate by one point. As the points accumulate, the target will start to develop feelings for this monster, eventually loving it like a partner and protecting it as such. The target's love for the Murcielago will become stronger each time it receives this ability (up to a maximum of 7 points).\nGuidelines for the Number of Times Bonds of Love and Blood has been Received and its Effects\nNumber of Times |\nEffect Guideline |\n1 – 3 |\nRespect and assist the wishes of this monster as much as possible without affecting one's own life, property, position, etc. If the monster becomes an enemy in battle, it will sabotage combat activities as much as possible. |\n4 – 5 |\nThe desires of this monster should be given priority in all aspects of life. The preservation of property, position, and name is secondary. When the monster is an enemy in battle, it does not take any active action at first but betrays its allies the moment it is injured (meaning its HP is reduced). |\n6 |\nThis monster is considered a lover equal to one's own life. If requested, one will offer all their life except their own without thinking twice. If they are allies in a battle, they will betray their allies without hesitation and join forces with this monster. |\n7 |\nThey come to think of this monster as everything that is life to them. If they are told to die, they will kill themself without hesitation. |\nThis effect is permanent and can be used only once per week; even if the resistance succeeds, the accumulated Bonds of Love and Blood points are kept. Also, the target gets a bonus to all action checks equal to half of the Bonds of Love and Blood points (rounded up) when the target is acting in accordance with the monster's will (as determined by the GM).\nThis effect is Curse type. Murcielago can have only one target under this effect at the same time. If this effect is used once for a character and then used on another character by the same monster, the character's Bonds of Love and Blood points will immediately return to 0, and all effects will be lost."},{"title":"⏩ △ Bat Shapeshifting","description":"Murcielago changes its own appearance into a bat about 20 cm in length. Or, it returns to its original form from the state of being a bat.\nWhen in the form of a bat, the physical abilities of the bat will be equivalent to its appearance (enough to fly as a bat), and all unique skills will be ineffective. Also, the bat form is not treated as a character and is not a target of any effect. If the character is changed during a battle, it can leave the battlefield.\nThis ability can be used only once per hour, and unless this ability is used, the shape never changes.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nThe Lustrous Blood of Murcielago (2,000G/Red S) |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9 - 12 |\nBarbarous Directives (500G/White A) |\n13+ |\nBlood Family Directives (5,000G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Murcielago","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"b43M9vHwkQgwOhbo","name":"Zeanemo Attacker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zeanemo-attacker","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Elven","habitat":"Seas","reputation":14,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15/18 (swimming)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 118","description":"Among the Zeanemo , these are particularly large specimens of the soldier class who are specially trained in weapons fighting.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"🗨Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles / 8 (15) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This ability may only be used once per turn, just before a Major Action. Within \"Range: Touch\" it is used to entangle \"Target: 1 Character\" with the tentacles within their right eye. If the target fails the Evasion check, the following two effects occur:\n- If the monster makes a melee attack against its target immediately afterward, the target's Evasion check is decreased by -2. This effect only applies to that single Evasion check (the tentacles automatically release after the melee attack).\n- The target must perform a Fortitude Check with Target Number 13. If the target fails, it is paralyzed for the next 1 minute (6 rounds) and suffers a -1 penalty on Accuracy checks. This effect is Poison type and does not accumulate."},{"title":"◯Behind the Right Eye","description":"The character who became the target of the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles] can declare that they will \"aim at the right eye\" when making a weapon attack against this monster on their turn (regardless of whether the Evasion check was successful or not against the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles]). If the declared attack hits, its physical and/or magic damage is increased by 4 points.\nIf this action is taken and the increase in damage actually occurs, PCs will no longer receive the loot \"Blue Strange Eye\" from the targeted monster.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBlue Strange Eye (160G/Red B) |\n2 - 8 |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |\n9+ |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zeanemo Attacker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"bz7dD1Afdvi91Ul3","name":"Hog Hoodling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hog-hoodling","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Various","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR III p. 329","description":"This is a Hoodling Youma who is used to handling animals and fights by riding on them. The riding animal is carried around for food and may be a variety of small to medium size animals, not limited to pigs.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Dismounting","description":"This monster's Rider section is mounted on the Pig section. If the Rider is dismounted, all sections suffer a -2 penalty on all Skill Checks and have their damage reduced by -2 points.\nSee the Rider class and the Riding Rules (see CR III, p. 87) for rules for this monster on how to dismount and mount back at the mount.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nDirty Hood (20G/White B) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 11 |\nCheap Meat (100G/Red A) |\n12+ |\nFine Meat (200G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hog Hoodling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ceCQFmWZMvRWB2bT","name":"Sahagin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:sahagin","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Gilman","habitat":"Coasts, River Deltas","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12/16 (Swimming)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"SSW; Monstrous Lore p. 73","description":"Sahagin resemble fish with arms and legs. They are treated as slaves among the Gilman tribes and are often used for labor and as soldiers. Sahagin are very self-conscious and timid, and will not fight unless ordered to by a superior. They primarily live in water but sometimes attack small boats or children playing on the shore.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":"2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 10 |\nSahagin Trident (30G/Black White B) |\n11+ |\nOrnate Trident (120G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sahagin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dI673MCDuMgZGmLK","name":"Zeanemo Master","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zeanemo-master","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Elven, Sylvan","habitat":"Seas","reputation":18,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"18/20 (swimming)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 120","description":"Extremely powerful, both physically and mentally, these leaders reign supreme in the Zeanemo collective. They are the leader of the Zeanemo and lead the other Zeanemos in battle.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Fairy Magic 9 Level / Magic Power 12 (19)","description":"Can use Earth, Water/Ice, Light, or Dark types.\nIt does not change even if the contract pattern (see MA, p. 136) is used."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"🗨Mana Strike = +12 damage","description":"May deal an additional +12 damage to their next melee attack. At risk, they take a -2 penalty to their Fortitude and Willpower checks."},{"title":"⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles / 13 (20) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This ability may only be used once per turn, just before a Major Action. Within \"Range: Touch\" it is used to entangle \"Target: 1 Character\" with the tentacles within their right eye. If the target fails the Evasion check, the following two effects occur:\n- If the monster makes a melee attack against its target immediately afterward, the target's Evasion check is decreased by -2. This effect only applies to that single Evasion check (the tentacles automatically release after the melee attack).\n- The target must perform a Fortitude Check with Target Number 18. If the target fails, it is paralyzed for the next 1 minute (6 rounds) and suffers a -1 penalty on Accuracy checks. This effect is Poison type and does not accumulate."},{"title":"◯Behind the Right Eye","description":"The character who became the target of the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles] can declare that they will \"aim at the right eye\" when making a weapon attack against this monster on their turn (regardless of whether the Evasion check was successful or not against the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles]). If the declared attack hits, its physical and/or magic damage is increased by 4 points.\nIf this action is taken and the increase in damage actually occurs, PCs will no longer receive the loot \"Strange White Eye\" from the targeted monster.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nStrange White Eye (1,200G/Red S) |\n2 - 10 |\nOcean Pearl (200G/Gold Red A) |\n11+ |\nSilver Pearl (3,000G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zeanemo Master","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"dKO0szUwFHlPpTtk","name":"Ira Sabinga","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ira-sabinga","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Mountains, Floating Rocks","reputation":13,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Wind-type +3 Damage","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"13/13 (Flight)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CO","description":"An assault soldier from among the Sabinga , highly skilled in combat. They confront the enemy directly, delivering swift and varied attacks with their weapons. However, they are not known for their intelligence, nor are they adept at strategy or negotiations.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨 Somersault Attack","description":"Flips and flutters back and forth in front of the target, attacking at an irregular trajectory.\nDeclaring this before a melee attack grants the Sabinga a +1 bonus to its Accuracy Check, but incurs a -1 penalty to its Evasion Check.\nThis ability cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters with melee attacks that can be reached, but the damage will be reduced by -3.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nKeen Weapon (100G/Black White A) |\n10+ |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ira Sabinga","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"e8Ia61r0xDm8xNlr","name":"Vampire Tetrahedron","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:vampire-tetrahedron","level":17,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Nosferatu, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":19,"weakness":26,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":23,"movementSpeed":"18/36(Flying)","fortitude":"22 (29)","willpower":"22 (29)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 104","description":"Among the Nosferatu , there exists a Matter Clan of vampires who have spent many years studying as scholars. Like other clans, they focus on contracts, but their first priority is to pass on knowledge.\n\nDespite their considerable proficiency in Barbarous, they do not like to exclude others from their work. They view almost everything as a research target, and their only concern is whether or not they can prove their own ideas through experiments or other means. They prefer to \"preserve\" the state of things so that their research targets will never cease, and they do not go around killing or destroying without careful consideration.\n\nHowever, they will not tolerate any interruption that may interfere with their research and will try to eliminate it with their own abilities. They are also characterized by their arrogance and ruthlessness, and when it comes to the experiments they have in mind, they do not care about the lives of others.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic , Divine Magic 14 Level / Magic Power 21 (28)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Double Cast ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"◯ Normal Weapon Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Knowledge &amp; Weakness Exploit / 21 (28)","description":"Can make Sage Intelligence checks with a Standard Value of 21 (fixed value of 28).\nIf this monster makes an attack against another character who is detected as having a weak point, the effect of the attack is doubled."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Vampire Tetrahedron receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Regeneration = 12 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Vampire Tetrahedron recovers 12 HP. This does not affect the Vampire Tetrahedron at 0 HP or lower."},{"title":"◯ Vampire Body","description":"As long as a Vampire Tetrahedron is under sunlight, it takes 12 magic damage at the end of its turn and receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks. This damage cannot be reduced in any way. Additionally, the Vampire Tetrahedron cannot use their [ ◯ Regeneration] or [ ◯ Normal Weapon Immunity] abilities."},{"title":"⏩ Fourth Dimensional Laws / 22 (29) / Willpower / Negates","description":"It is a limited manifestation of a higher level of reason that is incomprehensible to the human mind.\nThis skill affects in \"Range/Area: 1 (100m) / Target \" affects \"Target: 1 Character\". Target will treat \"5\" or \"6\" as \"0\" for each dice rolled for the Skill Checks for 10 seconds (1 round). So, Success Value can become even 1 or 0. If a dice roll is changed by an effect such as [ Sword's Grace/Change Fate ], or if a dice roll is changed again, this effect will still work, so for example \"1,2\" roll changed to \"5,6\" will result in 0+0= 0 result.\nEven with this effect, the automatic failure still occurs only when \"1, 1\" was rolled.\nThis effect can be used only once in 10 seconds (1 round) for the same target, and consumes 5 MP to use."},{"title":"◯ Vampire of the Matter Clan","description":"If a Claws attack hits, the monster's HP will be restored by the applied damage.\nA target whose HP is reduced to 0 or less by Claws' attack suffers a -15 penalty on Death Checks. If such a target fails the Death Check, the monster chooses one of the following three options: make the target a vessel, make the target die, or scar the soul for 5 soulscars of the target and turn it into a Mad Blood .\nThose that become Mad Bloods begin to act immediately afterward.\nThe vessels do not age the same as there are under the effect of [ Preservation ] (see CR II, p. 142). They cannot take action, and no other effect or damage is applied except for canceling this effect can affect them. This effect is treated as a Curse-type effect with a Success value of 26. If the effect is dispelled, the target is \"dead\" at the time of dispelling.\nIf Vampire Tetrahedron does not recover HP by [ ◯ Vampire of the Matter Clan] for 7 days, their HP and MP will be reduced by 12 points, and they lose their unique skill [ ◯ Regeneration]. This reduction will accumulate every 7 days, but it will all be removed immediately when the [ ◯ Vampire of the Matter Clan] is used."},{"title":"◯ Revival","description":"When the HP of this monster becomes 0 or less, and there is a character within a 100m radius who has become a vessel by the effect of [ ◯ Vampire of the Matter Clan], the monster will immediately take over the character's body and revive itself. When this happens, the HP is restored to its maximum value, but the MP inherits the current value of the Vampire before revival.\nThe vessel character dies at this stage. To revive, the HP of the new Vampire Tetrahedron must be reduced to 0 or less, and the corpse must be retrieved (for example, if the Vampire dies by falling off a cliff, they may resurrect out of the PCs' sight). If there are multiple vessels within the area of effect, a character will be randomly selected from them to become the new body.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBeautiful Tetrahedron (6,000G/Gold Black S) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11 - 12 |\nGlasses of the Immortal (3,500G/Gold Black White S) |\n13+ |\nGolden Recording Glasses of the Immortal (16,500G/Gold Black White SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Vampire Tetrahedron","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"eCleeOFhYZAtKTZU","name":"Talos Soldier","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:talos-soldier","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Vulcan","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice +3 Damage","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"16/-","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"BM","description":"Talos are artificial creatures believed to have been created by Barbarous and Dark Dwarves . These creatures were driven underground during the era of the Ancient Magic Civilization. According to legend, Talos were made by magically mineralizing various creatures and feeding them into a furnace that could burn the ore called \"Ignis Blaze.\"\n\nTalos resemble warriors standing about 2 meters tall. They wear tightly fitted armor and carry large swords. Their armor acts as a natural outer shell, and although they have horns, the horns grow directly from their skulls, not from their helmets. Their faces are Humanoid but lack expression.\n\nTalos were created to fight and serve Barbarous. They are fearless and possess great combat skills. They have a general resistance to magic, and when they exert themselves, flames spew from the outer joints and gaps along the inner thigh. Because Talos is an artificial lifeform, it does not possess a soul and, therefore, does not have Soulscars. As a result, it is unaffected by Swords of Protection. However, a major weakness of Talos is its inability to perceive fairies and spirits.\n\nDuring the Magic Civilization era, Talos were believed to have been extensively used. However, most of them were seemingly destroyed in the battles of that era, making them rarely seen today. Nonetheless, Talos can still be found in boxes called \"Fire's Casing\" in Magic Civilization ruins. As long as they remain within these casings, they seem to continue sleeping without aging.\n\nOpening a Fire's Casing with the correct sequence makes an individual the master of the Talos. However, a Talos cannot survive without consuming a Humanoid heart once a year. Although not certain, there is a theory that Talos served as a motif in the foundational research of Runefolk . Some similarities can be observed between the two.\n\nTalos Soldiers are the lowest class of mass-produced soldiers. They have minimal intelligence and lack human emotions. They mechanically follow the orders of their masters. In some cases, they are found in large numbers and are used as subordinates by Drakes .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Anti-Magic Shell","description":"Gains a +4 bonus to resistance checks against magic. However, this does not apply to resistance to Fairy Magic and Nature Magic."},{"title":"◯ Fairy/Spirit Blindness","description":"Cannot sense or hear the voices of fairies and spirits. When damaged by Fairy Magic, Fairies or Nature Magic, it suffers 3 additional points of damage."},{"title":"⏩ Ignis Blaze","description":"Flames spews from its entire body. Damage from melee attacks becomes fire type, with a +2 bonus to Accuracy Checks and a +4 bonus to damage. This effect is not cumulative. When the creature uses this ability, it receives 5 fixed damage at the end of its turn."},{"title":"🗨 Desperate Strike I","description":"When using this, if the attack hits, it deals +5 damage, and the user receives 5 points of fixed damage. If the attack does not hit, no fixed damage is suffered.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 10 |\nShattered Ignis Ore Core (300G/Gold Black A) |\n11+ |\nCracked Ignis Ore Core (1,000G/Gold Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Talos Soldier","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"fQAtluiEqUuQVNuw","name":"Drake Baron (Dragon Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:drake-baron-dragon-form","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":13,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"20/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR II p. 347","description":"This is the Dragon form of the Drake Baron (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 7 Level /Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats[ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► Breath of Light/11 (18)/Fortitude/Half","description":"The Drake Baron may vomit a mass of pure energy directed toward a single target. The energy travels to \"Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Shot \" and deals 2d + 16 energy magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], and [ Recovery (5 pts.) ] Techniques."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Humanification","description":"It instantly transforms into Human form. Refer to Drake Baron (Human Form) for data on the Human form. If the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it is immediately stunned.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Dragonification].\nWing"},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nSword Shard (200G) x 5 |\n2 - 9 |\nDraconian Horn (500G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nMajestic Draconian Horn (4,200G/Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Drake Baron (Dragon Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gikZdRwKjP2s8I5X","name":"Yeti","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:yeti","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":1,"languages":"Giantish","habitat":"Cold Regions, Snowy Mountains","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"17","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"SW2.0 CR III, p. 302","description":"A snow Giant covered in white hair, a Yeti stands tall at over 5m. Often found in cold and snowy areas, Yetis are quite territorial, and will mercilessly defend their territory from any invaders. Their arms are larger than their body, and their devastating claw attacks can rend steel with little effort, so retreat is recommended if accidentally angering one.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Water/Ice Immunity","description":"Upper Body"},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Yeti successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack against the same target.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":""},{"title":"► Bow","description":"Yeti’s height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nWhen the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 12 |\nWhite Fur Pelt (1,000G/Red S) |\n13+ |\nSilver Fur Pelt (9,000G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Yeti","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"gnDimB8CXseIWNjl","name":"Dark Troll","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dark-troll","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Giantish","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":13,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"17","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 340","description":"Much leaner than a typical Troll , a Dark Troll has an excellent sense of fighting and a strong religious belief. A high-ranking member of Troll society, they stand out with their jet-black skin and dangerous aura. Dark Trolls greatly hate cowardice and will respect those who show their strength, even Humanoids who dare to stand up to the Dark Troll's immense power.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 7 Level/Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +10 damage","description":"May deal an additional +10 damage to their next melee attack. At risk, they take a -2 penalty to their Fortitude and Willpower checks."},{"title":"◯ Dark Regeneration = 5 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Dark Troll recovers 5 HP. This has no effect if the Dark Troll is at 0 HP or lower or is under sunlight."},{"title":"◯ Weakened","description":"As long as a Dark Troll is under sunlight, it receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nTroll Blood (100G/Red A) |\n2 - 11 |\nGem (300G/Gold A) x 1d |\n12+ |\nStrange Holy Symbol (3,300G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dark Troll","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hDQ3sE6AteMRcg7P","name":"Deep Sahagin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:deep-sahagin","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Gilman","habitat":"Oceans, Deep Seas","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Earth damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"12/16 (Swimming)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement), p. 134","description":"The Deep Sahagin, an ancient species of Sahagin , typically dwells in the deep sea and rarely shows itself on land. However, in the depths of the ocean, sinister plans for invading the surface world are being hatched, and occasionally, their figures can be spotted along the coastline at midnight. Their plans are believed to be progressing steadily, quite literally under the surface. Most Deep Sahagin worship the Sea Snatcher Eiryak.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯Water/Ice Absorption","description":"When receiving physical or magical damage of Water/Ice type, HP and MP will not decrease from the damage, and they will not receive any adverse effects from water/ice properties. Additionally, HP is restored by the same amount as the damage that would have been applied."},{"title":"►Water Spout / 9 (16) / Fortitude / Half","description":"With a \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot \", deals 2d+8 points of Water/Ice magic damage to 1 target character.\nThis ability cannot be used underwater. Using this ability consumes 5 MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nOrnate Trident (120G/Black White A) |\n8+ |\nWell-Maintained Trident (1,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Deep Sahagin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hJlVi5qDwDDXX6jU","name":"Lizardman Bearer","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lizardman-bearer","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Lizardman, Dragonic","habitat":"Swamps, Wetlands","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Earth damage + 3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"12/12 (Swimming)","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"KF","description":"This is one of the Lizardmen caste. Their fighting ability is no different from that of an ordinary Lizardman, but they carry a battle flag attached to their spear. In battle, they stay in the rear or beside their regiment, inspiring and supporting their comrades.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Inspiring Flag Spear/Can't","description":"Lizardman Bearer raises its flag spear high, inspiring allies.\nLizardmen (regardless of gender) within \"Range: Caster\" and \"Target: All Areas (30m radius) / All\" get +1 bonus to Accuracy check and Magic Power of unique skill for 10 seconds (1 round) and regain 5 HP immediately.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nLizardman Flag (100G/Green Black A) |\n2 - 10 |\nNothing |\n11+ |\nSeven-color Scales (220G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lizardman Bearer","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hLZClwnQR3oxjtIL","name":"Drake Count (Dragon Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:drake-count-dragon-form","level":18,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":19,"weakness":26,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":23,"movementSpeed":"30/60(Flying)","fortitude":"24 (31)","willpower":"24 (31)","source":"CR III p. 341","description":"This is the Drake version of the Drake Count (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Energy Immunity","description":"Body"},{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 15 Level/Magic Power 21 (28)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"A Drake Count (Dragon Form) can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Universal Metamagic ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Multi-Action ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"A Drake Count (Dragon Form) can use the [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Recovery (9 pts.) ], [ Giant Arms ], and [ Sphinx Knowledge ] Techniques."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +21 damage","description":"A Drake Count may deal an additional +21 damage to their next melee attack. If they do, at risk, they receive a -2 penalty to Fortitude and Willpower checks until their next turn."},{"title":"► Radiant Breath/24 (31)/Fortitude/Half","description":"Drake Count spits out a pure energy mass at \"Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Shot \" and explodes it at the point of impact, dealing \"Target: 1 area (6m Radius) / 20\" 2d+25 energy magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used in consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Humanification","description":"It instantly transforms into Human form. Refer to Drake Count (Human Form) for data on the Human form. If the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it is immediately stunned.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ⏩ △ Instant Dragonification].\nWing"},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Drake Count (Dragon Form) receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the Wing sections falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"🗨 Decoy Attack II","description":"It gains -2 to Accuracy checks, but the damage is increased by +8 on hit.\nIf the declared attack is evaded, the enemy receives a -2 penalty to Evasion checks for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is cumulative up to - 8 but is lost if the target fails an Evasion check even once.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nHeraldic Ring (3,000G/Gold White S) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nMajestic Draconian Horn (4,200G/Red S) |\n13+ |\nNoble Draconian Horn (12,600G/Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Drake Count (Dragon Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hQ2NwRRZdJU8lCXm","name":"Bolg Heavy Arm","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bolg-heavy-arm","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":10,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR I p. 403","description":"These are heavily-armed warriors of the Bolg tribe of Youma . Armed with a shield and a greatsword, they will do their best to crush their enemies without fear of being wounded.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150/Black White A) |\n8+ |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bolg Heavy Arm","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"hpj7fyQ4xutfIQBj","name":"Cryodibraz","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:cryodibraz","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Cold Regions","reputation":11,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 118","description":"This is a Cryoblaz with high combat power. They are the core of any raiding party.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":""},{"title":"⏩Freezing Stance","description":"This effect lasts for 10 seconds (1 round), does not accumulate, and consumes 3 MP when used.\nDamage caused by a Weapon attack becomes Water/Ice type and increases by +2. If the Cryodibraz is hit by a melee attack, the attacker will be dealt an additional 1 point of Water/Ice fixed damage for the duration, regardless of the success or failure of the melee attack.\nThis effect ends immediately after the Cryoblaz receives 1 or more points of Fire-type applied damage without waiting 10 seconds (1 round). If it is caused by a melee attack, the effect disappears first, and the attacker will not be dealt fixed damage."},{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":""}],"lootTable":[{"roll":"8 - 11","loot":"|"},{"roll":"12+","loot":"|"}]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Cryodibraz","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"i4IpkqW8TQOWvGre","name":"Owlcrudel","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:owlcrudel","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Avian, Barbaric","habitat":"Forests","reputation":14,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"10/30 (Flying)","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Natural History of Ursyla , p. 123","description":"This is an Arakcruder which has evolutionarily adapted to forest activities. While its wings have become compact and lost the ability to fly long distances, its mysterious pair of eyes can detect prey and enemies even in darkness. Though they struggle with intense sunlight, they can function perfectly well in dappled forest light, making them prone to ambushing Humanoids who visit the Great Sebrae Forest of the Ursyla region. Due to their preference for darkness, some make their lair within Shallow Abysses.\n\nThey prefer to operate alone as they believe in silent hunting, but under a commander they deem trustworthy, they can execute well-coordinated group operations.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Flight","description":"Gain a +1 bonus modifier to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯Horn Catch","description":"When an attacker's Accuracy check against this monster fails with a roll of 4 or lower, this monster tears away the attacker's weapon with its horned crest.\nWhen this effect occurs, the attacker drops their weapon on the spot. The weapon cannot be used until it is picked up with a Major Action. If this occurs on the first Accuracy check of an attack declared with [ Repeated Strike ], the second Accuracy check cannot be performed. This also applies to Auto-Return thrown weapons and weapons connected by [ Pull of Soul Tethers ]; the weapon is dropped on the spot and will not return to the thrower.\nThis effect does not apply to attacks with weapons that the GM clearly declares as being fixed to the character. Attacks made with natural body parts such as fists, tails, or bites cannot be dropped, but the attacker automatically takes 4 points of fixed damage."},{"title":"►Rainbow Leap / 7 (14) / Danger Sense / Negates","description":"This effect can only be used when playing in Standard Combat (see CR II, p. 48) or Advanced Combat (see ET, p. 78). When using this effect, this monster's movement is limited to \"Limited Move.\" Additionally, the battlefield must be in a forest or a location with equivalent-level overhead footing.\nDesignate 1 character within 10m of this monster who is not in melee combat. If that character fails a Danger Sense check, move to their coordinates and execute a beak attack. This attack hits automatically without performing an Accuracy check. If the target succeeds in its Danger Sense check, this monster cannot move from its position and remains in place.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7+ |\nBarbarous Owl's Antler (300G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Owlcrudel","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"iTcmTCGwo4FNbtWo","name":"Kobold Apprentice","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:kobold-apprentice","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":1,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Youma, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":7,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"13","fortitude":"3 (10)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"School of Wizardry Eusiz (SW2.5 supplement), p. 108","description":"This is a Kobold wizard who has picked up spellbooks and other things around the magic school in Eusiz, and either learned magic alone or by studying under other Barbarous wizards. It is an outstanding individual among Kobolds, and as a wizard, has the same abilities as a novice adventurer, so it is not to be underestimated.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"▶Magic (1 system) Level 2 / Magic Power 4 (11)","description":"This monster has learned two levels of one of the following: Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic , Divine Magic , or Magitech ."},{"title":"◯ Targeting or Metamagic/Targets","description":"The GM determines which Combat Feat the Kobold Apprentice has learned.\nIf the monster has learned [ Targeting ], stray shots cannot occur.\nIf the monster has learned [ Metamatic/Targets ], they may double, triple, etc. the MP cost of single-target spells to cast them on multiple targets."},{"title":"◯ Delicate Loot","description":"If physical damage reduces the monster's HP to 0 or less, the \"Fragile Implement\" loot item will be lost.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nFragile Implement (40G/-) |\n2 - 8 |\nCheap Weapon (10G / Black/White B) |\n9+ |\nBag of Silver (30G/-) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Kobold Apprentice","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"iVySf299xM8MHgHd","name":"Gremlin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gremlin","level":2,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Arcana, Youma","habitat":"Highlands, Mountains","reputation":9,"weakness":12,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":11,"movementSpeed":"16/32 (Flying)","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"5 (12)","source":"CR I p. 397","description":"Gremlins look like infants with hair all over their bodies, with small fangs and bat-like wings. They work hard and are mischievous, sometimes tricking and kidnapping Humanoid children or robbing livestock.\n\nThey like to break things like watermills and windmills. Because of that, Humanoids use \"Gremlin laughed\" as a synonym for failing devices.\n\nGremlins have the same position as Bolgs in the Barbarous army.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 2 Level/Magic Power 4 (11)","description":""},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur."},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"A Gremlin receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNone |\n8+ |\nStrange Necklace (160G/White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gremlin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ike26HMB5ozUBDys","name":"Quepala'marga'ula","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:quepalamargaula","level":12,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Arcana, Drakish","habitat":"Forests, Caves, Swamps, Shallows","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"15 15","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 333","description":"This is a highest-ranking Quepala'ula , usually acting as tribal chiefs. Although they are regarded as quite powerful among the Barbarous, they do not take their place as generals in the Barbarous army, preferring to hide in the dark and plotting. There are some Quepala'marga'ulas who prefer to dwell in Shallow Abysses.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 12 Level/Magic Power 15 (22)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ] [ Metamagic/Targets ], [ Rune Master ], and[ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"◯ Poison/15 (22)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"If the Bite attack hits, the target is dealt additional 12 Poison magic damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nSpellbook (500G/White A) |\n7 - 10 |\nEsoteric Spellbook (1,500G/White S) |\n11+ |\nRare Grimoire (3,000G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Quepala'marga'ula","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"j8KERta1C6LacvQA","name":"Zeanemo","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:zeanemo","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Elven","habitat":"Seas","reputation":11,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"12/18 (swimming)","fortitude":"5 (12)","willpower":"4 (11)","source":"Natural History of Burlight , p. 117","description":"The Zeanemo have the ability to breathe underwater and primarily inhabit the oceanic shallows near the Burlight Region.\n\nAt first glance, they resemble Elves , with their slender build, beautiful facial features, long pointed ears, and fair to pale skin. According to tradition, Zeanemo were once Elves who were soulscarred by the god Eiryak, the Sea Snatcher.\n\nThe most notable difference from Elves in their appearance is their right eye. A Zeanemo's right eye lacks an eyeball and instead contains an anemone-like tentacle. Normally, they keep this tentacle stored in their eye socket and close their eyelids. However, during fights or when preying on their targets, they fully open their eye, revealing the flexible tentacle. This tentacle can be used as a weapon in addition to their regular attacks. It often exhibits stunning shades of pink and orange, resembling a blooming flower. To conceal their unique eye, Zeanemos sometimes wear an eye patch when their eyes are closed, making them appear more like ordinary Elves.\n\nZeanemo are capable of briefly venturing onto land for about an hour, but they must return to a water-rich environment or face death. They wear clothing made from plant fibers and are skilled in using various weapons. Occasionally, they don armor crafted from shells and turtle shells.\n\nWhile they possess intelligence and may initially appear peaceful, their true nature is brutal and cruel, and they have a penchant for plundering. They harbor a strong animosity towards Elves and often raid their settlements, including ships crewed by Elves. Zeanemo are capable of breeding with Elves and occasionally abduct young Elves. They have a lifespan of approximately 500 years and their power increases with age.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles / 5 (12) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This ability may only be used once per turn, just before a Major Action. Within \"Range: Touch\" it is used to entangle \"Target: 1 Character\" with the tentacles within their right eye. If the target fails the Evasion check, the following two effects occur:\nIf the monster makes a melee attack against its target immediately afterward, the target's Evasion check is decreased by -2. This effect only applies to that single Evasion check (the tentacles automatically release after the melee attack).\nThe target must perform a Fortitude Check with Target Number 10. If the target fails, it is paralyzed for the next 1 minute (6 rounds) and suffers a -1 penalty on Accuracy checks. This effect is Poison type and does not accumulate."},{"title":"◯Behind the Right Eye","description":"The character who became the target of the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles] can declare that they will \"aim at the right eye\" when making a weapon attack against this monster on their turn (regardless of whether the Evasion check was successful or not against the [⏩Entangling Poisonous Tentacles]). If the declared attack hits, its physical and/or magic damage is increased by 4 points.\nIf this action is taken and the increase in damage actually occurs, PCs will no longer receive the loot \"Strange Eye\" from the targeted monster.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nStrange Eye (80G/Red B) |\n2 - 9 |\nWeapon (30G/Black White B) |\n10+ |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Zeanemo","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"jFTNvNMKCs4DPjan","name":"Goblin Shaman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:goblin-shaman","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Sylvan","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"11/-","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Monstrous Lore p. 78","description":"This is a higher class Goblin Youma . They look like ordinary Goblins, but they are decorated with dark-colored bird feathers and gems. They are more intelligent than ordinary Goblins and can use magic.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Fairy Magic 5 Level/Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"Types used are \"Earth\", \"Fire\", \"Wind\", and \"Dark\"."},{"title":"► Divine Magic 2 Level/Magic Power 5 (12)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"Can use [ Metamagic/Targets ] Combat Feat.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nBag of Silver (30G) x 1d |\n6 - 9 |\nGems (150G/Gold A) x 1d |\n10+ |\nLuxury Ornaments (500G/Gold White A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Goblin Shaman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"jmrlk0dYwA37aHmK","name":"Dagger Hoodling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dagger-hoodling","level":1,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":1,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Various","reputation":6,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"10","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 396","description":"Armed with a dagger, this Hoodling excels in close combat.\n\nHoodlings are short-sighted Youma , unable to understand the battlefield, and are so eager to fight that they are blind to their surroundings. They act in groups and obey stronger Barbarous such as Goblins and Bolgs. They have no fear of death and are mainly used as slaves for their bigger cousins.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dagger Hoodling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"k4TGpaKDYKZCJ1XA","name":"Quepala'ula","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:quepalaula","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Arcana, Drakish","habitat":"Forests, Cave, Swamp, Shallow","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR I p. 406","description":"This is a Barbarous with a snake head. From the neck down, it is almost the same as a Human, but the neck and head are those of a thick snake, together about 50 cm long.\n\nAlthough Quepala'ulas are known to have inherited knowledge from the Magic Civilization Period, their clan can be divided into two main groups. The first are those who prefer dark, damp places and live in tribes. In these settlements, the lower Barbarous, such as Goblins and Bolgs , often serve as slaves and guards.\n\nThe others live in Shallow Abysses, utilizing their knowledge of Magic Civilization to control daemons as their followers. They use the area as a hunting ground, leaving a few zones of seeming safety amidst the thick growth of poison grass and mushrooms, where they enjoy slowly hunting down any passing prey.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Magic (2 systems) 6 Level /Magic Power 8 (15)","description":"Most of them have Truespeech and Spiritualism Magic at 6th level, but some of them might instead of one of them have Summoning Arts at 6th level."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"◯ Poison/7 (14)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"If their Bite attack hits, the target is dealt additional 6 Poison magic damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nNothing |\n5 - 8 |\nArcana-Language Book (170G/White A) |\n9 - 12 |\nSpellbook (500G/White A) |\n13+ |\nEsoteric Spellbook (1,500G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Quepala'ula","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"kfcwOn7mSR2rna7G","name":"Quepala'laga'ula","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:quepalalagaula","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Shallows","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"AB, p. 91","description":"Within Quepalas , these are individuals who primarily operate in Shallow Abysses.\n\nHaving inherited knowledge about the Shallows from Daemons, they possess unique understanding regarding the laws of maintaining, expanding, moving, and transferring Shallows.\n\nParticularly long-lived individuals have knowledge and experience not only with the Shallow, but also with traversing the Daemon World, making their existence feared beyond their actual capabilities by Humanoids and other Barbarous.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯Extraordinary, Unique Power = 10 points (Shallow)","description":"At the start of their turn, if their current MP is 10 points or less, recover 10 points. Additionally, if they have used Abyssal Magic during that turn, they can use all enhanced effects of casted Abyssal Magic.\nThis effect is only valid in Shallows or equivalent environments."},{"title":"►Magic (2 systems) 10 Level / Magic Power 12 (19)","description":"They have learned either or both Summoning Arts and Abyssal Magic (enhanced effects will be used for 2 rounds). In case of learning only one, the other system is usually either Truespeech Magic or Spiritualism Magic ."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting , [ Metamagic/Targets ], [ Magic Convergence ], and [ Magic Control ]."},{"title":"◯Poison / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the Bite attack hits, the target is dealt additional 10 Poison magic damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nSpellbook (500G/White A) |\n9+ |\nEsoteric Spellbook (1,500G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Quepala'laga'ula","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"khlq5lPPDZYZDUXa","name":"Quepala","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:quepala","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric","habitat":"Forests, Caves, Marshes, Shallows","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"6 (13)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Ancient Blue (2.5 supplement), p. 134","description":"Among the Quepala'ula , Quepalas are those who excel in physical abilities. However, they cannot use magic. Because of this, they most often serve as bodyguards to the Quepala'ula. They rarely use weapons, primarily attacking with bite. They carry large rectangular shields in their hands, using them to protect themselves and their guard targets.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison / 7 (14) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If their Bite attack hits, the target is dealt additional 5 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"🗨△Cover I","description":"The effect is the same as the Combat Feat [ Cover I ].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n7 - 11 |\nShield with a sophisticated design (150G/Black White A) |\n12+ |\nLuxurious shield (500G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Quepala","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"km5hFBptRS6jcS3y","name":"Loud Bolg Commander","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:loud-bolg-commander","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":13,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"CR II p. 340","description":"These are the frontline commander of Bolgs , leading their Youma troops through fear.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"△ Frightful Commander/Can't","description":"Gives the order and forces subordinates to follow it.\nAll Accuracy and Evasion checks for \"Target: All areas (30m Radius)/All\" with \"Range: Caster\" are increased by +1. User can exclude any character from the target when used. The character itself is always excluded. This effect is treated as a psychic type with a success value of 0. This ability can only be used in Combat Preparation and lasts until it is individually removed or until this monster is no longer on the battlefield."},{"title":"🗨 Repeated Strike II","description":"Can make two Accuracy checks; if either one hits, damage is dealt once. If the first Accuracy check is successful, the damage is increased by +4; if the second check instead is successful, the damage is determined as usual."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBarbarous' Orders (500G/White A) |\n2 - 9 |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |\n10+ |\nWell-Kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Loud Bolg Commander","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"kwOKk3sQkXeD1qIe","name":"Ogre Berserker","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ogre-berserker","level":11,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Ogre, Drakish","habitat":"Various","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"+2 Magic Damage","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"19","fortitude":"16 (23)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"CR III p. 333","description":"Although they have no shapeshift ability and cannot cast spells, they are a subspecies of Ogres , boasting a strong body twice the size of a normal Ogre and formidable strength. Because of their low intellect, they are used by Ogres and Drakes, but as long as they can fight, Ogre Berserkers are happy.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack II","description":"If an Ogre Berserker successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack. They can make a third attack against the same target if a second attack hits."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike II","description":"An Ogre Berserker can deal an additional +12 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by the Ogre Berserker this turn receives a -2 penalty.\nThis declaration should have been made at the time of the first attack. It cannot be made during an additional attack from the [ ◯ Continuous Attack II].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nBag of Silver (200G) |\n9 - 12 |\nGems (500G/Gold A) x 1d |\n13+ |\nGolden Berserker Accessory (4,500G/Gold White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ogre Berserker","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"kyMpUDi8GGL2wGDC","name":"Hugl Motor","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hugl-motor","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Lizardman, Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Deserts, Mountains","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"15/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 345","description":"This is a skilled warrior of the Hugl Youma tribe who knows how to use Techniques .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ △ Mobile Flying","description":"It gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns. When used in Combat Preparation, it cannot be used in the first round, regardless of the result of the Initiative check."},{"title":"◯ Winged Pursuit","description":"If it is hit with a Claw attack, it can make an additional melee attack with wings.\nAccuracy bonus, damage, and other values are the same as for the claw attack. This ability cannot be used on the same turn in which [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying] is used. Also, once an additional attack is made with this ability, [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying] cannot be used on that turn."},{"title":"⏩ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Bear Muscle ], [ Daemonfinger ], and [ Giant Arms ] Techniques.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nAmber Scales (90G/Red B) |\n5 - 8 |\nSeven-color Scales (220G/Gold Red A) |\n9+ |\nShining Seven-colored Scales (570G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hugl Motor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"l56qpRbA3VftMqqO","name":"Hugl Assaulter","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hugl-assaulter","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Lizardman, Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Desert, Mountain","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Wind type damage +3 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"15/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR I p. 403","description":"This is a Youma warrior of the Hugl clans with sharper fingers and enhanced fighting skills.\n\nSkilled at fighting multiple opponents, they use their claws and wings to strike down one foe after another. They are carefree and are sometimes asked to serve as guards for weaker Barbarous.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ △ Mobile Flying","description":"It gains a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion checks for melee attacks for 10 seconds (1 round).\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns. When used in Combat Preparation, it cannot be used in the first round, regardless of the result of the Initiative check."},{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"They can make two Claws attacks each round. After checking the result of the first attack, the monster can choose whether to make a second attack on the same target further or on a different target of their choice."},{"title":"◯ Winged Pursuit","description":"If it hits with a Claw attack, it can make an additional melee attack with wings. Accuracy bonus, damage, and other values are the same as for the claw attack.\nThis ability cannot be used on the same turn in which [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying] is used. Also, once an additional attack is made with this ability, [ ⏩ △ Mobile Flying] cannot be used on that turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nEarth-toned Scales (30G/Red B) |\n5 - 8 |\nAmber Scales (90G/Red B) |\n9+ |\nSeven-color Scales (220G/Gold Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hugl Assaulter","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lOaoELaiDajclbZO","name":"Glass Basilisk (Monstrous Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:glass-basilisk-monstrous-form","level":12,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Basilisk, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Cold Region, Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"12 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"BM","description":"A Glass Basilisk that has shown its true form: A large lizard about 5m long, with one eye milky-white and cloudy and the other colorless and transparent. In this form, unlike its rational human form, the Glass Basilisk is driven by emotion and tramples all those before it.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison, Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poisonous Blood / 14 (21) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"This is the same as the Glass Basilisk (Human Form) , except for the difference in Resistance value.\nRight Evil Eye"},{"title":"⏩ Glass Gaze / 14 (21) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This is the same as the Glass Basilisk (Human Form) , except for the difference in Resistance value.\nLeft Evil Eye"},{"title":"⏩ Paralyzing Gaze / 14 (21) / Willpower / Negates","description":"This is the same as the Glass Basilisk (Human Form) , except for the difference in Resistance value.\nHead"},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 10 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"Can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ].\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Standing Upright","description":"If the HP of [Section: Body] is reduced to 0 or less, all other Sections receive a -2 penalty to their Evasion."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Humanization","description":"It instantly transforms into Human form. Refer to Glass Basilisk (Human Form) for data on the Human form. If the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it immediately falls unconscious.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Monstrous Form].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBasilisk Pureblood (1,000G / Red S) |\n2 - 11 |\nGlass Eye (24,00G / Gold Red S) |\n12 - 13 |\nGlazed Eye (6,000G / Gold Red S) |\n14+ |\nGlass Eye (12,000G / Gold Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Glass Basilisk (Monstrous Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lYERX62ZypZELGmg","name":"Loreley","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:loreley","level":4,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Elven, Sylvan","habitat":"Rivers","reputation":10,"weakness":14,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14/14 (Swimming)","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"CR II p. 334","description":"They are a tribe of Barbarous who live in rivers and riverbanks and take the form of beautiful, light-robed women. They charm Humanoid men with their magical singing voices and kidnap them to live in their dwellings. However, it is said that when they are bored or their prey are no longer needed, they will leave their captives to drown.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Basic Spellsongs 1 Level/7 (14)/All areas (40m Radius)","description":""},{"title":"► Special Spellsong [Love Song] /7 (14)/All areas (40m Radius)","description":"Can use the [ Love Song ] (see CR II, p. 194) spellsong. This unique skill can only be used if a male is in the opposing faction and if [ ► Basic Spellsongs] were used on the previous turn."},{"title":"► [Finale: Spring Breeze]/7 (14)","description":"Uses [ Finale: Spring Breeze ] at \"Range: 2 (40m)\" to deal 1 character 2d+4 Wind magic damage.\nThis unique skill could be used only if [ ► Basic Spellsongs] or [ ► Special Spellsong] were used on the previous turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nNothing |\n6 - 8 |\nWater Feathered Kimono (100G/White A) |\n9 - 12 |\nBeautiful Feathered Kimono (300G/White A) |\n13+ |\nShining Feathered Kimono (1,000G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Loreley","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"laAvu1hr04BeO2O4","name":"Drake (Dragon Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:drake-dragon-form","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR I p. 409","description":"A Drake will change into dragon form if in danger. They always carry a magical sword that allows them to transform. While transforming, the Drake takes on a silvery-white sheen of razor-edged scales. Its physique becomes sleek and streamlined, and its wings become as sharp as a sword.\n\nDespite their huge size, they retain high agility and are quick to attack.\n\nFor the Human form of this monster, see Drake (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Spiritualism Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"► Breath of Light/8 (15)/Fortitude/Half","description":"With \"Range/Area: 2 (50m)/ Shot ,\" it spits out a chunk of energy at \"Target: 1 Character,\" dealing 2d+10 Energy magic damage.\nThis unique skill cannot be used on consecutive turns."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Humanification","description":"It instantly transforms into Human form. Refer to Drake (Human Form) for data on the Human form.\nIf the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it immediately falls unconscious.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Dragonification].\nWing"},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"All section receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf one of the wings falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nSword Shard (200G) |\n7 - 10 |\nSword Shard (200G) x 2 |\n11 |\nSword Shard (200G) x 3 |\n12+ |\nDecayed Magic Sword (4,000G/Gold Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Drake (Dragon Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"lfLxdlJLrZpLPpVv","name":"Talos Juggernaut","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:talos-juggernaut","level":11,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":0,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Vulcan, Arcana","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice Damage +3","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"25/-","fortitude":"15 (22)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"Among the Talos , this juggernaut is the most heavily fortified in terms of offensive power and is specifically designed to break through enemy lines, even operating independently.\n\nStanding at nearly three meters tall, it wields a massive sword and a large shield. Its thick and foreboding outer shell exudes an intimidating presence.\n\nThey excel in combat against magicians and demonstrate their combat prowess in group battles. Furthermore, they serve as leaders among other Talos and possess the intelligence to comprehend complex strategies. They display unwavering loyalty to their masters and possess a high level of emotional intelligence, enabling them to care for their masters and lend a listening ear during peaceful times.\n\nTo sustain its life, a Talos Juggernaut must consume a humanoid heart every six months.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Mana Absorbing Shell","description":"Gains a +4 bonus to resistance checks against magic. Also, if the resistance check succeeds, HP is recovered equal to the MP used for the spell (the actual number used, or the equivalent for 1 character if [Metamagic/Targets] was present).\nThis does not apply to resistance to Fairy Magic or Nature Magic."},{"title":"◯ Fairy/Spirit Blindness","description":"Cannot sense or hear the voices of fairies and spirits. When damaged by Fairy Magic, Fairies, or Nature Magic, it suffers 3 additional points of damage."},{"title":"⏩ Ignis Blaze","description":"Flames spew from its entire body. Damage from melee attacks becomes fire type, with a +3 bonus to Accuracy Checks and a +6 bonus to damage. This effect is not cumulative. When the creature uses this ability, it receives 8 fixed damage at the end of its turn."},{"title":"🗨 Desperate Strike II","description":"When using this, if the attack hits, it deals +10 damage, and the user receives 10 points of fixed damage. If the attack does not hit, no fixed damage is suffered."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"Talos Juggernaut can attack with a weapon up to 5 target characters within the skirmish in which it resides.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nShattered Ignis Ore Core (800G / Gold Black A) |\n6 - 9 |\nCracked Ignis Ore Core (1000G / Gold Black S) |\n10+ |\nDull Ignis Ore Core (4000G / Gold Black S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Talos Juggernaut","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"mSBMA8Lh5NLZXnZ6","name":"Bolg Suppressor","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:bolg-suppressor","level":14,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountain, Cave","reputation":19,"weakness":24,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"18 (25)","willpower":"16 (23)","source":"CR III p. 337","description":"This is a Bolg Youma fighter who has trained their body to the utmost limit and is filled with a strong presence beyond ordinary people's reach. Although they are hand-to-hand fighters, it is said that they can do more than an ordinary army just alone, and they are trusted by the upper Barbarous as a trump card in local battles.\n\nBolg Suppressors specialize in striking enemies with the heels of their palms, knocking them down in the process. They then look down fiercely at their fallen opponent, defeating their spirit.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"Can make two Fist attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯ Counter","description":"This is the same effect as the combat feat [ Counter ]."},{"title":"◯ Crushing Palm Strike (Fall) / 17 (24) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"If the target is hit by a Fist attack, the target will fall prone on a failed Fortitude check."},{"title":"◯ Crushing Palm Strike (Withering) / 17 (24) / Willpower / Negates","description":"If the target is hit by a Fist attack and fails the Willpower check, the target may not speak or declare any Minor Action or active combat feats for the next 10 seconds (1 round). This effect is of the Psychic type."},{"title":"⏩ Pressure Point/17 (24)/Willpower/Neg","description":"Roll 1d. Bolg Suppressor hits the target with its powerful aura, receiving 10 fixed damage to its MP if it rolls \"1-3\" and to its HP if it rolls \"4-6\".\nThis effect can be used only once in 10 seconds (1 round) and consumes 10 points of its own MP when used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBarbarous' Orders (500G/White A) |\n2 - 4 |\nBattle Gear (30G/White B) |\n5 - 10 |\nSoldier's Outfit (500G/White A) |\n11+ |\nGolden Battle Outfit (3,200G/Gold White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Bolg Suppressor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"mY2mUJDJzHHLw8FB","name":"Forest Giant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:forest-giant","level":13,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":4,"languages":"Giantish","habitat":"Forest","reputation":15,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"19","fortitude":"18 (25)","willpower":"15 (22)","source":"BM","description":"This is a giant about 6 meters tall who lives in the forest. It is usually found deep in the forest, living with nature, and is rarely seen. They are usually calm and quiet among giants, but once it considers someone an enemy, it has no mercy for them and will crush them with its well-trained strikes and techniques.\n\nThey are by no means stupid and can negotiate. However, they are very territorial and will not tolerate intrusion by others. They usually live alone, but rarely travel in search of mates. They have no concept of money and consider everything as their own, so they sometimes get into trouble by eating livestock without permission.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"A Forest Giant can use the [ Gazelle Feet ], [ Strong Blood ], [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Bear Muscle ], and [ Recovery (5 points) ] Techniques."},{"title":"► War Cry / 12 (19) / Willpower / Negates","description":"The Forest Giant unleashes a mighty yell, causing fear in those who fail to resist within a 10-meter radius around them. This fear, treated as a Psychic effect, gives a -2 penalty to all Skill Checks for the next 30 seconds (3 rounds).\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"A Forest Giant's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect disappears when the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMassive Weapon (300G/Black White A) |\n2 - 11 |\nGold Bracelet (2,500G/Gold White S) |\n12+ |\nGiant's Treasure (10,000G/Gold SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Forest Giant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"n41tEx4FNXmvDDla","name":"Arbor Senior","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:arbor-senior","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Drakish, Sylvan","habitat":"Forests","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Monstrous Lore p.86","description":"This is an Arbor leader, an experienced member of the clan. The number of eye-like patterns on their body has been increasing with age, and they look more mischievous.\n\nThey lead the younger Arbors and Ogres in attacks and sabotage of Humanoid cities and strongholds.\n\nThey are skilled defenders and fire fighters, adept at surrounding their targets and ensuring that the job gets done.\n\nThey also seem to be able to mate with long-lived Meria , and long-lived Meria have been seen living together with Arbor Seniors in captivity.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Magic (1 system) 7 Level / Magic Power 10 (17)","description":"An Arbor Senior can cast either Fairy Magic or Nature Magic at 7th level.\nIn the case of Fairy Magic, the types used are \"Earth\" and \"Fire\"."},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"► Flame Shield","description":"The Arbor Senior creates a wall of fire with his anger. It is placed in front of up to 5 targets within a 3m radius of the Arbor Senior, and the target gains +3 Defense for 3 minutes (18 rounds). Also, any character who uses a melee attack or \"Range: Touch\" effect against the target during the duration of this effect will receive 5 fire magic damage after the damage or effect applied. There is no resistance against this damage, but reducing magic damage and fire damage are effective.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nOminous Branches (130G/Red Green A) x 2 |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 10 |\nFiery Residue (900G/Gold A) |\n11+ |\nVindictive Residue (2,400G/Gold S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Arbor Senior","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"oNcmHOhTj3NdfGhy","name":"Tyrant Strider","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:tyrant-strider","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Magitech","habitat":"Grasslands, Mountains","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"26 (4 Legs)","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"Natural History of Dorden , p. 120","description":"This is a Tyrant proficient in combat. The upper body has become more adept at wielding weapons, and ranged attacks are now possible depending on the situation. Additionally, mobility has further increased, allowing for actions such as temporarily leaving the battlefield and regrouping for a charge.\n\nTyrants are a rare Barbarous species, and even those with high capabilities rarely take on leadership roles, such as gang leaders. Instead, they are more often found as sentries.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Delicate Loot","description":"If the HP of Lower Body section is 1 or higher and the HP of Upper Body section falls to 0 or below, the loot \"Glossy Fur\" will be lost."},{"title":"◯In One Fell Swoop","description":"When performing a Normal Move during its turn, an additional Major Action for the Upper Body section is added.\nUpper Body"},{"title":"◯Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"🗨Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters with melee attacks that can be reached, but the damage will be reduced by -3. If more than one is hit, the damage is determined individually."},{"title":"🗨Repeated Strike I","description":"Can make two Accuracy checks; if one hits, the damage is dealt once."},{"title":"►Weapon Throw / 9 (16) / Evasion / Negates","description":"The Tyrant Strider removes and throws the projectile weapon equipped on the back of the Lower Body. Deals \"2d+9\" points of physical damage to 1 target character within \"Range: 1 (10m)\".\nThis ability can only be used twice in total per battle.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯Stable Posture","description":"If it makes a Full Move during its turn, only the Upper Body section can perform a Major Action. However, in addition to the -4 penalty on Evasion checks for Full Moves, it also receives a -2 penalty on action checks for Major Actions."},{"title":"⏩Tiger Crouch Stance","description":"Lowers the Lower Body into a crouching position, preparing for a leap. When attempting to \"withdraw from the skirmish area,\" if the Lower Body section performs this action, all sections of this character are treated as having completed preparations for withdraw.\nIn this case, the Upper Body section does not receive a penalty to the Evasion check, while only the Lower Body section receives a -4 penalty.\nThis effect, as an exception, allows movement to the enemy rear area on the next round's turn in Simplified Combat, even when there are opposing characters present in the frontline area."},{"title":"◯Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 10 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +6 points.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGlossy Fur (400G/Red A) |\n2 - 9 |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) |\n10+ |\nWell-Kept Weapon (1,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Tyrant Strider","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"oTtz9nxMHGm1LjAC","name":"Formica Soldier","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:formica-soldier","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Formica","habitat":"Deserts, Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Barbarous Tales (2.0 sourcebook), p. 40","description":"Formica look like an upright ant with four arms. Covered with a hard outer shell, their bodies are extremely tough. They are not much taller than humans, but with four arms, they can masterfully wield two weapons.\n\nTheir language is difficult to learn, and even if someone can speak it, they can hardly communicate with them. They are pack-driven and follow the orders of their leaders. They have no emotions and feel no fear. Although their intelligence is low, they are able to communicate quickly and empathically with other animals, and they work in groups to hunt down their enemies.\n\nTheir biology is also similar to that of ants, building huge underground nests in deserts and dry areas. They consider all living things other than themselves as food and attack them. They also have an excellent sense of smell to track their prey.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"►Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"A Formica Soldier can make two Weapon attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"►Formic Acid / 7 (14) / Fortitude / Negates","description":"A Formica can spit acid at an enemy character in the same skirmish, dealing 2d+6 Poison magic damage."},{"title":"🗨Sensitive Smell","description":"Any Track check made by a Formica is performed with a standard value of 9 (fixed success value of 16) when tracking prey."},{"title":"◯Shared Senses","description":"If there is another Formica (of any type) in the skirmish this monster is in, it gains a +1 bonus to all of its Accuracy checks. This effect is not cumulative.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBeetle Shell (30G/Red B) |\n2 - 6 |\nSharp Weapon (100G/Black White A) x 2 |\n7 - 10 |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) x 2 |\n11+ |\nExtravagant Weapon (500G/Black White A) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Formica Soldier","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pb7Abd4u19YfpfmE","name":"Arrow Hoodling","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:arrow-hoodling","level":1,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":1,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Various","reputation":6,"weakness":11,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2 points","initiative":9,"movementSpeed":"10","fortitude":"2 (9)","willpower":"3 (10)","source":"CR I p. 395","description":"Hoodlings are a small Youma common on the Alframe continent. They are ugly and have grayish skin. They have large heads, long, slender limbs, and walk with a forward slant.\n\nThey hate their look and hide by wearing hoods. Also, they hate beautiful things and especially enjoy killing Humans and Elves.\n\nArrow Hoodlings are armed with bows and prefer to surround their prey in groups, shooting and killing them all at once.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Bow","description":"Shooting Attack with a bow at \"Range: 2 (20m)\". Accuracy check and damage are the same as a normal attack."},{"title":"◯ Targeting","description":"Stray shots cannot occur.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nCrude Weapon (10G/Black White B) |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8+ |\nDirty Hood (20G/White B) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Arrow Hoodling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pbdtuBtBc9xFmL4p","name":"High Goblin","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:high-goblin","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forest, Mountain, Cave","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"16/-","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"Battle Mastery p. 109","description":"High Goblins were created in the Magic Civilization Period by a Drake wizard-king using a Goblin as a base material. This Youma is often compared to the Humanoid Newmen , who were also created through magical experimentation.\n\nTheir skin is morbidly pale and they have huge red eyes. Although they are rather large for Goblins, their body is thin and bare, and they are relatively powerful aside from Goblin Lords and other even larger types. However, their resistance to magic, which they gain from the anti-magic enchantment crests that appear on their body, and their unwavering aggressiveness due to their lack of fear, make them a great threat to their opponents. They have been deployed in many battles as the ultimate soldiers against other wizard-kings.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Anti-Magic Enchantment","description":"When this monster performs a Willpower check against magic and succeeds, the result is treated as Negated regardless of the type of magic. If the Willpower check fails, the effect of the magic is applied as if it had succeeded and costs 5 MP to the High Goblin.\nThis effect does not occur if no MP was consumed. This ability does apply to effects other than spells, even if they require a Resistance Check."},{"title":"◯ Psychic Resistance","description":"High Goblin is immune to Psychic (Weak) effects.\nHigh Goblin also gains a +4 bonus when it makes a Willpower roll against any Psychic-type spell or unique skill.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 10 |\nHigh quality Weapon (150G/Black White A) |\n11+ |\nEngraved Weapon (600G/Black White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"High Goblin","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"pl0VQ1kgneiyjNaI","name":"High Goblin Fanatic","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:high-goblin-fanatic","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":11,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"16/-","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"13 (20)","source":"BM","description":"This is a higher species of High Goblin and is considered something akin to a knight in Goblin society. They are fearsome mad warriors who wear heavy armor and use massive weapons far beyond their height to ravage their enemies.\n\nThey were created to take pleasure in blind obedience to the High Goblin Maiden , and they are fanatically loyal to her, even to the point of cutting off their own heads with a smile if they are told to die on the spot.\n\nTherefore, the combination of High Goblin Fanatic and High Goblin Maiden is a vicious fighting force, as Fanatics can be strongly enhanced by the High Goblin Maiden.\n\nThey believe in fighting as a shield of the High Goblin Maiden with their life. If they should lose the High Goblin Maiden they are supposed to protect, they will start a desperate fight to the end involving everything and everyone around him.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"🗨 △ Cover I","description":"High Goblin Fanatic can use the [ Cover I ] combat feat (see p. 33)."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike II","description":"A High Goblin Fanatic can deal an additional +12 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by the High Goblin Fanatic this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"High Goblin Fanatic can attack with a weapon up to 5 target characters within the skirmish in which it resides.\nIf declared at the same time as a [Power Strike II], only one of the hit characters will be dealt additional damage."},{"title":"◯ Maiden Fanaticism","description":"It is blindly fanatical to the High Goblin Maiden (see p. 116). The bonus to Accuracy checks received by its [ ► Frenzy Aroma] is increased to +2.\nIf a High Goblin Maiden is killed within a radius of 30 meters, it becomes enraged and gains a +2 bonus on Accuracy checks and +8 to damage for 10 seconds (1 round). If more than one High Goblin Maiden is killed within 10 seconds, this effect is cumulative.\nThis effect is of the Psychic type."},{"title":"◯ Advanced Anti-Magic Enchantment","description":"When this monster performs a Willpower check against magic, if Willpower succeeds, the result is treated as Negated regardless of the type of magic. Furthermore, even if the Willpower check fails, the effect of the magic is still Negated and costs 10 MP to the High Goblin. This effect does not occur if no MP was consumed.\nThis ability does apply to effects other than spells, even if they require a Resistance Check."},{"title":"◯ Psychic Resistance","description":"High Goblin is immune to Psychic (Weak) effects.\nHigh Goblin also gains a +4 bonus when it makes a Willpower roll against any Psychic-type spell or unique skill.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 4 |\nLarge Weapon (300G / Black White A) |\n5 - 10 |\nEngraved Weapon (600G / Black White A) |\n11+ |\nRare Weapon (4000G/ Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"High Goblin Fanatic","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"qMZ31Ka10WQHLWQJ","name":"Dark Troll Adept","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dark-troll-adept","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Giantish","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR II p. 348","description":"This is a Troll priest who is not only a skilled priest but also a capable warrior among the Dark Trolls .\n\nInterestingly, Trolls are sworn to serve the gods rather than to fight themselves. They serve as judges of the divine battles within the Troll clan and preside over rituals. They can also serve as advisors and bless Troll officers, providing spell support to allies when confronted with powerful enemies.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 10 Level /Magic Power 13 (20)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Hawk Eye ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +13 damage","description":"May deal an additional +13 damage to their next melee attack. At risk, they take a -2 penalty to their Fortitude and Willpower checks."},{"title":"◯ Dark Regeneration = 7 points","description":"At the end of each round, a Dark Troll Adept recovers 7 HP. This has no effect if the Dark Troll Adept is at 0 HP or lower or is under sunlight."},{"title":"◯ Weakened","description":"As long as a Dark Troll is under sunlight, it receives a -2 penalty to all Accuracy and Evasion Checks.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nTroll Blood (100G/Red rounds) |\n2 - 8 |\nGem (300G/Gold A) x 1d |\n9+ |\nStrange Holy Symbol (3,300G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dark Troll Adept","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"qwawZarFoHwvNKpu","name":"Ogre","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ogre","level":6,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric, Ogre, Drakish, Arcana","habitat":"Various","reputation":12,"weakness":15,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":14,"movementSpeed":"18","fortitude":"10 (17)","willpower":"9 (16)","source":"CR II p. 337","description":"Much larger than the Lesser Ogre species, Ogres wield significant physical and magical power. Standing close to 3m tall, they can use larger equipment. Ogres act as though they are master tacticians, using Lesser Ogres and other Barbarous as fodder for their evil (and often cowardly) operations to attack Humanoid races. However, their success rate isn't the greatest, and those who fail often tend to be sent on those same suicide missions by other Ogres.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 5 Level / Magic Power 8 (15)","description":""},{"title":"◯ ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"⏩ △ Personification","description":"An Ogre may take on the appearance and mannerisms of a character they have eaten or change back.\nWhen transformed, the Ogre's maximum HP and MP are decreased by 5. Accuracy, Evasion, Fortitude, and Willpower are also reduced by 1 point each. This form can be held up to 18 hours per day.\nThe [ ⏩ △ Personification] can also be ended with Minor Action or during Combat Preparation.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nBag of Silver (100G) x 1d |\n9 - 12 |\nGem (150G/Gold A) x 1d |\n13+ |\nSword Shard (200G) x 3 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ogre","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"rUbrFg3I1xVwlg4U","name":"Arakcruder Predator","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:arakcruder-predator","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Aviary, Barbaric","habitat":"Mountains","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"10/40 (Flying)","fortitude":"13 (20)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"CR III p. 332","description":"It is a very powerful Arakcruder (see p. 77). They justify their violent nature by defining justice as simply being strong. When cornered, they go berserk and begin to rampage without restraint.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"This monster receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Spear Pursuit","description":"A monster's spear can be used as a melee attack against an opponent who has been attacked with a beak.\nAccuracy check and damage are the same as those of the beak. This effect is effective only when the monster is Flying."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"This ability can only be used with [ ◯ Spear Pursuit]. It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Bear Muscle ], [ Gazelle Feet ], [ Recovery (5 pts.) ], and [ Beetleskin ] Techniques."},{"title":"◯ Rage","description":"This effect appears automatically when this monster's current HP becomes less than half its maximum value (rounding up) and disappears automatically when its HP recovers to more than half its maximum value.\nThe monster becomes frenzied and attacks indiscriminately and without regard for the consequences. In all melee attacks, the target is randomly selected from among possible targets, friend or foe. When declaring [ 🗨 Cleave II], select 5 targets at random (or all of them if there are fewer than 5 suitable targets).\nAll melee attacks gain a +2 bonus to Accuracy checks and +4 points to damage. At the same time, the monster receives a -2 penalty on Evasion checks.\nWhile this effect is in effect, this monster cannot use the [Recovery] Technique.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGems (300G/Gold A) |\n2 - 4 |\nBeautiful Feathers (30G/Gold Red B) |\n5 - 11 |\nSeven-colored Feather (200G/Gold Red A) |\n12+ |\nDazzling Feathers (2,000G/Gold Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Arakcruder Predator","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"rfkUvU4umMb282Qu","name":"Minotaur","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:minotaur","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Minotaur","habitat":"Various","reputation":10,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Magic damage +2 points","initiative":12,"movementSpeed":"12","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"CR II p. 339","description":"This gigantic creature has the body of a human and the head of a bull. It has low intelligence and is ferocious, becoming uncontrollable when enraged.\n\nIt is skilled at finding sword labyrinths and sometimes lives inside them like a guardian.\n\nIt prefers to kidnap Humanoid women, frightening and tormenting them for several days before devouring them.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Cleave I","description":"It can attack up to 3 characters within reach with melee attacks, but the damage will be reduced by -3. If more than one is hit, the damage is determined individually."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"⏩ △ Techniques","description":"They may use the [ Bear Muscle ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Cat's Eyes ], [ Gazelle Feet ], and [ Recovery (5 pts.) ] Techniques.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMinotaur's Axe (475G/Black White A) |\n2 - 6 |\nNothing |\n7 - 9 |\nBig Horn (150G/Red A) |\n10+ |\nBeautiful Horn (600G/Red A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Minotaur","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ro9TO3ngwEd39CQT","name":"Onyx Basilisk (Monstrous Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:onyx-basilisk-monstrous-form","level":14,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric,","habitat":"Desert, Ruins","reputation":12,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"12(Many Legs)","fortitude":"17 (24)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"CR III p. 336","description":"This is the Monstrous form of the Onyx Basilisk (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity, ◯ Disease Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Poison Blood/17 (24)/Fortitude/Negates","description":"It is the same as the unique skill of Onyx Basilisk (Human Form) , except for a different target number.\nRight Evil Eye"},{"title":"⏩ Onyx Gaze/16 (23)/Willpower/Negates","description":"It is the same as the unique skill of Onyx Basilisk (Human Form) , except for a different target number.\nLeft Evil Eye"},{"title":"► Stagnation Gaze/15 (22)/Willpower/Negates","description":"It is the same as the unique skill of Onyx Basilisk (Human Form) , except for a different target number.\nHead"},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 12 Level/Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Universal Metamagic ], and [ Wordbreak ].\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Standing Upright","description":"If the HP of the Body is 0 or less, all other sections get a -2 penalty on Evasion checks."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Humanification","description":"It instantly transforms into Human form. Refer to Onyx Basilisk (Human Form) for data on the Human form. If the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it immediately falls unconscious.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after using [ ► Monstrous Form].\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBasilisk Pureblood (1,000G/Red S) |\n2 - 9 |\nOnyx Eye (4,000G/Gold Red S) |\n10 - 12 |\nEye of Stagnation (10,000G/Gold Red SS) |\n13+ |\nEvil Onyx Eye (20,000G/Gold Red SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Onyx Basilisk (Monstrous Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"t1uqkyTE9SaRuaYQ","name":"Fire Giant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:fire-giant","level":16,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Neutral","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Giantish","habitat":"Caves, Volcanoes","reputation":17,"weakness":21,"weakPoint":"Water/Ice damage +3 points","initiative":21,"movementSpeed":"25","fortitude":"23 (30)","willpower":"23 (30)","source":"Barbarous Tales 2.0 p. 60","description":"This is a Giant of about 7m tall which lives near volcanoes. They resemble dwarves in appearance and customs. They worship the Flame Warrior Grendal and forge huge weapons. They have immunity to fire, and their hair and beards shimmer with flames. Their skin is reddish-bronze, and they wear clothes made of asbestos and metal armor.\n\nThey are not hostile to everyone, but will warn anyone who approaches the mine which is their territory, and will show no mercy to those who still try to sneak in.\n\nThey often possess extremely powerful magic swords, either forged by themselves or found on 1,000-year-old corpses. Some of these swords are legendary. Many people challenge Fire Giants for their hoard, but none ever return.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fire Immunity","description":""},{"title":"◯ Continuous Attack","description":"If a Fire Giant successfully hits a target in melee, they may make a second attack against the same target.\nUpper Body"},{"title":"► Divine Magic 13 Level / Magic Power 17 (24)","description":""},{"title":"🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"Can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"► War Cry / 20 (27) / Willpower / Negates","description":"The Fire Giant unleashes a powerful yell, causing fear in those who fail to resist within a 10-meter radius around Fire Giant. This fear, treated as a Psychic effect, gives a -2 penalty to all Action Checks for the next 30 seconds (3 rounds).\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = Impossible • +4","description":"The Upper Body cannot be attacked in melee. Against any ranged attacks, Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks.\nWhen the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nFlame Crystal (1,600G/Gold S) x 4 |\n2 - 7 |\nGiant Helmet (9,000G/Black White S) |\n8+ |\nGiant's Treasure (10,000G/Gold SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Fire Giant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"t70PqsgISbXsOXZy","name":"Centaur Heavy Knight","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:centaur-heavy-knight","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Centaur","habitat":"Plains","reputation":13,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Earth Damage +3","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"40 (4 Legs)/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"10 (17)","source":"BM","description":"It is a heavily armed Centaur that specializes in physical attacks and does not use Fairy Magic. It is the first one to enter the battlefield and is responsible for breaking the enemy's defense line into pieces.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Charge / 10 (17) / Evasion / Negates","description":"This attack can only be used after Normal Move.\nCentaur Heavy Knight charges, spearing an enemy character with a melee attack, dealing 2d+20 physical damage."},{"title":"◯ Rampage","description":"After [ ► Charge], Centaur Heavy Knight can make additional Major Action.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nHeraldic Spear (150G / Black White A) |\n8 - 10 |\nWell-Balanced Spear (600G / Black White A) |\n11+ |\nWell-Kept Spear (1000G / Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Centaur Heavy Knight","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tB9LT9JJ08A6aZXE","name":"Gilman","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gilman","level":5,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Gilman","habitat":"Coasts, River Deltas","reputation":13,"weakness":16,"weakPoint":"Fire Damage +3","initiative":13,"movementSpeed":"18/18 (swimming)","fortitude":"7 (14)","willpower":"7 (14)","source":"Barbarous Tales (2.0 sourcebook), p. 37","description":"Gilmen are Humanoid in shape, with fish-like faces and covered in fine scales from head to toe. Able to breathe and move in water without penalty, Gilmen tend to live close to, if not in, the water. Caves and estuaries near rivers are common Gilman settlements, but there are also underwater civilizations as well.\n\nGilmen tend to share few to no values with Humanoid races and are fairly emotionless. In combat, a Gilman will fight to win, and will protect allies even if it becomes disadvantageous to do so. They are also rather stoic and will not panic, even if abandoned by their allies.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"► Feint Attack","description":"The Gilman receives a +1 Accuracy bonus to the next attack. Characters wearing metal armor are unaffected.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 3 |\nNothing |\n4 - 8 |\nMysterious Shells (130G/Gold Red A) |\n9+ |\nGems (150G/Gold A) x 1d |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gilman","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"tCZeAG8zhyOoL4Oe","name":"Diablo Lieutenant (Daemon Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:diablo-lieutenant-daemon-form","level":11,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Daemonic","habitat":"Wilderness, Shallow","reputation":19,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3","initiative":19,"movementSpeed":"20/20 (Flying)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"14 (21)","source":"CR II p. 351","description":"This is the Daemon form of the Diablo Lieutenant (Human Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Tough Skin","description":"Whenever it receives physical or magical damage of the Bludgeoning type, the damage is reduced by 3 points.\nHead"},{"title":"◯ Limited 2 Actions","description":"The monster can perform two Major Actions in one round. However, the monster must choose two different actions from the melee attack, [ ► Daemonic Eyes II] or [ ► Spray of Evil]."},{"title":"► Daemonic Eyes II/Can't","description":"With a sharp look in its eyes, it makes its enemies shrivel.\nWith \"Range/Area: 1 (10m)/Target\", select any number of targets and deal each of them 3 curse fixed damage.\nAfterward, Diablo's HP is restored by the sum of all applied damage dealt to the targets.\nUsing this ability consumes 3 points of MP per character targeted."},{"title":"► Evil Spray/14 (21)/Willpower/Half","description":"With \"Range: Self\" and \"Target: 2-3 areas (10m Radius)\", it releases a cursed spray and deals 2d+11 curse magic damage to the target.\nThis effect can exclude any character from the target except itself. It never removes itself, but the resistance is always treated as a success.\nBody"},{"title":"◯ Flight","description":"Receives a +1 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks.\nIf the Body section falls to 0 HP or lower, this unique skill cannot be used."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides."},{"title":"► Humanification","description":"It changes to the Human form. For data on the Human form, refer to Diablo Lieutenant (Human Form) . If the Body section has suffered HP or MP damage or has been affected by magic or other effects, these are carried over to the Human form. If its HP is less than 0, it immediately falls unconscious.\n[ ► Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after [ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] was used. Also, [ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] cannot be used for 3 hours immediately after the [ ► Humanification] was used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G) x 2 |\n2 - 7 |\nBlack Gem (300G/Gold A) x 1d |\n8 - 12 |\nJet-Black Gem (2,200G/Gold S) x 2 |\n13+ |\nTrue Dark Gem (4,900G/Gold S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Diablo Lieutenant (Daemon Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uFE5qZ6FPE1Ka4io","name":"Goblin High King","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:goblin-high-king","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":12,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Magic Damage +2","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"14/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"BM","description":"A Goblin High King is so powerful that it is called the \"Only King\" among Goblins . Its height is over 2 meters, and its presence is enough to intimidate even the most powerful Barbarous.\n\nIn battle, he sacrifices many of his men while assessing the capabilities of his opponents and exploiting gaps in their defenses to launch a wave of attacks.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Wait Action","description":"If this monster loses initiative at the start of combat, it can perform two Major Actions in the first round."},{"title":"◯ High King","description":"All \"Target: 1 Entire Character\" within \"Range/Area: 2 (50m) / Target \" around the Goblin High King are inspired by his presence and gain a +1 bonus to Accuracy checks, increasing their damage by +2 points for 10 seconds (1 round). However, while under this effect, they cannot restore HP and MP. If the affected allies are Barbarous of Level 7 or lower, this effect is considered to be \"Resistance: Can't\", otherwise it is \"Resistance: Optional\". It is treated as a Psychic effect with a Success Value of 20.\nAlthough it can be used as many times as the High King wants during its turn, its effects do not stack on a target."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike I","description":"They can deal an additional 4 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"► King's Authority / 10 (17) / Willpower / Negates","description":"The Goblin High King makes its presence known to \"Target: All Areas (20m Radius) / All\". They will be unable to target with melee attacks, ranged attacks, magic, or other effects that harm the Goblin High King for 10 seconds (1 round).\nUsing this effect consumes 5 points of MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nGlittering Necklace (2,000G/Gold White S) |\n2 - 5 |\nBag of Silver (50G) x 1d |\n6 - 10 |\nGem (150G/Gold A) x 1d |\n11+ |\nGoblin Crown (700G/Gold White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Goblin High King","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"uLm0vTuKO5mRav57","name":"Hecatoncheires","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:hecatoncheires","level":15,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Giantish","habitat":"Various","reputation":16,"weakness":22,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"21 (28)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"CR III p. 338","description":"This is a 12-armed Giant of about 6 meters in height. When fighting, they carry weapons on 6 arms and shields on the other 6. They value bravery and respect those who come at them fairly and squarely, but they are angry at those who act cowardly. Because of this, they are often entrusted with guarding important places such as the treasury and are not often seen outside.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Swords Dance/Can't","description":"The Hecatoncheires does a strange, flailing dance that deals (2d x (Remaining Arms) + 5) Physical damage to one target in the same skirmish.\nThis ability cannot be used when even one Arm has completed its Major Action. Also, after this ability is used, Major Actions of all Arms are completed."},{"title":"◯ Limited Attacks","description":"Due to the size of the Hecatoncheires, only two Arms can attack the same target in 10 seconds (1 round)."},{"title":"🗨 Power Strike II","description":"They can deal an additional +12 damage on their next attack. However, any Evasion Check made by them this turn receives a -2 penalty."},{"title":"◯ Layered Protection","description":"The Defense of Upper Body section is increased by +2 points for each remaining Arm section.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Hecatoncheires' height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. This effect disappears when the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nMassive Weapon (300G/Black White A) x 6 |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nLump of Silver (3,600G/Gold S) |\n13+ |\nLump of Gold (18,000G/Gold SS) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Hecatoncheires","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"vGeDR4Jvn4gDACe2","name":"Dawn Ripper","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:dawn-ripper","level":7,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric","habitat":"Ruins","reputation":14,"weakness":17,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"8 (15)","willpower":"8 (15)","source":"KF","description":"This is a Dawn species that has developed its skills and abilities through its work. Many Humanoids mistake these monsters for Humanoid assassins or vampires, and there have been confirmed cases where such rumors were true.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"► Divine Magic 7 Level/Magic Power 9 (16)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +9 damage","description":"A Dawn Ripper can deal an additional 9 damage on their next attack. However, any Fortitude or Willpower Check made by the Dawn Ripper this turn receives a -1 penalty.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nBarbarous Orders (500G/White A) |\n2 - 7 |\nNight Robe (280G/White A) |\n8+ |\nRobe of Darkness (780G/White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Dawn Ripper","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"ven0r4GBEwvKmqNs","name":"Ogre Warlord","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:ogre-warlord","level":13,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Trade Common, Barbaric,","habitat":"Various","reputation":16,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Physical damage +2 points","initiative":20,"movementSpeed":"20","fortitude":"18 (25)","willpower":"18 (25)","source":"CR III p. 334","description":"Although they lack the shapeshift ability, Ogre Warlords are a superior species of Ogres , possessing physical and magical powers far superior to those of ordinary Ogres. Though not much different in appearance from an ordinary Ogre, they are sometimes adorned with crowns and necklaces and carry specially forged swords that prove their kingship.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 2 times","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic 10 Level/Magic Power 14 (21)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 ► Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Multi-Action ], [ Targeting ], [ Magic Convergence ], [ Magic Control ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Wordbreak ]."},{"title":"🗨 Mana Strike = +14 damage","description":"An Ogre Warlord may deal an additional +14 damage to their next melee attack. If they do, at risk, they receive a -2 penalty to Fortitude and Willpower checks until their next turn.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nBag of Gold (1,400G) |\n9 - 12 |\nLuxury Ornaments (500G/Gold White A) x 2d |\n13+ |\nRoyal Treasured Sword (8,000G/Gold Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ogre Warlord","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"vensKsydtnpyOJTu","name":"Manodanryu","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:manodanryu","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma, Sea Animal","habitat":"Forest, Ruins","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":16,"movementSpeed":"14/-","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"A superior species of Manogaryu who are reputed to have subdued Mythical Beasts and large animals. Manodanryu customarily incorporate the name of the animal or Mythical Beast they have tamed into their own name, which can be used to guess at how strong an individual is.\n\nIt is said one legendary Manodanryu is said to have tamed a dragon, but it has not been confirmed whether this was a true story or a boast.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Twin Strike &amp; Double Attack","description":"Can make two Whip attacks each round, though each attack requires its own Accuracy check. They may choose to attack different characters with each attack."},{"title":"◯ Multiple Declarations = 3 times","description":""},{"title":"◯ Subjugation II","description":"Adds +2 bonus to Accuracy/Evasion versus Animals and Mythical Beasts."},{"title":"🗨 Whip Feint","description":"Deliberately leaves an opening in its attack to bait the opponent into evading. This has the same effect as [ Decoy Attack I ]."},{"title":"🗨 Vital Aim","description":"Aims the whip for a weak point and attacks. If the Accuracy Check roll result is 9 or greater, +5 damage is added to the attack's damage roll. As a risk, the Manodanryu receives a -2 penalty to its attack."},{"title":"🗨 All-Out Offense","description":"Puts all of their strength behind the whip and launches a vicious blow. This adds +8 damage to the attack's damage roll, but as a Risk, the Manodanryu suffers a -2 penalty to its Evasion.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 9 |\nBeast Tamer's Whip (660G / Red A) |\n10+ |\nWhip of Subjugation (1680G / Red S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Manodanryu","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"vq9wpm1tQUkelMGy","name":"High Goblin Raider","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:high-goblin-raider","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five Senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Youma","habitat":"Forests, Mountains, Caves","reputation":12,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Physical Damage +2","initiative":18,"movementSpeed":"20/-","fortitude":"11 (18)","willpower":"12 (19)","source":"BM","description":"These are High Goblins trained specifically for surprise attacks.\n\nThey are feared for appearing seemingly from nowhere to wreak havoc on the battlefield.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Fast Action","description":"If High Goblin Raider wins the initiative during the first round of combat, it may take two Major Actions that round."},{"title":"◯ Shadow Sneak","description":"Can leave or pass through skirmishes without movement blocking or requiring the Prepare to Withdraw action."},{"title":"◯ Painful Strike","description":"If the 2d roll of the damage roll is 9 or more, the damage is increased by an additional +8 points."},{"title":"◯ Anti-Magic Enchantment","description":"When this monster performs a Willpower check against magic and succeeds, the result is treated as Negated regardless of the type of magic. Furthermore, even if the Willpower check fails, the effect of the magic is applied as if it had succeeded and cost 5 MP to the High Goblin.\nThis effect does not occur if no MP is consumed. This ability does apply to effects other than spells, even if they require a Resistance Check."},{"title":"◯ Psychic Resistance","description":"High Goblin is immune to Psychic (Weak) effects.\nHigh Goblin also gains a +4 bonus when it makes a Willpower roll against any Psychic type spell or unique skill.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 5 |\nHigh-quality Weapon (150G / Black White A) |\n6 - 11 |\nEngraved Weapon (600G / Black White A) |\n12+ |\nRare Weapon (4000G / Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"High Goblin Raider","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"x0k4CpRBbwp8jt1f","name":"Diablo Captain (Human Form)","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:diablo-captain-human-form","level":15,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"High","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Drakish, Daemonic","habitat":"Wilderness, Shallows","reputation":23,"weakness":26,"weakPoint":"Energy damage +3 points","initiative":24,"movementSpeed":"25/25(Flying)","fortitude":"19 (26)","willpower":"19 (26)","source":"CR III p. 339","description":"This is a Diablo who has led an army through age and many combat experiences.\n\nThey are a skilled commander of Barbarous and Daemons and is a master of drawing out their strengths, sometimes leading the troops, but they are also devoted to the training of young Diablos. They have a broad perspective on the expansion of Barbarous as a whole. Therefore, they are not only at odds with Humanoids but also often engage in strategic bargaining and political dealings.\n\nWhen transformed into the daemon form, they expose their true ferociousness and destroy their enemies with their fighting instincts.\n\nFor the Daemon form of this monster, see Diablo Captain (Daemon Form) .","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Tough Skin","description":"Whenever it receives physical or magical damage of the bludgeoning type, it is reduced by -3 points."},{"title":"◯ Flight II","description":"Receives a +2 bonus to Accuracy and Evasion only for melee attacks."},{"title":"◯ Limited 2 Actions","description":"The monster can perform two Major Actions in one round. However, this is limited to one weapon melee attack and one [ ► Daemonic Eyes III] once each.\nIt cannot use [ 🗨 Cleave II] for that melee attack."},{"title":"🗨 Cleave II","description":"It attacks with a weapon up to 5 characters within the skirmish in which it resides."},{"title":"► Daemonic Eyes III/Can't","description":"With a sharp look in its eyes, it makes enemies shrivel.\nWith \"Range/Area: 2 (30m) / Target \", select any number of targets and deal 10 curse fixed damage each. Afterward, Diablo's HP is restored by the sum of all applied damage dealt to the targets.\nUsing this ability consumes 4 points of MP per character targeted."},{"title":"◯ Barbarous and Daemons Strengthening","description":"All Barbarous and Daemon monsters except for the Diablo Captain within \"Range: Self\" and \"Target: All Areas (30m Radius) / All\" receive a +2 bonus on all action checks except Evasion checks, and the physical and magic damage they cause is increased by +2 points."},{"title":"⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift","description":"The character changes into the daemon form with Minor Actions or during Combat Preparation. For the data, see Diablo Captain (Daemon Form) . HP and MP are restored to their maximum values, and all effects of magic, etc., are negated. In the turn in which this unique skill is performed, only the Head section of the Daemon Form is treated as having completed the Major Action, and the Right Side and Left Side sections can make it this turn.\n[ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] cannot be used for 3 hours immediately after the [ ► Humanification] was used. Also, [ ► Humanification] cannot be used for 1 hour immediately after [ ⏩ △ Instant Daemonshift] was used.\n2d |\nLoot |\nAlways |\nAbyss Shard (200G) x 5 |\n2 - 5 |\nJet-Black Gem (2,200G/Gold S) x 2 |\n6 - 12 |\nTrue Dark Gem (4,900G/Gold S) x 2 |\n13+ |\nAbyssal Treasure (15,500G/Gold SS) x 2 |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Diablo Captain (Human Form)","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xPFyFASmliB3rqMX","name":"Quepala'ula'ula","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:quepalaulaula","level":8,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":3,"languages":"Barbaric, Arcana, Drakish","habitat":"Forests, Caves, Swamps, Shallows","reputation":15,"weakness":18,"weakPoint":"Fire damage + 3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"15","fortitude":"9 (16)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"CR III p. 331","description":"This is a Quepala'ula who is particularly knowledgeable and excels in magical knowledge. They are sometimes the leaders of settlements in the larger Shallow Abysses. They are gruesome and brutal and have a strong hatred for Humanoids and the beings who are in their service.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"► Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic 8 Level/Magic Power 10 (17)","description":""},{"title":"◯ 🗨 Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"◯ Poison/10 (17)/Fortitude/Neg","description":"If their Bite attack hits, the target is dealt additional 8 poison magic damage.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nArcana-Language Book (170G/White A) |\n7 - 10 |\nSpellbook (500G/White A) |\n11+ |\nEsoteric Spellbook (1,500G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Quepala'ula'ula","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xVM5Hb6ACmYhzlbK","name":"Quepa","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:quepa","level":3,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":2,"languages":"Barbaric, Arcana, Daemonic","habitat":"Forests, Caves, Swamps, Shallows","reputation":10,"weakness":13,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":10,"movementSpeed":"14","fortitude":"4 (11)","willpower":"6 (13)","source":"AB, p. 89","description":"This is a juvenile specimen of the Quepala'ula species with a snake head. While retaining its snake head, from the neck down it has a form similar to a human child.\n\nStrangely, they are rarely seen in Quepala'ula settlements, with most sightings concentrated in the Shallow Abysses where the Barbarous gather.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Poison Immunity","description":""},{"title":"►Magic (1 system) 2 Level / Magic Power 4 (11)","description":"Most of them have mastered one of the following magic systems: Truespeech Magic , Spiritualism Magic , or Abyssal Magic (enhanced effects are only used for one round)."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use the Combat Feats [ Targeting ] and [ Metamagic/Targets ].\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 8 |\nNothing |\n9+ |\nArcana-Language Book (170G/White A) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Quepa","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"xheKNsDJy7SKAPSY","name":"Lake Giant","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:lake-giant","level":10,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Low","perception":"Five senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Giantish","habitat":"Lakesides","reputation":16,"weakness":19,"weakPoint":"Fire damage +3 points","initiative":15,"movementSpeed":"18/18 (Swimming)","fortitude":"14 (21)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Natural History of Dorden , p. 121","description":"Although it shares some similarities with the Forest Giant in terms of body size and ecology, this Giant is recognized as a subspecies due to differences in details.\n\nIt has a strong territorial instinct and rarely strays from the area around the lakeside it has claimed as its territory. It attempts to prey on any living creature that approaches within its territory.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯Underwater Aptitude","description":"There are no restrictions or penalties for actions in water."},{"title":"◯Water/Ice Immunity","description":"Upper Body"},{"title":"►War Cry / 12 (19) / Willpower / Negates","description":"The Lake Giant unleashes a mighty yell, causing fear in those who fail to resist within a 10-meter radius around the Lake Giant. This fear, treated as a Psychic-type effect, gives a -2 penalty to all Skill Checks for the next 30 seconds (3 rounds).\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯Limited Attack Obstacle = +4•None","description":"The Lake Giant's height prevents enemies from attacking it. The Upper Body section receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks.\nThis effect disappears when the Lower Body section falls to 0 HP or lower. Also, this ability is temporarily disabled whenever the Lower Body section is in water."},{"title":"◯Kick from Underwater","description":"Whenever its Lower Body is in water, it gets a +2 bonus to Accuracy checks for Kick attacks."},{"title":"►Water Splash / 12 (19) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Kicks up the water around itself. Targets within \"Range: Caster\" and \"1 area (6m radius)/All\" take 2d+7 points of Water/Ice-type magic damage and are knocked prone. This ability can only be used when the Lower Body section is submerged in water.\nThis ability cannot be used in consecutive turns.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 7 |\nNothing |\n8 - 12 |\nGold Ring (2,500G / Gold White S) |\n13+ |\nGiant Helmet (9,000G/Black White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Lake Giant","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"yBoFj8oG2tyfK2Bp","name":"Gian Fomor","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:gian-fomor","level":14,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five Senses","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Giant","habitat":"Various","reputation":19,"weakness":23,"weakPoint":"Accuracy +1","initiative":25,"movementSpeed":"24/-","fortitude":"20 (27)","willpower":"17 (24)","source":"BM","description":"Gian Fomors are incredibly powerful Fomor Giant generals who once led entire legions of Barbarous. At present, however, no Gian Fomors are in command, as the higher-level Drakes are very wary of rebellion and are keeping them subdued.\n\nUsually, Gian Fomors are given nominal assignments and relegated to the far reaches and frontiers of the Barbarous territories. Their subordinates, too, are merely watchdogs, whose movements are constantly reported to the higher Drakes. Gian Fomors, however, have not lost their former vigor. They spend their long years in hiding, believing that one day Fomor's legions will sweep the earth.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Chain Attack","description":"After an attack, Gian Fomor can attack the same target again, regardless of its success or failure. This ability can add only one additional attack per round."},{"title":"◯ Counter","description":"Identical effect as the Combat Feat [ Counter ].\nUpper Body"},{"title":"⏩ △ Technique &amp; ◯ Muscle Mystery","description":"Can use [ Cat's Eye ], [ Beetleskin ], [ Bear Muscle ], [ Giant Arms ], [ Titan's Foot ], [ Troll Vitals ], and [ Recovery (14 points) ]. These Techniques have twice the normal duration."},{"title":"⏩ Stratagem and Maneuver/All Areas (50m Radius)","description":"Can use [ Surging Offense IV: Radiant Strikes ] (Accuracy +1, Physical Damage +1).\nEvery third turn, they can use [ Maneuver: Unexpected Blow II ] (+4 Accuracy, +4 Damage). They cannot use Stratagems if no other allies will be affected by them.\nLower Body"},{"title":"◯ Attack Obstacle = +4 • None","description":"Fomor height prevents enemies from attacking it.\nThe Upper Body receives a +4 bonus to Evasion checks against melee attacks. When the Lower Body falls to 0 HP or lower, this effect disappears.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nBag of Silver (100G / - ) x 2d |\n7 - 11 |\nBag of Silver (300G / -) x 2d |\n12+ |\nGeneral's Insignia (7,300G/Gold White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Gian Fomor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
{"_id":"zaAzyFn0FMH3EJd6","name":"Deep Sahagin Priest","type":"monster","system":{"revealed":false,"sourceUrl":"https://sw25.wikidot.com/monster:deep-sahagin-priest","level":9,"monsterType":"Barbarous","intelligence":"Average","perception":"Five senses (Darkvision)","disposition":"Hostile","soulscars":4,"languages":"Barbaric, Gilman","habitat":"Oceans, Deep Seas","reputation":17,"weakness":20,"weakPoint":"Earth damage +3 points","initiative":17,"movementSpeed":"15/20 (Swimming)","fortitude":"12 (19)","willpower":"11 (18)","source":"Ancient Blue (SW2.5 supplement), p. 134","description":"They are the central priests of the Deep Sahagins . While holding a position close to that of a guide and chieftain, their abilities as a priest warrior are quite formidable.","combatStyles":[],"uniqueSkills":[{"title":"◯ Underwater Aptitude","description":""},{"title":"◯Water/Ice Absorption","description":"When receiving physical or magical damage of Water/Ice type, HP and MP will not decrease from the damage, and they will not receive any adverse effects from water/ice properties. Additionally, HP is restored by the same amount as the damage that would have been applied."},{"title":"◯🗨Magic Aptitude","description":"They can use Combat Feats [ Targeting ], [ Metamagic/Targets ], and [ Multi-Action ]."},{"title":"🗨Mana Strike = +11 Damage","description":"Increases damage by +11 points. As a risk, they take a -2 penalty to their own Fortitude and Willpower checks until their next turn."},{"title":"► Divine Magic 8 Level / Magic Power 11 (18)","description":""},{"title":"⏩Quick Water Spit / 10 (17) / Fortitude / Half","description":"Deals 2d+9 points of Water/Ice magic damage to target 1 character within \"Range/Area: 1 (10m) / Shot \".\nThis ability can only be used once per round and cannot be used underwater. Additionally, using it consumes 10 MP.\n2d |\nLoot |\n2 - 6 |\nOrnate Trident (120G/Black White A) |\n7 - 12 |\nWell-Maintained Trident (1,000G/Black White S) |\n13+ |\nStrange Holy Symbol (3,300G/White S) |"}],"lootTable":[]},"img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","prototypeToken":{"name":"Deep Sahagin Priest","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"width":1,"height":1,"depth":1,"texture":{"src":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":"mp"},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":false,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":null}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"flags":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false},"items":[],"effects":[],"sort":0}
